":"50calDhruv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjI3OTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/187989371990b0e478026d6d38845a7eb367fc21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:06:33Z","email":"dhruvmuthria@gmail.com","name":"50calDhruv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:06:33Z","email":"dhruvmuthria@gmail.com","name":"50calDhruv"},"message":"Note the build --watch footgun in the README\n\nSpent a while convinced federation was broken in dev mode. It wasn''t —\nvite build --watch empties dist at the start of each rebuild, and I was\nkilling the process group mid-build, so the remotes were serving empty\ndirectories. The shell dutifully showed its error boundary for remotes\nthat were fine.\n\nVerified pnpm dev properly afterwards: shell in dev mode against the three\nbuilt remotes renders the catalog, add-to-cart moves the badge, and the\ndynamically registered account remote loads, with no console errors.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"bacb598c3875a76c91f4f397c0d7791e6b7194a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/git/trees/bacb598c3875a76c91f4f397c0d7791e6b7194a0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/git/commits/187989371990b0e478026d6d38845a7eb367fc21","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80627988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv","id":80627988,"login":"50calDhruv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjI3OTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv/shopFront/commit/187989371990b0e478026d6d38845a7eb367fc21","node_id":"C_kwDOUaYhVNoAKDE4Nzk4OTM3MTk5MGIwZTQ3ODAyNmQ2ZDM4ODQ1YTdlYjM2N2ZjMjE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv/shopFront/commit/85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd","sha":"85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd"}],"sha":"187989371990b0e478026d6d38845a7eb367fc21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/187989371990b0e478026d6d38845a7eb367fc21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80627988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv","id":80627988,"login":"50calDhruv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjI3OTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:43:27Z","email":"dhruvmuthria@gmail.com","name":"50calDhruv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T19:43:27Z","email":"dhruvmuthria@gmail.com","name":"50calDhruv"},"message":"Wire up the three remotes, the event bus, and failure isolation\n\nThis is the rest of it: catalog, cart and account are now real Module\nFederation remotes, the shell consumes them, and everything in the brief\nis verifiable in a browser.\n\nHow it fits together:\n\n- catalog and cart are declared in the shell''s vite config, so their URLs\n  are baked into the host bundle. account deliberately is not — the shell\n  reads /remotes.json at runtime and calls registerRemotes(). Moving that\n  one needs no host rebuild.\n- Remotes render relative <Routes> and never their own <BrowserRouter>.\n  The shell matches /catalog/*, hands over the rest of the path, and stops\n  caring.\n- Every remote mounts through <RemoteBoundary>: lazy import, Suspense, its\n  own error boundary, and a retry that builds a fresh lazy component\n  (React.lazy caches rejected promises, so reusing it replays the failure\n  forever). Toggle remotes off in the footer toolbar or with ?down=.\n- The bus now splits into commands (cart:add, cart:setQty) and facts\n  (cart:updated, auth:changed). Only the shell turns one into the other,\n  so there''s exactly one writer for cart state. Facts are replayed to late\n  subscribers, otherwise the lazy-loaded cart renders empty until the user\n  happens to change something.\n\nTwo things bit me, both now written up:\n\nThe subpath trap. Sharing ''@shop/ui'' does not share ''@shop/ui/events'' —\nModule Federation keys shares by import specifier, not by package. The\nbuild succeeded, React was genuinely shared, the config looked right, and\nthe app died with \"no EventBusProvider\" because the shell and the remotes\neach had their own copy of the context object. Every subpath crossing the\nboundary needs its own entry.\n\nProduct cards were different widths. The <li> was a flex row, so each card\nsized to its content instead of filling the grid cell, which made the\naspect-ratio images resolve to different heights and knocked every title\nout of alignment. Found it by measuring in the browser, not by looking.\n\nMeasured what shared singletons actually save (pnpm analyze drives a real\nbrowser over six routes and gzips what it fetched): 360.7 kB vs 462.9 kB,\nso 102.2 kB / 22%. Worth knowing that sharing costs the host ~19 kB and\n~23 extra requests before it saves anything — it breaks even at about one\nremote. Also measured: statically declared remotes get their container\nfetched eagerly (cart pulled 5 files while sitting on /catalog), while the\ndynamic one pulled nothing.\n\npnpm verify is green and pnpm verify:federation passes 19/19.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"25eff455931d4038144443a494a7bd360bbce991","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/git/trees/25eff455931d4038144443a494a7bd360bbce991"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/git/commits/85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80627988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv","id":80627988,"login":"50calDhruv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjI3OTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv/shopFront/commit/85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd","node_id":"C_kwDOUaYhVNoAKDg1YzNhZDljNDFiMTZmYTQ2YTQ1Y2RhOGNkMGRhOWIwNDZkYjI2YmQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv/shopFront/commit/c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337","sha":"c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337"}],"sha":"85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/85c3ad9c41b16fa46a45cda8cd0da9b046db26bd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80627988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv","id":80627988,"login":"50calDhruv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjI3OTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:53:29Z","email":"dhruvmuthria@gmail.com","name":"50calDhruv"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T18:59:11Z","email":"dhruvmuthria@gmail.com","name":"50calDhruv"},"message":"Set up the workspace and get the shell running\n\nFirst slice of the micro-frontend storefront. No Module Federation yet —\nI wanted routing, layout and the providers solid on their own first, so\nthat when federation breaks later I know it isn''t this layer.\n\nWhat''s here:\n\n- packages/ui — Button, Input, Card, and the Tailwind v4 design tokens.\n  Tokens ship as CSS rather than a JS preset because v4 dropped presets.\n- packages/ui/events — the typed event bus remotes will use to talk to the\n  shell. It lives in the shared package instead of the shell so remotes\n  never import from the host.\n- packages/mocks — MSW handlers. Its own package because service workers\n  are origin-scoped: the shell covers every remote once federated, but a\n  remote running standalone still needs the same handlers.\n- apps/shell — nav, routing table, auth and cart state. The remote routes\n  render placeholders for now.\n\nCart state sits in the shell rather than the future cart remote. That way\nthe count badge is correct before that remote ever loads, and stays\ncorrect if it''s down.\n\nOne fix worth noting: MSW was ending up in the main chunk, because\n@shop/mocks exported the handlers statically and imported them\ndynamically, so Rollup stopped splitting them. Entry is 73.6 kB gzip now.\n\nAuth is a localStorage flag and MSW runs in production builds. Both are\ndemo shortcuts and say so in the code.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c42acc074bb332c243ed1dae0729d3823ff7e686","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/git/trees/c42acc074bb332c243ed1dae0729d3823ff7e686"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/git/commits/c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/80627988?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv","id":80627988,"login":"50calDhruv","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgwNjI3OTg4","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/50calDhruv","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/50calDhruv/shopFront/commit/c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337","node_id":"C_kwDOUaYhVNoAKGMwZjE1Nzk2YzNjZDc2ZTJhZGQyZTlmMzQzMGU3MjcwZWUzOGUzMzc","parents":[],"sha":"c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits/c0f15796c3cd76e2add2e9f3430e7270ee38e337"}],"requestUrl":"https://api.github.com/repos/50calDhruv/shopFront/commits?per_page=100&page=1&sha=187989371990b0e478026d6d38845a7eb367fc21&since=2025-03-31T23%3A59%3A59.000Z&until=2026-10-08T16%3A02%3A26.647Z"}');
