ervedAt":"2026-10-09T00:40:11.908Z","repositoryId":1369866628,"sha":"d32a3737e4461e82e84ad18aac7a58cfb4aa9cb3"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:40:11.908Z","raw":[{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a28fe7ab7900b2ca5cd27d4e39f95f22a8d47a1d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:11:45Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T14:11:45Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Target the Pimcore 2026.3 platform line\n\nPin pimcore/pimcore and both Studio bundles to ~2026.3.0 and rebuild the frontend\nagainst @pimcore/studio-ui-bundle 2026.3.0, since the shipped module federation build\nbelongs to exactly one SDK line. No source changes were needed: none of the APIs this\nbundle uses changed in 2026.3.\n\nFixes for the 2026.2 line continue on the 2026.2 branch.","tree":{"sha":"091a20c47e7cfcc8d54f4b57ece6085245d6b98b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/091a20c47e7cfcc8d54f4b57ece6085245d6b98b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/a28fe7ab7900b2ca5cd27d4e39f95f22a8d47a1d","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/a28fe7ab7900b2ca5cd27d4e39f95f22a8d47a1d","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKGEyOGZlN2FiNzkwMGIyY2E1Y2QyN2Q0ZTM5Zjk1ZjIyYThkNDdhMWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c","sha":"d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c"}],"sha":"a28fe7ab7900b2ca5cd27d4e39f95f22a8d47a1d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a28fe7ab7900b2ca5cd27d4e39f95f22a8d47a1d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:25:58Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T13:25:58Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Follow symlinks and make the nav entry a perspective permission\n\nTwo things a deployed installation runs into.\n\nA release directory is mostly symlinks - a shared var/, config/ or storage/\npointed into every release - and those were the one part of the project the\nviewer refused to open: the jail compared the realpath() against the root, so\nevery link out of the release was \"outside of the file viewer root\".\n\nThe jail is now logical. normaliseRelative() already resolves \".\" and \"..\" and\nrefuses a path that walks above the root, so no spelling of a path can leave it;\na link the project itself placed in the tree is followed, and resolve() hands\nback the path as it was addressed rather than its target, which keeps\ntoRelative() - and every path the UI shows and sends back - inside the root.\nfollow_symlinks: false restores the physical check for installations that want\nit. A linked file is now written through to its target instead of being replaced\nby a regular file, and a dangling link is listed as unreadable rather than\nwarning its way through every stat.\n\nThe navigation entry carried no permission at all. It could not be switched off\nper perspective, because the perspective editor only renders permissions the\nbackend registered, and for anyone below admin it was a menu entry that led\nnowhere but a 403. It now declares system.scopFileViewer, registered by\nStudioContextPermissionsSubscriber and labelled in both catalogues - Studio\nassembles that translation key itself, so without it the checkbox would show the\nraw key. TranslationsTest asserts the three stay in sync.","tree":{"sha":"be57220f62788a618a491aa20438accfefa8d16c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/be57220f62788a618a491aa20438accfefa8d16c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKGQ3ODczNDRiOWE1NTU4OTllM2FiNzliMWNjNDE2ZDgyMGZmZDUzM2M","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1","sha":"a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1"}],"sha":"d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/d787344b9a555899e3ab79b1cc416d820ffd533c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:25:46Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T11:25:46Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Number releases after the Pimcore platform line they target\n\nThe frontend ships as a prebuilt module federation bundle compiled against a pinned\n@pimcore/studio-ui-bundle, so a release belongs to exactly one platform line - but\nnothing said so. \"v1.4.0\" carries no compatibility information, and the requires were\nloose enough to let composer install this against a Studio SDK the shipped build was\nnever compiled against: with a calendar major, \"^2026.2\" means \"<2027.0.0\", so 2026.3\nand 2026.4 were in range.\n\nPin both platform requires to \"~2026.2.0\" (>=2026.2.0 <2026.3.0) and number releases the\nway the Pimcore packages themselves are numbered, starting at 2026.2.0. The third segment\nstays this bundle''s own counter; it is not Pimcore''s patch level, which the README now\nsays outright because the numbers invite exactly that reading.\n\nConsumers have to change their constraint once: \"^1.0\" does not match a calendar release,\nand composer keeps such a project on 1.4.0 without saying anything.","tree":{"sha":"b6b966fd98e4ad92a70b05b42bdc4cd9222fb11f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/b6b966fd98e4ad92a70b05b42bdc4cd9222fb11f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKGE3OGRiZjI3YjJkNGQ3MDRlMWYzMDJlMzM4OTIwYWViMjE2NzM1ZTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28","sha":"8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28"}],"sha":"a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a78dbf27b2d4d704e1f302e338920aeb216735e1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T10:27:59Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T10:27:59Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Keep the tree expanded when a file is opened, add rename and delete\n\nThree things, all in the tree panel and the service behind it.\n\nOpening a file in a subfolder collapsed the tree back to the root, so every folder\nopened to reach that file had to be opened again for the next one. TreeElement does not\nmerely seed its expansion state from `defaultExpandedKeys` on mount, as the comment here\nassumed: it mirrors the prop into state in an effect keyed on the array and then drives\nthe tree''s `expandedKeys` from that state. The panel passed an inline `[ROOT_KEY]`, a new\narray on every render - and opening a file changes `selectedPath`, which renders the\npanel. `selectedKeys` had the same shape and wrote its state on every render too. Both\nare hoisted to stable values now. A full reload still collapses the tree, which is\nintended; that goes through the remount on `key={treeGeneration}`.\n\nRename and delete join create in the context menu, which files now get as well - until\nnow a right-click there fell through to the browser. Deleting always confirms first and\ntakes a folder''s whole subtree with it; the root itself is refused by both. Open editor\ntabs follow a rename and close when the file behind them is gone, including files inside\na renamed or deleted folder.\n\nBoth operations address the entry through its parent rather than through resolve(),\nwhich returns the realpath: renaming or deleting what a symlink points at is never what\nwas asked for, and the recursive delete unlinks symlinked directories instead of walking\ninto them. The path jail still applies, since it is the parent that gets resolved.\n\nWhile here: i18next escapes interpolated values by default, which is for translations\nrendered as raw HTML. Ours are rendered as text by React, so the only thing that escaping\nachieved was turning every path in a message into \"var&#x2F;log\".","tree":{"sha":"f7f3e35d0e977808fad86b5cab3ef8f3ddeff42c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/f7f3e35d0e977808fad86b5cab3ef8f3ddeff42c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKDgyNzdhM2M0MWQzZGMzNWIzNzgyM2JmMWM3MDBmNGMzYWY0YWVhMjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f","sha":"df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f"}],"sha":"8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/8277a3c41d3dc35b37823bf1c700f4c3af4aea28"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:06:19Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T14:06:19Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Open the root node by default and fix its alignment\n\nTwo problems with the root node introduced in v1.3.0.\n\nIt stayed collapsed: TreeElement does not forward expandedKeys to antd. It\nseeds its own internal expansion state from defaultExpandedKeys instead,\nwhich is verifiable in the running app - the controlled expandedKeys stops at\nthe TreeElement boundary while antd receives defaultExpandedKeys. Expansion\nis therefore no longer controlled from here; the tree is remounted on a full\nreload so the default applies again. Per-folder reload does not need it, as\nthe node keeps its key and stays expanded while its children are swapped.\n\nThe home icon also sat above the label rather than beside it, because antd''s\n`icon` slot is rendered as its own block in this tree. It now lives inside\nthe title, and `hasRoot` lines the root row up the way Studio''s own trees do.","tree":{"sha":"219551076b21b8f22f1863f2b63ed6c24f07b310","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/219551076b21b8f22f1863f2b63ed6c24f07b310"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKGRmNGFiNDc3NzgwMzYzZThlNzE5ZDhkYjk0YWFkM2NhYjkxNDJiNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db","sha":"525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db"}],"sha":"df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/df4ab477780363e8e719d8db94aad3cab9142b6f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:59:13Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:59:13Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Make the frontend build id independent of untracked files\n\nThe build id is a hash of the frontend sources and names the shipped archive,\nbut the walk that produced it also picked up .DS_Store — which is git-ignored,\nso it exists on a developer''s machine and never in CI or a fresh clone. The\ncommitted archive name therefore could not match what anyone else built from\nthe same sources, which is what the new CI check caught on its first run.\n\nOS and editor droppings are now skipped. Verified: building with and without\n.DS_Store present yields the same id.\n\nThe CI check now compares the build id rather than the archive bytes. The id\nis the source hash, so it is the property actually worth asserting; byte\ncomparison would also fail on harmless toolchain drift, such as a different\nnode minor re-minifying identical sources.","tree":{"sha":"e16f5698b390694bde08a28e004cab16a5dd1e17","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/e16f5698b390694bde08a28e004cab16a5dd1e17"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKDUyNWMyYjE2YzYzOTYyMGY1MTI4MmM3MTIyNDAwMjcxODgzZDkxZGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb","sha":"72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb"}],"sha":"525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/525c2b16c639620f51282c7122400271883d91db"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:56:10Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:56:10Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Show the project root as a tree node, add CI\n\nThe root had no node, so there was nowhere to right-click to create a file or\nfolder at the top level - the context menu only existed on directories below\nit. The root is now its own node with a home icon and the same menu. The API\naddresses the root as an empty path, which is not a usable antd key, so the\ntree works in keys and converts at the API boundary.\n\nCI runs the suite on PHP 8.4 and 8.5, type-checks the frontend, and rebuilds\nit to check the committed archive matches the sources. That last one matters\nbecause consumers install the archive rather than building it, so tagging\nwithout rebuilding would ship stale UI.\n\nThe php constraint claimed 8.3, which was never installable: pimcore/pimcore\n^2026.2 itself requires ~8.4 || ~8.5, so composer could not resolve on 8.3.","tree":{"sha":"d790a06bfa2a732431f790ac2f26ceed3bb61c67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/d790a06bfa2a732431f790ac2f26ceed3bb61c67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKDcyMjQzZWIxOGVhOWFiMjAxNjRkYzU4NmZmNTJkNjM4M2E4MDE3Y2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a","sha":"673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a"}],"sha":"72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/72243eb18ea9ab20164dc586ff52d6383a8017cb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:49:08Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:49:08Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Add file and folder creation to the tree context menu\n\nA directory''s right-click menu now offers \"New file\" and \"New folder\"\nalongside the existing reload. The name is asked for in a form modal, the\nentry is created through a new POST /entry endpoint, and only that folder is\nrefreshed. A new file is opened straight away, since creating one is almost\nalways the first half of editing it.\n\nThe name is validated as a single path segment: separators, \".\" and \"..\",\ncontrol characters and over-long names are rejected, so a caller cannot\nescape the parent directory it addressed. The parent still goes through the\nexisting path jail, excluded paths are refused on both the parent and the\nresulting path, and read-only mode refuses creation entirely. Existing\nentries are never overwritten - including names taken by a dangling symlink,\nwhich file_exists() alone does not report.\n\nRenaming and deleting stay out of scope.","tree":{"sha":"e4ab1bf27c9b26e1e5d1cac9ce10c2bf61f23a3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/e4ab1bf27c9b26e1e5d1cac9ce10c2bf61f23a3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKDY3M2NkODIxNWU2YzkwZTJjZTYxZDQ3ZTY5ZjM4NTAyMWZkYjM3OGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b","sha":"cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b"}],"sha":"673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/673cd8215e6c90e2ce61d47e69f385021fdb378a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:42:01Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:42:01Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Add English and German UI translations\n\nEvery user-facing label was hardcoded English. They now go through\nuseTranslation with keys namespaced under scop-file-viewer., including the\nmain navigation entry and the widget title, which take a translation key\nrather than a literal.\n\nCatalogues live in src/Resources/translations/studio.{en,de}.yaml. Symfony\ndiscovers them from the bundle path and Studio merges them into its own\nstudio catalogue, so nothing has to be registered. Flat dot notation is\nrequired - the Studio translator does not resolve nested YAML.\n\nTranslationsTest guards the failure modes that are invisible at build time:\na key used in the UI but not translated renders as the raw key, and a\nplaceholder that differs between locales renders literally for that locale.\nIt also fails on orphaned keys, which are usually half-applied renames.\n\nBackend exception messages are still English; they are returned by the API\nand shown as-is.","tree":{"sha":"8e164893d5e685f1bf57fe1f32e195bd9e8ebca0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/8e164893d5e685f1bf57fe1f32e195bd9e8ebca0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKGNkZjJlNTc0OGYyYjNlYzRjNTk3YjBlNjg1NjU1NjBlNjE5N2U2OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79","sha":"a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79"}],"sha":"cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/cdf2e5748f2b3ec4c597b0e68565560e6197e69b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:35:03Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:35:03Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Fix editor scrolling by constraining the tab pane height\n\nThe previous flex sizing was correct but not sufficient: antd sizes the\nactive tab pane from its content, so with a long file open the pane grew to\n1141px inside a 772px content box and every height below it inherited that.\nThe editor therefore still had no bounded height, .cm-scroller had nothing to\nscroll within, and long files were clipped instead of scrollable.\n\nConstraining .ant-tabs-content and .ant-tabs-tabpane to 100% height gives the\neditor a real box to scroll inside. Tabs'' own `fullHeight` prop does not reach\nthis element.\n\nVerified in the browser: the scroller goes from clientHeight 1083 /\nscrollHeight 1083 (nothing to scroll) to clientHeight 714 / scrollHeight 1083.","tree":{"sha":"06de3b777230c806f290dab3d0413224b1af4bca","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/06de3b777230c806f290dab3d0413224b1af4bca"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79","node_id":"C_kwDOUaaBhNoAKGE0ZjQzMTk4NDNiMDc4ODExN2E1ZjQ5YWU0NThiNThiNzc4MTNlNzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commit/be4a8b42ea8041ac26ea013c4f0b3e8ad91abfcd","sha":"be4a8b42ea8041ac26ea013c4f0b3e8ad91abfcd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/be4a8b42ea8041ac26ea013c4f0b3e8ad91abfcd"}],"sha":"a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/a4f4319843b0788117a5f49ae458b58b77813e79"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/commits/be4a8b42ea8041ac26ea013c4f0b3e8ad91abfcd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:29:16Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T13:29:16Z","email":"alex.scheider26@gmail.com","name":"Alexander Scheider"},"message":"Fix editor scrolling, fill the available width, add an editor border\n\nThe editor could not be scrolled: .cm-editor was sized with height: 100%,\nwhich only resolves against a parent with a definite height. Where it did\nnot resolve the editor grew to fit its content instead, so .cm-scroller had\nno bounded height to scroll within and a long file was simply clipped by the\nancestor''s overflow: hidden. It is now sized as a flex child (flex: 1;\nmin-height: 0), the same way Studio sizes its own CodeMirror instances.\n\nSplitLayout sizes are percentages and both items need one. Only the left item\nhad a size, so the right pane kept its default rather than claiming the\nremainder and left dead space to its right. Both items now get a\ncomplementary pair, and the tree yields width once a file is open.\n\nThe editor also gets a border in the Studio border token, with the focused\nstate picking up the primary colour.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c660789b9d257891695b54f50d8988d255560607","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/trees/c660789b9d257891695b54f50d8988d255560607"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/scope01-GmbH/ScopStudioFileViewerBundle/git/commits/be4a8b42ea8041ac26ea013c4f0b3e8ad91abfcd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6016485?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ascheider","id":6016485,"login":"ascheider","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwMTY0ODU=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ascheider/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https: