pi.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/commits/fa57cf9fca4cc56e50b87f111aff269f00417ac1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T12:44:50Z","email":"vadimkosenkov.work@gmail.com","name":"vadimkosenkov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T12:44:50Z","email":"vadimkosenkov.work@gmail.com","name":"vadimkosenkov"},"message":"feat: the iPhone app, with both quizzes inside its bundle\n\n- Capacitor 8 iOS project for the shell (apps/shell/capacitor.config.ts,\n  apps/shell/ios; Swift Package Manager, no CocoaPods).\n- The app ships the shell and both quiz remotes in one bundle, with a\n  manifest pointing inside it (ADR-013). Nothing in the applications\n  changes: only the manifest''s values differ from the web.\n- The welcome screen says that signing in does not work in the app yet\n  (Google refuses its sign-in page inside a web view); Phase 13b adds a\n  native sign-in.\n- The API now always allows the app''s origin `capacitor://localhost` in\n  CORS, without which every request from the app failed.\n- Nx targets ios-bundle / ios-sync / ios-open / serve-ios, and the\n  release workflow no longer fails when an environment has no variables.\n- Docs: ios.md, ADR-013, microfrontends, README, CLAUDE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"56837153d64cf578f3d624dfcfe263bf853e6ef7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/git/trees/56837153d64cf578f3d624dfcfe263bf853e6ef7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-