ments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/commits/d302528e1ffcd37aab1762c14144df3ed3737818/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:01:08Z","email":"vadimkosenkov.work@gmail.com","name":"vadimkosenkov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T11:01:08Z","email":"vadimkosenkov.work@gmail.com","name":"vadimkosenkov"},"message":"feat: container images, release pipeline and per-environment configuration\n\n- The shell reads config.json at start-up instead of compiling the API URL\n  and the Google client id in, so one build runs on every environment;\n  a deployment replaces config.json and federation.manifest.json\n  (tools/scripts/write-deploy-config.mjs). ADR-012.\n- The site sends its server configuration to the browser (TransferState):\n  links kept pointing at localhost after hydration.\n- Dockerfiles for the API (one image for every environment) and the site\n  (built per environment, because its pages are prerendered).\n- ci.yml builds both images on every PR; release.yml publishes them to\n  GHCR with the static bundles, and deploys to Render and Netlify once an\n  environment sets DEPLOY_ENABLED.\n- Docs: deploying.md, ADR-012, ci-cd.md, frontend.md, site.md, README,\n  CLAUDE.md.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83fc949a1e0780e8b61989655591811d783873af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/git/trees/83fc949a1e0780e8b61989655591811d783873af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/git/commits/d302528e1ffcd37aab1762c14144df3ed3737818","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81422814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov/followers","following_u