r-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/commits/c08334c0ac2188c9c90e1edbe81a2bd4599bd1e0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T15:48:02Z","email":"vadimkosenkov.work@gmail.com","name":"vadimkosenkov"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T15:48:02Z","email":"vadimkosenkov.work@gmail.com","name":"vadimkosenkov"},"message":"feat: set up Nx workspace foundation with enforced boundaries, CI and ADRs\n\nBootstrap the World Quiz monorepo: Nx 23 with Angular 22 apps (shell,\ncapitals, flags), an Express 5 API, a Cypress e2e project and two pure\nTypeScript libraries (quiz-domain, shared-util).\n\nArchitecture boundaries are enforced by tooling rather than convention:\nscope/type tags with @nx/enforce-module-boundaries, and a platform-purity\nguard for quiz-domain/shared-util (no DOM/Node types in tsconfig, banned\nframework and Node built-in imports) so the same quiz rules can run in the\nbrowser and on the server.\n\nAlso fixes .gitignore ignoring package-lock.json, which broke Nx''s project\ngraph, and drops tsconfig baseUrl, which TypeScript 6 deprecates.\n\nAdds GitHub Actions CI (format, lint, typecheck, test, build, Cypress e2e\nvia nx affected), ADR-001 (Nx), ADR-002 (Native Federation), ADR-007\n(testing), and documentation of the approved leaderboard and mastery rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"92597fd5d345831d01b88f8d40a56ac18a47ec57","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/git/trees/92597fd5d345831d01b88f8d40a56ac18a47ec57"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vadimkosenkov/angular-ionic-nx-mf-world-quiz/git/commits/c08334c0ac2188c9c90e1edbe81a2bd4599bd1e0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81422814?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkosenkov/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vadimkos