low","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/f1b7f065a18584e7f1456a8b0e36fb64b53e2aad","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGYxYjdmMDY1YTE4NTg0ZTdmMTQ1NmE4YjBlMzZmYjY0YjUzZTJhYWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b","sha":"f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b","sha":"30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b"}],"sha":"f1b7f065a18584e7f1456a8b0e36fb64b53e2aad","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/f1b7f065a18584e7f1456a8b0e36fb64b53e2aad"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:19:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:19:27Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(ci): build the remotes before the tests that check them\n\n`pnpm test` runs before `pnpm build:apps` in CI, so\n`remote-conformance.test.ts` had no `dist/` to read and every case in it\nthrew `ENOENT`. My previous commit turned that file''s silent skip into a\nhard failure — the right instinct for a rename that made it pass by doing\nnothing, the wrong assertion for a suite that legitimately runs before\nthe build.\n\nThe order in CI was also hiding the problem it caused: with `test` ahead\nof `build:apps`, those conformance checks had never run in CI at all,\nunder either the skip or this failure. `build:apps` now comes first, so\nthey run against real artefacts.\n\nThe suite is honest about all three states instead of conflating them:\n\n- the app directories it names are checked whatever the build state, so a\n  rename fails with the directory that no longer exists — the case the\n  last commit was reaching for,\n- no artefacts at all means nobody has run `pnpm build:apps`, which skips\n  rather than failing on a clean checkout,\n- some but not all means a broken or partial build, which still fails and\n  names the remotes that are missing.\n\nReproduced each one: moved every `dist/` aside (skips), restored one of\nfour (fails naming the other three), and pointed one entry at a\ndirectory that does not exist (fails naming it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"5feeaa81ad70e5650a2250c7b4a59c2911672220","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/5feeaa81ad70e5650a2250c7b4a59c2911672220"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b","verification":{"payload":"tree 5feeaa81ad70e5650a2250c7b4a59c2911672220\nparent 93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789492767 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789492767 +0000\n\nfix(ci): build the remotes before the tests that check them\n\n`pnpm test` runs before `pnpm build:apps` in CI, so\n`remote-conformance.test.ts` had no `dist/` to read and every case in it\nthrew `ENOENT`. My previous commit turned that file''s silent skip into a\nhard failure — the right instinct for a rename that made it pass by doing\nnothing, the wrong assertion for a suite that legitimately runs before\nthe build.\n\nThe order in CI was also hiding the problem it caused: with `test` ahead\nof `build:apps`, those conformance checks had never run in CI at all,\nunder either the skip or this failure. `build:apps` now comes first, so\nthey run against real artefacts.\n\nThe suite is honest about all three states instead of conflating them:\n\n- the app directories it names are checked whatever the build state, so a\n  rename fails with the directory that no longer exists — the case the\n  last commit was reaching for,\n- no artefacts at all means nobody has run `pnpm build:apps`, which skips\n  rather than failing on a clean checkout,\n- some but not all means a broken or partial build, which still fails and\n  names the remotes that are missing.\n\nReproduced each one: moved every `dist/` aside (skips), restored one of\nfour (fails naming the other three), and pointed one entry at a\ndirectory that does not exist (fails naming it).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAv0r95A\nJ3IXtOaNa6+FIf/+fNZa1Zle08b1Lj2BrubNHHkowznHS0QOpoKPPmxUoKwJg7qQCvwZpDqPN67v\nhQQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T17:19:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDMwMTkwYThmNTA5YTI2ODQwNzY0Zjg0ZmNiNDIxOThkNzYyZDRjMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2","sha":"93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2"}],"sha":"30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/30190a8f509a26840764f84fcb42198d762d4c0b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:13:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:13:40Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(deps): point the lockfile importers at the renamed app directories\n\nCI could not install: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` failed with\n`ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE` against `apps/field-widgets/package.json`,\nreporting all 22 of its dependencies as \"added\". The app directories were\nrenamed with `git mv` and the lockfile still named the old ones, so from\npnpm''s point of view four packages had vanished and four new ones had\nappeared with no resolutions.\n\nNothing about the dependency graph changed, so neither does the lockfile\nbeyond the four importer keys, re-sorted as pnpm writes them. Verified as\nexactly that: parsed both versions and compared them, with the rename\napplied, key by key — the importers match and every other section is\nuntouched, which also rules out the git+ssh fallback the boundary test\nguards against (this machine cannot reach codeload). `pnpm install\n--frozen-lockfile` now reports \"Lockfile is up to date, resolution step\nis skipped\", which is the check that failed.\n\nThe boundary test gains the rule that would have caught it. A local\ninstall keeps working with a stale importer, because `node_modules` is\nalready linked — only CI''s `--frozen-lockfile` notices — so the\nlockfile''s importers are now checked against the workspace directories\non disk. Confirmed the new test fails when one importer is renamed back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"007914bfa4f2776251b2be922186a3fef8954c4a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/007914bfa4f2776251b2be922186a3fef8954c4a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2","verification":{"payload":"tree 007914bfa4f2776251b2be922186a3fef8954c4a\nparent 9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789492420 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789492420 +0000\n\nfix(deps): point the lockfile importers at the renamed app directories\n\nCI could not install: `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` failed with\n`ERR_PNPM_OUTDATED_LOCKFILE` against `apps/field-widgets/package.json`,\nreporting all 22 of its dependencies as \"added\". The app directories were\nrenamed with `git mv` and the lockfile still named the old ones, so from\npnpm''s point of view four packages had vanished and four new ones had\nappeared with no resolutions.\n\nNothing about the dependency graph changed, so neither does the lockfile\nbeyond the four importer keys, re-sorted as pnpm writes them. Verified as\nexactly that: parsed both versions and compared them, with the rename\napplied, key by key — the importers match and every other section is\nuntouched, which also rules out the git+ssh fallback the boundary test\nguards against (this machine cannot reach codeload). `pnpm install\n--frozen-lockfile` now reports \"Lockfile is up to date, resolution step\nis skipped\", which is the check that failed.\n\nThe boundary test gains the rule that would have caught it. A local\ninstall keeps working with a stale importer, because `node_modules` is\nalready linked — only CI''s `--frozen-lockfile` notices — so the\nlockfile''s importers are now checked against the workspace directories\non disk. Confirmed the new test fails when one importer is renamed back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAt/qrEn\nvi0yVRE9gCAnAn9/6B2ly7wAGqkXMLbAlOEb95zN0NeyJZmls+3dPFsgbo9GgCt0S80NsR/Spm59\nPgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T17:13:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDkzYTZjYTZjZDFhYTBjNzg4OGUwMzdmNzlkODc5YjA3Y2RkZTdjYTI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496","sha":"9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496"}],"sha":"93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/93a6ca6cd1aa0c7888e037f79d879b07cdde7ca2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:07:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T17:07:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: typecheck the test harness, which was hiding two dead test ids\n\n`pnpm typecheck` ran `pnpm -r run typecheck`, and pnpm''s `-r` excludes the\nworkspace root, so nothing ever typechecked the root project — `test/**`,\n`scripts/**`, `playwright.config.ts`. The HMR spec was reading\n`ids.widgets.rigStatusIncrement` and `ids.widgets.kpiTile`, neither of\nwhich exists on `TEST_IDS` any more; both came back `undefined` and\nPlaywright failed on a `getByTestId(undefined)` instead of at compile\ntime. The root project is now typechecked first, which needed `allowJs`\n(the specs import the plain-JS helpers in `scripts/`) and a JSDoc\nsignature on `conformanceEnv`.\n\nAlso:\n\n- the dead test ids are now the live ones (`rigStatusAdvance`,\n  `productionKpi`), so the HMR spec runs again,\n- `test/e2e/zz-probe.spec.ts` was a debugging scratch spec that should\n  never have been committed,\n- the devtools tab list stopped short of the dock''s right edge, leaving\n  its bottom border hanging in mid-air,\n- `fitView` on the dependency graph clamped only its maximum zoom, so a\n  wide graph opened shrunk to `minZoom` with illegible labels; it now\n  clamps both ends and the user pans,\n- the \"light theme\" screenshot was capturing the dark theme with the\n  palette still open: react-aria''s search field takes the first Escape to\n  clear the query, so it never closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"88b7ede133509fe1f8f5e80d7e89d340e3b43f8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/88b7ede133509fe1f8f5e80d7e89d340e3b43f8a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496","verification":{"payload":"tree 88b7ede133509fe1f8f5e80d7e89d340e3b43f8a\nparent 75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789492030 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789492030 +0000\n\nfix: typecheck the test harness, which was hiding two dead test ids\n\n`pnpm typecheck` ran `pnpm -r run typecheck`, and pnpm''s `-r` excludes the\nworkspace root, so nothing ever typechecked the root project — `test/**`,\n`scripts/**`, `playwright.config.ts`. The HMR spec was reading\n`ids.widgets.rigStatusIncrement` and `ids.widgets.kpiTile`, neither of\nwhich exists on `TEST_IDS` any more; both came back `undefined` and\nPlaywright failed on a `getByTestId(undefined)` instead of at compile\ntime. The root project is now typechecked first, which needed `allowJs`\n(the specs import the plain-JS helpers in `scripts/`) and a JSDoc\nsignature on `conformanceEnv`.\n\nAlso:\n\n- the dead test ids are now the live ones (`rigStatusAdvance`,\n  `productionKpi`), so the HMR spec runs again,\n- `test/e2e/zz-probe.spec.ts` was a debugging scratch spec that should\n  never have been committed,\n- the devtools tab list stopped short of the dock''s right edge, leaving\n  its bottom border hanging in mid-air,\n- `fitView` on the dependency graph clamped only its maximum zoom, so a\n  wide graph opened shrunk to `minZoom` with illegible labels; it now\n  clamps both ends and the user pans,\n- the \"light theme\" screenshot was capturing the dark theme with the\n  palette still open: react-aria''s search field takes the first Escape to\n  clear the query, so it never closed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFvab0J+\n/6n43vjQBe8NQMKTfpKpaO0ZKwsLdPIQ/maF+PFXzZiEXt4I1h5lTDRftK5/Gt29hkAWijHF79K0\nvwA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T17:07:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDk0NThlMWE2NTFlN2QxNDk4N2M0ZmRjMTQ0MjMwMjJlYjQ0ZWE0OTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34","sha":"75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34"}],"sha":"9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/9458e1a651e7d14987c4fdc14423022eb44ea496"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:55:23Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:55:23Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: follow the subsurface rename through the docs and the CLI tests\n\nThe rename in 05314d1 left the prose behind. Every page that named an\nasset, `asset-tracker`, `legacy-reports`, `widget-a` or `widget-b` now\nnames the well, `well-planner`, `production-reports`, `subsurface-widgets`\nor `field-widgets` it actually refers to, and the API-reference generator\nin `apps/docs/scripts/docs-lib.mjs` was fixed at the source rather than in\nits generated output.\n\nAlso:\n\n- the docs home page said \"Four packages\" while the repository ships six;\n  `@platform/host-react` and `@platform/devtools` were missing cards,\n- `developer-tools.mdx` still described the floating drawer rather than\n  the bottom dock,\n- `examples.mdx` described the old contrived apps and did not list\n  `screenshots.spec.ts`,\n- `packages/cli/test/{create,create-lint}.test.ts` still asserted the old\n  template file map (`src/routes/assets/**`, `src/widgets/asset-card.tsx`),\n  which the new scaffold no longer produces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"a67dbc06486eeb6179b2dce23734b484ad7e3ff0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/a67dbc06486eeb6179b2dce23734b484ad7e3ff0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34","verification":{"payload":"tree a67dbc06486eeb6179b2dce23734b484ad7e3ff0\nparent 05314d17d68dd5d9ee93c07320c875b95cbf2546\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789491323 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789491323 +0000\n\ndocs: follow the subsurface rename through the docs and the CLI tests\n\nThe rename in 05314d1 left the prose behind. Every page that named an\nasset, `asset-tracker`, `legacy-reports`, `widget-a` or `widget-b` now\nnames the well, `well-planner`, `production-reports`, `subsurface-widgets`\nor `field-widgets` it actually refers to, and the API-reference generator\nin `apps/docs/scripts/docs-lib.mjs` was fixed at the source rather than in\nits generated output.\n\nAlso:\n\n- the docs home page said \"Four packages\" while the repository ships six;\n  `@platform/host-react` and `@platform/devtools` were missing cards,\n- `developer-tools.mdx` still described the floating drawer rather than\n  the bottom dock,\n- `examples.mdx` described the old contrived apps and did not list\n  `screenshots.spec.ts`,\n- `packages/cli/test/{create,create-lint}.test.ts` still asserted the old\n  template file map (`src/routes/assets/**`, `src/widgets/asset-card.tsx`),\n  which the new scaffold no longer produces.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFDOa+dm\nhE9/mxsQLVGfZpVTjQHMRwPChycHKGWaNp6RH97pI6H70spfLANgpOQc+ObvypUxppP5SUZdGiFN\nawg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T17:07:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDc1NzYzY2Q1ZTNlY2JjNWUzN2E3ZmI1NDk2YTc0OTM2MzAwNGNjMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/05314d17d68dd5d9ee93c07320c875b95cbf2546","sha":"05314d17d68dd5d9ee93c07320c875b95cbf2546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/05314d17d68dd5d9ee93c07320c875b95cbf2546"}],"sha":"75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/75763cd5e3ecbc5e37a7fb5496a749363004cc34"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/05314d17d68dd5d9ee93c07320c875b95cbf2546/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:27:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T16:27:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat: rebuild the shell, examples and devtools on Tecton''s own patterns\n\nThe platform shipped adapters for Tecton and then hand-rolled the things\nTecton already ships. `@tecton/react/tecton/shell-actions` — the command\ntrigger, the icon action cluster, the overflow menu, the user menu — was\nimported nowhere in the repo. The header was instead two raw `<select>`\nelements, a button whose label read `Theme: dark`, a bare `<span>` for the\nuser, and no visible way to open the command palette at all, although\n`TEST_IDS.shell.paletteTrigger` had been defined since the first commit.\n`tecton/page-header`, `tecton/panel`, `tecton/stat`, `tecton/meter`,\n`components/{empty,input-group,chip,checkbox,dropdown-menu}` were all present\nand all unused. Tecton''s own gallery ships `shell-01`, \"the micro-frontend\nhost\" — our product, already designed. We had built a worse one beside it.\n\n**The shell is a host again.** `ShellHeader` composes `AppShellHeader` with the\napp finder (moved out of the home page, where it read as a link list), the\nbreadcrumb trail as the application context slot, `ShellCommandTrigger`,\n`ShellActions` for help, what''s new, developer tools and settings, a\n`ShellOverflow` below `lg`, and a `ShellUserMenu` that absorbs the two selects\nand the theme toggle. `?` opens a shortcuts dialog listing every shortcut the\ncommand registry knows, so a remote''s shortcuts appear the moment it mounts.\nEvery shell route gets a `PageHeader`; the failure lab is `Panel`s; the 404s\nare a `page-state` composition rather than an `<h1>404</h1>`.\n\n**The examples are a showcase.** They were three pumps, two reports and a\nwidget that was literally a counter. They are now a subsurface domain built\nfrom the same models as Tecton''s blocks: 18 typed wells, field development\nalternatives with real economics, horizons and a production series.\n`well-planner` is concept-select FDA cards, a filterable well inventory with\nselection and row actions, and a well detail page with section tabs.\n`production-reports` keeps its deliberate absence of a design system — that is\nwhat proves a remote can bring its own stack — but is a real reporting app,\nand now honours the shell''s theme instead of rendering dark text on a dark\nground. The widget libraries export well summaries, production KPIs with\nperiod-on-period deltas, FDA status and rig tallies.\n\n  asset-tracker  -> well-planner        legacy-reports -> production-reports\n  widget-a       -> subsurface-widgets  widget-b       -> field-widgets\n\n**The developer tools dock like a browser''s.** A small bug icon in the\nbottom-right corner opens a full-width panel along the bottom edge, resizable\nby dragging its top edge, with its height and open state remembered per\nbrowser and `Esc` to close — the TanStack Router Devtools shape. Full width\nmeans the thirteen tabs fit one row again, so the wrap workaround from\n`cd1720e` is deleted rather than kept. The dependency graph gets a real node\ncomponent instead of a string with an embedded newline, a themed minimap that\nis no longer a white rectangle on the dark theme, share scopes as tints rather\nthan fills, a grid layout for the package column so `fitView` stops shrinking\nthe graph below legibility, and `useNodesState` so a dragged node survives the\n250 ms snapshot refresh.\n\nTwo defects found by looking at the running pages rather than by any test:\n\n- `/settings` crashed with React error #185. A selector I wrote for the\n  shortcuts dialog mapped registry entries to fresh objects, and `shallowEqual`\n  compares array elements by identity, so every `getSnapshot` returned a new\n  value and `useSyncExternalStore` never settled. It selects the registry''s own\n  entries now and maps in a memo.\n- `remote-conformance.test.ts` skipped its whole suite after the directory\n  rename — `describe.skipIf(!built)` over paths that no longer existed. The\n  missing-build case is now a named failing test instead of a silent pass.\n\n`test/e2e/screenshots.spec.ts` captures every surface into `test-results/`, so\nthe next regression of this kind shows up as a CI artefact.\n\n`tsconfig.app.json` turns `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` off for applications\nonly: `@tecton/react` is consumed as source, and its `tecton/overflow.tsx`\nindexes arrays without guarding. `internal/*` and `packages/*` — the code that\nships — keep the flag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"2375cb2d3d3973ed137b59f7f37b047297c04a9e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/2375cb2d3d3973ed137b59f7f37b047297c04a9e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/05314d17d68dd5d9ee93c07320c875b95cbf2546","verification":{"payload":"tree 2375cb2d3d3973ed137b59f7f37b047297c04a9e\nparent f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789489646 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789489646 +0000\n\nfeat: rebuild the shell, examples and devtools on Tecton''s own patterns\n\nThe platform shipped adapters for Tecton and then hand-rolled the things\nTecton already ships. `@tecton/react/tecton/shell-actions` — the command\ntrigger, the icon action cluster, the overflow menu, the user menu — was\nimported nowhere in the repo. The header was instead two raw `<select>`\nelements, a button whose label read `Theme: dark`, a bare `<span>` for the\nuser, and no visible way to open the command palette at all, although\n`TEST_IDS.shell.paletteTrigger` had been defined since the first commit.\n`tecton/page-header`, `tecton/panel`, `tecton/stat`, `tecton/meter`,\n`components/{empty,input-group,chip,checkbox,dropdown-menu}` were all present\nand all unused. Tecton''s own gallery ships `shell-01`, \"the micro-frontend\nhost\" — our product, already designed. We had built a worse one beside it.\n\n**The shell is a host again.** `ShellHeader` composes `AppShellHeader` with the\napp finder (moved out of the home page, where it read as a link list), the\nbreadcrumb trail as the application context slot, `ShellCommandTrigger`,\n`ShellActions` for help, what''s new, developer tools and settings, a\n`ShellOverflow` below `lg`, and a `ShellUserMenu` that absorbs the two selects\nand the theme toggle. `?` opens a shortcuts dialog listing every shortcut the\ncommand registry knows, so a remote''s shortcuts appear the moment it mounts.\nEvery shell route gets a `PageHeader`; the failure lab is `Panel`s; the 404s\nare a `page-state` composition rather than an `<h1>404</h1>`.\n\n**The examples are a showcase.** They were three pumps, two reports and a\nwidget that was literally a counter. They are now a subsurface domain built\nfrom the same models as Tecton''s blocks: 18 typed wells, field development\nalternatives with real economics, horizons and a production series.\n`well-planner` is concept-select FDA cards, a filterable well inventory with\nselection and row actions, and a well detail page with section tabs.\n`production-reports` keeps its deliberate absence of a design system — that is\nwhat proves a remote can bring its own stack — but is a real reporting app,\nand now honours the shell''s theme instead of rendering dark text on a dark\nground. The widget libraries export well summaries, production KPIs with\nperiod-on-period deltas, FDA status and rig tallies.\n\n  asset-tracker  -> well-planner        legacy-reports -> production-reports\n  widget-a       -> subsurface-widgets  widget-b       -> field-widgets\n\n**The developer tools dock like a browser''s.** A small bug icon in the\nbottom-right corner opens a full-width panel along the bottom edge, resizable\nby dragging its top edge, with its height and open state remembered per\nbrowser and `Esc` to close — the TanStack Router Devtools shape. Full width\nmeans the thirteen tabs fit one row again, so the wrap workaround from\n`cd1720e` is deleted rather than kept. The dependency graph gets a real node\ncomponent instead of a string with an embedded newline, a themed minimap that\nis no longer a white rectangle on the dark theme, share scopes as tints rather\nthan fills, a grid layout for the package column so `fitView` stops shrinking\nthe graph below legibility, and `useNodesState` so a dragged node survives the\n250 ms snapshot refresh.\n\nTwo defects found by looking at the running pages rather than by any test:\n\n- `/settings` crashed with React error #185. A selector I wrote for the\n  shortcuts dialog mapped registry entries to fresh objects, and `shallowEqual`\n  compares array elements by identity, so every `getSnapshot` returned a new\n  value and `useSyncExternalStore` never settled. It selects the registry''s own\n  entries now and maps in a memo.\n- `remote-conformance.test.ts` skipped its whole suite after the directory\n  rename — `describe.skipIf(!built)` over paths that no longer existed. The\n  missing-build case is now a named failing test instead of a silent pass.\n\n`test/e2e/screenshots.spec.ts` captures every surface into `test-results/`, so\nthe next regression of this kind shows up as a CI artefact.\n\n`tsconfig.app.json` turns `noUncheckedIndexedAccess` off for applications\nonly: `@tecton/react` is consumed as source, and its `tecton/overflow.tsx`\nindexes arrays without guarding. `internal/*` and `packages/*` — the code that\nships — keep the flag.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCMZBVTj\nOB4e/ih3Bnnf0M3rY99O7MilyAHiTf+aiUtXq+5GnH3gYQ7T+86mHoDYn4RPbxLcIdd6poTFLbgx\nNwg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T17:07:18Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/05314d17d68dd5d9ee93c07320c875b95cbf2546","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDA1MzE0ZDE3ZDY4ZGQ1ZDllZTkzYzA3MzIwYzg3NWI5NWNiZjI1NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b","sha":"f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platfor