o}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGYzMWJmMzFjY2Y2YjJiOGQxY2JiYTBhYmNhOTFlNzFhZWQ3NThhOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/7dd0d9ba4399eb9c1528cf4ea49acbb3b8d5fa1e","sha":"7dd0d9ba4399eb9c1528cf4ea49acbb3b8d5fa1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/7dd0d9ba4399eb9c1528cf4ea49acbb3b8d5fa1e"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96","sha":"cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96"}],"sha":"f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/f31bf31ccf6b2b8d1cbba0abca91e71aed758a9b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T15:21:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T15:21:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(devtools): the Faults panel was unreadable, and the tab row overlapped it\n\nBoth defects were visible only by looking at the page — the E2E asserts on\nroles and dispatches events, so it passed against a panel no one could read.\n\nTecton''s `Switch` renders its children *inside* the pill track, a fixed\n34x16 box. The Faults panel passed each fault''s description as children, so\nevery label spilled out of its switch and painted over the ones beside it.\nThe label belongs beside the switch, tied to it by id — which is how the\nshell''s own settings host renders a boolean field.\n\nThe tab row is the second half. Tecton sizes a tab list to one row and each\ntab to `calc(100% - 1px)` of it, so the thirteenth tab (Faults) wrapped onto\na second row that fell outside the list''s height and drew over the panel\ncontent — the rule under it struck through \"PER REMOTE\". Releasing the\nlist''s height alone does not work: the tabs resolve their own height against\nit, so an auto-height list has nothing to resolve against and the tabs\nstretch. The list now grows with its rows, each tab takes its own text''s\nheight, and neither grows to fill a row it happens to be alone on.\n\nVerified by screenshotting the shell, both panels, the palette, the settings\nhost, the widget dashboard, the fault-injected error state and both themes.\n574 unit tests and 27 E2E pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"c096f53cea70716ea8b2c6ee6dc5a5e3174e7f91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/c096f53cea70716ea8b2c6ee6dc5a5e3174e7f91"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96","verification":{"payload":"tree c096f53cea70716ea8b2c6ee6dc5a5e3174e7f91\nparent 0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789485667 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789485667 +0000\n\nfix(devtools): the Faults panel was unreadable, and the tab row overlapped it\n\nBoth defects were visible only by looking at the page — the E2E asserts on\nroles and dispatches events, so it passed against a panel no one could read.\n\nTecton''s `Switch` renders its children *inside* the pill track, a fixed\n34x16 box. The Faults panel passed each fault''s description as children, so\nevery label spilled out of its switch and painted over the ones beside it.\nThe label belongs beside the switch, tied to it by id — which is how the\nshell''s own settings host renders a boolean field.\n\nThe tab row is the second half. Tecton sizes a tab list to one row and each\ntab to `calc(100% - 1px)` of it, so the thirteenth tab (Faults) wrapped onto\na second row that fell outside the list''s height and drew over the panel\ncontent — the rule under it struck through \"PER REMOTE\". Releasing the\nlist''s height alone does not work: the tabs resolve their own height against\nit, so an auto-height list has nothing to resolve against and the tabs\nstretch. The list now grows with its rows, each tab takes its own text''s\nheight, and neither grows to fill a row it happens to be alone on.\n\nVerified by screenshotting the shell, both panels, the palette, the settings\nhost, the widget dashboard, the fault-injected error state and both themes.\n574 unit tests and 27 E2E pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGXv1ON3\nv49BRv7CAmSWYbLhDlW5pbKWMHJQ+blmMLgl1VbqZShzKh0X/FDCzqqLO7a3Ry0HlB56MMtoKY2P\nnQg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T15:21:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGNkMTcyMGVmZjI0NmFkYTExYTg0MDA3ZTE0NmJiYWQ2NzIxMjRmOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f","sha":"0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f"}],"sha":"cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/cd1720eff246ada11a84007e146bbad672124f96"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:50:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:50:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: drop the removed `hostKind` option from the host reference\n\n`80f3471` removed `PlatformHostOptions.hostKind` and `PlatformHost.kind`,\nbut three places still documented them: the `createPlatformHost` example\nand the `PlatformHost` member table in the host reference page, and the\nAPI-surface line in `renderLlmTxt()`.\n\nEdited the generator rather than `llm.txt`, then regenerated. `docs:check`\npasses over 71 pages and the site builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"eeb3c30d0f791d386efc19df7105ab2ac09f1ca2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/eeb3c30d0f791d386efc19df7105ab2ac09f1ca2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f","verification":{"payload":"tree eeb3c30d0f791d386efc19df7105ab2ac09f1ca2\nparent 80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789483817 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789483817 +0000\n\ndocs: drop the removed `hostKind` option from the host reference\n\n`80f3471` removed `PlatformHostOptions.hostKind` and `PlatformHost.kind`,\nbut three places still documented them: the `createPlatformHost` example\nand the `PlatformHost` member table in the host reference page, and the\nAPI-surface line in `renderLlmTxt()`.\n\nEdited the generator rather than `llm.txt`, then regenerated. `docs:check`\npasses over 71 pages and the site builds.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQFVYP6NF\nAEhQmoeIexTlqFqRwkl/dJmces76eUiMy0fBfzvLEe43Zv4sBKxfR0K4eORaYcofS/0A2WavRvW3\nIwY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T14:50:24Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDA2MjdiZDQzOTVmYWM4NWNkZDczMmFhNjQ3ZDI2ODM3NzA2YTYxMWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b","sha":"80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b"}],"sha":"0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/0627bd4395fac85cdd732aa647d26837706a611f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:32:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:32:11Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor: remove the host `kind` field\n\n`kind` was `\"shell\" | \"harness\"`, and with the harness gone it could only ever\nbe `\"shell\"` — a field that tells a remote nothing. It is gone from\n`HostBridge.host`, from `MfeInstance.host`, from `DiagnosticSnapshot.host` and\nfrom `PlatformHost`, along with the `PlatformHostOptions.hostKind` option that\nset it.\n\nThis is a breaking change to the bridge contract, which\n`internal/core/src/protocol.ts` says takes a protocol major bump. The protocol\nstays at 1.0 deliberately: nothing is in production, so there is no remote built\nagainst the old shape to keep loading, and bumping to 2.0 now would say more\nabout compatibility than is true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"b42a43e19f549eddd64ce1539656d3cbb1a64d90","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/b42a43e19f549eddd64ce1539656d3cbb1a64d90"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b","verification":{"payload":"tree b42a43e19f549eddd64ce1539656d3cbb1a64d90\nparent 5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789482731 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789482731 +0000\n\nrefactor: remove the host `kind` field\n\n`kind` was `\"shell\" | \"harness\"`, and with the harness gone it could only ever\nbe `\"shell\"` — a field that tells a remote nothing. It is gone from\n`HostBridge.host`, from `MfeInstance.host`, from `DiagnosticSnapshot.host` and\nfrom `PlatformHost`, along with the `PlatformHostOptions.hostKind` option that\nset it.\n\nThis is a breaking change to the bridge contract, which\n`internal/core/src/protocol.ts` says takes a protocol major bump. The protocol\nstays at 1.0 deliberately: nothing is in production, so there is no remote built\nagainst the old shape to keep loading, and bumping to 2.0 now would say more\nabout compatibility than is true.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJpF60YT\ndTNFBdaznIHYOpiNgzKPPo5hZv66nSL/n5WtTj3qmgjSTSXWUN8jQ7+3O4AIas5LxZMSD+N9jzFT\nXAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T14:32:15Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDgwZjM0NzFmNDY3MTQ3NGY0NDBiNjI0YTRmZjM3ODM5NDNiYTQzMGI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381","sha":"5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381"}],"sha":"80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/80f3471f4671474f440b624a4ff3783943ba430b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:23:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:23:59Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor: drop the last of the harness — the \"harness\" host kind\n\nDeleting the harness left `hostKind: \"shell\" | \"harness\"` behind as a union\nwhose second value nothing could produce. The only things still saying\n\"harness\" were two test bridges describing themselves as one, and the developer\ntools rendering `Shell (shell)` in the dependency graph and the overview panel.\n\nSo: the `\"harness\"` variant is gone from `HostBridge.host.kind`, from the\ndiagnostic snapshot and from `PlatformHost`, and `PlatformHostOptions.hostKind`\n— an option that existed only to build a harness — is gone with it. A shell no\nlonger declares what kind of host it is, because there is only one kind.\n\n`kind` itself stays. Removing a field from `HostBridge` is a breaking change to\nthe bridge contract, which `internal/core/src/protocol.ts` says requires a\nprotocol major bump: every remote built for 1.0 would stop loading. Narrowing a\nunion is not — a remote reading `bridge.host.kind` still gets a string, from a\nsmaller set — so this needs no bump and no rebuild.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"2931017e7186072931a284b2984b30656000fd0f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/2931017e7186072931a284b2984b30656000fd0f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381","verification":{"payload":"tree 2931017e7186072931a284b2984b30656000fd0f\nparent 63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789482239 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789482239 +0000\n\nrefactor: drop the last of the harness — the \"harness\" host kind\n\nDeleting the harness left `hostKind: \"shell\" | \"harness\"` behind as a union\nwhose second value nothing could produce. The only things still saying\n\"harness\" were two test bridges describing themselves as one, and the developer\ntools rendering `Shell (shell)` in the dependency graph and the overview panel.\n\nSo: the `\"harness\"` variant is gone from `HostBridge.host.kind`, from the\ndiagnostic snapshot and from `PlatformHost`, and `PlatformHostOptions.hostKind`\n— an option that existed only to build a harness — is gone with it. A shell no\nlonger declares what kind of host it is, because there is only one kind.\n\n`kind` itself stays. Removing a field from `HostBridge` is a breaking change to\nthe bridge contract, which `internal/core/src/protocol.ts` says requires a\nprotocol major bump: every remote built for 1.0 would stop loading. Narrowing a\nunion is not — a remote reading `bridge.host.kind` still gets a string, from a\nsmaller set — so this needs no bump and no rebuild.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQE4xXk4k\nv/umYzZDVqVKhWgP+qPMasyCkxxNLRx5ltxtJGGmOcmG8xA2z1ePCq4et3wX2eiqRY1DV9rUgkIe\nLQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T14:24:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDVhOWUzNDAxM2Y2MzRjZjg3ZWE5ZDc2YzlhOGQ5NzU5ODcyMDkzODE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de","sha":"63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de"}],"sha":"5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/5a9e34013f634cf87ea9d76c9a8d975987209381"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:16:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T14:16:07Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(deps): restore the codeload resolution for @tecton/react\n\nCI could not install: pnpm tried `git clone git@github.com:rpkapps/tecton-ui-1.git`\nand got `Permission denied (publickey)`, because the lockfile asked it to.\n\n`@tecton/react` is a git dependency, and pnpm normally resolves it to a codeload\ntarball over HTTPS — which is what `main` has. Regenerating the lockfile during\nthis work happened on a machine that cannot reach codeload, so pnpm silently\nfell back to an SSH git clone and wrote that into the lockfile. It works for\nanyone with an SSH key and fails for CI, which has none.\n\nThe nine affected lines are now byte-identical to `main`; no other dependency\nwas resolved over git. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` reports \"Lockfile is up\nto date\", so the lockfile still matches the manifests.\n\nThe boundary test gains a rule for it, because the failure mode is silent: a\nlockfile regenerated behind a restrictive network looks fine locally and breaks\nonly in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"5d823509ff20e51d2fe5cf9e9b33ee9e44569644","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/5d823509ff20e51d2fe5cf9e9b33ee9e44569644"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de","verification":{"payload":"tree 5d823509ff20e51d2fe5cf9e9b33ee9e44569644\nparent d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789481767 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789481767 +0000\n\nfix(deps): restore the codeload resolution for @tecton/react\n\nCI could not install: pnpm tried `git clone git@github.com:rpkapps/tecton-ui-1.git`\nand got `Permission denied (publickey)`, because the lockfile asked it to.\n\n`@tecton/react` is a git dependency, and pnpm normally resolves it to a codeload\ntarball over HTTPS — which is what `main` has. Regenerating the lockfile during\nthis work happened on a machine that cannot reach codeload, so pnpm silently\nfell back to an SSH git clone and wrote that into the lockfile. It works for\nanyone with an SSH key and fails for CI, which has none.\n\nThe nine affected lines are now byte-identical to `main`; no other dependency\nwas resolved over git. `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile` reports \"Lockfile is up\nto date\", so the lockfile still matches the manifests.\n\nThe boundary test gains a rule for it, because the failure mode is silent: a\nlockfile regenerated behind a restrictive network looks fine locally and breaks\nonly in CI.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBV3XKY5\nBh7kAvK2CXDoi9NG/CXsrW083GuPOc3WJUrOQVion2vEAEeWKXl2X15c6Dp2+7oeyf0iJinrj6ma\ncQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T14:16:10Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDYzZWFiZDM3NTg3Mzg1ODUyNGU1NjUyMjg1MjkxNTIzMjllOGQyZGU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701","sha":"d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701"}],"sha":"63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/63eabd375873858524e565228529152329e8d2de"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:32:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T13:32:17Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix: three defects the full verification found\n\nRunning the whole suite against a real Tecton checkout turned up three things\nthe partial run could not reach:\n\n- `apps/docs` failed to build: an unquoted colon in the developer-tools\n  frontmatter description is a YAML nested mapping. `docs:check`''s parser\n  tolerated it; the site''s did not.\n- The developer-tools chunk a shell lazily imports was named `dist-*.js`,\n  because the package''s build entry was `index`. Naming the entry `devtools`\n  makes it `devtools-*.js` for every shell, which is what belongs in a network\n  panel — and what the E2E identifies it by.\n- The fault-injection E2E reloaded the page to force a re-load, which builds a\n  new host and so clears the faults; and it navigated through the dashboard,\n  which mounts a widget from the remote it had just made unavailable. It now\n  navigates through the landing route, on the same host. Faults being per-host\n  and cleared by a reload is the right behaviour for a developer tool — you\n  cannot set one and forget it — so the documentation says so.\n\nVerified end to end: `pnpm check`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm build:apps` and\n`pnpm e2e` (27 tests, production and HMR projects) all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"60117ae169d5b4b54b9da1fc3a72095710e092f8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/60117ae169d5b4b54b9da1fc3a72095710e092f8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701","verification":{"payload":"tree 60117ae169d5b4b54b9da1fc3a72095710e092f8\nparent 18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789479137 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789479137 +0000\n\nfix: three defects the full verification found\n\nRunning the whole suite against a real Tecton checkout turned up three things\nthe partial run could not reach:\n\n- `apps/docs` failed to build: an unquoted colon in the developer-tools\n  frontmatter description is a YAML nested mapping. `docs:check`''s parser\n  tolerated it; the site''s did not.\n- The developer-tools chunk a shell lazily imports was named `dist-*.js`,\n  because the package''s build entry was `index`. Naming the entry `devtools`\n  makes it `devtools-*.js` for every shell, which is what belongs in a network\n  panel — and what the E2E identifies it by.\n- The fault-injection E2E reloaded the page to force a re-load, which builds a\n  new host and so clears the faults; and it navigated through the dashboard,\n  which mounts a widget from the remote it had just made unavailable. It now\n  navigates through the landing route, on the same host. Faults being per-host\n  and cleared by a reload is the right behaviour for a developer tool — you\n  cannot set one and forget it — so the documentation says so.\n\nVerified end to end: `pnpm check`, `pnpm build`, `pnpm build:apps` and\n`pnpm e2e` (27 tests, production and HMR projects) all pass.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQAeoilY8\n/s6yxda39FBkyqQXa6BnTkkRF5ncqdhKsuIHle63OHLuPigsfThFh9HbgGjT6OVPRddba2VGlb3i\njg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T13:34:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGQ5ZGE4OGJiMTA1OTU0M2EzYTEyOGNhMmQ0MjU1YzcyMWZkNTE3MDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3","sha":"18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3"}],"sha":"d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/d9da88bb1059543a3a128ca2d4255c721fd51701"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:51:09Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:51:09Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: finish the sweep — auth troubleshooting, chrome framing, scaffold tsconfig\n\n- `troubleshooting` gains the `AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` / `AUTH_FAILED` rows and two entries: the\n  three causes of an unavailable credential port, and why a cross-origin call is refused.\n- `failure-handling`, `examples` and `platform-context` describe the outlet renderers and the\n  notification host as what they now are — a shell''s own components over a platform port,\n  with the conformance shell as the reference implementation.\n- The scaffold''s tsconfig no longer includes the `e2e` and `playwright.config.ts` paths that\n  went with the harness.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"48749d19ab94f8c55bdc312307f6b872a2cdbe15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/48749d19ab94f8c55bdc312307f6b872a2cdbe15"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3","verification":{"payload":"tree 48749d19ab94f8c55bdc312307f6b872a2cdbe15\nparent b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789462269 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789462269 +0000\n\ndocs: finish the sweep — auth troubleshooting, chrome framing, scaffold tsconfig\n\n- `troubleshooting` gains the `AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` / `AUTH_FAILED` rows and two entries: the\n  three causes of an unavailable credential port, and why a cross-origin call is refused.\n- `failure-handling`, `examples` and `platform-context` describe the outlet renderers and the\n  notification host as what they now are — a shell''s own components over a platform port,\n  with the conformance shell as the reference implementation.\n- The scaffold''s tsconfig no longer includes the `e2e` and `playwright.config.ts` paths that\n  went with the harness.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJoF0662\nE2fHTbYUT0UPMZvp2+4G1qFW7KH8yFOKmNNJbEDf2iW7iqfTN2sI9h9nWqQpykp5or6onvc6csxK\nXAA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T08:51:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDE4MjgyZWRiZmFkZWYyMjJmMTFjZTcyMDllNWNiYWIyMzAwZGZmYzM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9","sha":"b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9"}],"sha":"18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/18282edbfadef222f11ce7209e5cbab2300dffc3"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:47:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:47:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"docs: describe the platform as it now is\n\nThe design contract, the README, AGENTS.md, the package descriptions, the llm.txt / llms.txt\ngenerator and the documentation site all still described a host that shipped the chrome, a\nharness that no longer exists and an SDK under its old name.\n\n- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`: the package table gains `@platform/host-react` and\n  `@platform/devtools` and loses `internal/devtools`; the host section says the package has no\n  peer dependencies and lists the headless API a shell builds its own UI on; \"Local development\n  modes\" becomes one loop, the manifest override; the bridge contract and the SDK surface gain\n  the credential port.\n- Two new reference pages, `@platform/host-react` and `@platform/devtools`, and\n  `reference/platform-react` is now `reference/mfe-react`.\n- `local-development` is rewritten around the override loop rather than the harness, and says\n  plainly that a deployed development shell is how you iterate with real authentication.\n- `developer-tools` explains that the shell supplies the loader, and documents the Faults panel.\n- The four chrome pages — command palette, help, release notes, breadcrumbs — are reframed\n  around the headless API plus a reference implementation to copy, rather than a component the\n  platform ships.\n\n`pnpm docs:generate` output and the JSON Schemas are regenerated: the `auth` capability and the\n`AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` / `AUTH_FAILED` codes appear in them, and `docs:check` passes over 71 pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"e968b4584207959106f8e9b69da8f6f9672ce4d2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/e968b4584207959106f8e9b69da8f6f9672ce4d2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9","verification":{"payload":"tree e968b4584207959106f8e9b69da8f6f9672ce4d2\nparent 19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789462039 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789462039 +0000\n\ndocs: describe the platform as it now is\n\nThe design contract, the README, AGENTS.md, the package descriptions, the llm.txt / llms.txt\ngenerator and the documentation site all still described a host that shipped the chrome, a\nharness that no longer exists and an SDK under its old name.\n\n- `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`: the package table gains `@platform/host-react` and\n  `@platform/devtools` and loses `internal/devtools`; the host section says the package has no\n  peer dependencies and lists the headless API a shell builds its own UI on; \"Local development\n  modes\" becomes one loop, the manifest override; the bridge contract and the SDK surface gain\n  the credential port.\n- Two new reference pages, `@platform/host-react` and `@platform/devtools`, and\n  `reference/platform-react` is now `reference/mfe-react`.\n- `local-development` is rewritten around the override loop rather than the harness, and says\n  plainly that a deployed development shell is how you iterate with real authentication.\n- `developer-tools` explains that the shell supplies the loader, and documents the Faults panel.\n- The four chrome pages — command palette, help, release notes, breadcrumbs — are reframed\n  around the headless API plus a reference implementation to copy, rather than a component the\n  platform ships.\n\n`pnpm docs:generate` output and the JSON Schemas are regenerated: the `auth` capability and the\n`AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` / `AUTH_FAILED` codes appear in them, and `docs:check` passes over 71 pages.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOaPWmrx\nL+Qa4k0/+Tkq/zmlK3VD9mgN7IZF0nvarPg3JS4PJifDZXiSnNITD5YqSfgH1C1DMemIdgXMWXay\nvAM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T08:51:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGIyZDI1OGU4NDI4MmU4OTBmNmQ1MDUwOGQyOTlhM2FjMTIxMzQ0ZTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a","sha":"19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a"}],"sha":"b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/b2d258e84282e890f6d50508d299a3ac121344e9"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:32:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:32:54Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(devtools): add the failure lab as a panel, working against a live shell\n\nFault injection was the one harness capability with no replacement, and as a\ndeveloper-tools panel it works in any shell rather than only in the harness.\n\n`@platform/host` gains a fault store the loader, the preflight and the\ncapability approval read:\n\n- `unavailable` — the load fails with `REMOTE_LOAD_FAILED`\n- `incompatibleShared` — every shared request is pinned to `^99.0.0`\n- `denyGroups` — the coarse preflight denies every remote that requires a group\n- `droppedCapabilities` — the named capabilities never reach the bridge\n\n`host.remotes.setFault()` is gated on `decideDevtools`, the same gate the tools\nthemselves pass, so production cannot reach it even by calling it; setting a\nfault drops cached definitions so the next load takes the faulted path. The\nloader wrapper is always installed and always delegates, so with no faults set\nit is a pass-through, and `host.loader` still returns the loader the shell\npassed in, extra API and all.\n\nThe panel''s fifth fault, a 404ing manifest, needs no host support: it is\n`setLocalOverride` pointed at a URL that does not resolve.\n\n`DevtoolsFaults` on the `DevtoolsHost` port is structural like the rest of it,\nso a shell that cannot inject faults simply omits `setFault` and the panel says\nso instead of rendering dead switches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"7e301f6ebb4c95c122d2d26f8592e7177ffe2459","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/7e301f6ebb4c95c122d2d26f8592e7177ffe2459"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a","verification":{"payload":"tree 7e301f6ebb4c95c122d2d26f8592e7177ffe2459\nparent c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789461174 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789461174 +0000\n\nfeat(devtools): add the failure lab as a panel, working against a live shell\n\nFault injection was the one harness capability with no replacement, and as a\ndeveloper-tools panel it works in any shell rather than only in the harness.\n\n`@platform/host` gains a fault store the loader, the preflight and the\ncapability approval read:\n\n- `unavailable` — the load fails with `REMOTE_LOAD_FAILED`\n- `incompatibleShared` — every shared request is pinned to `^99.0.0`\n- `denyGroups` — the coarse preflight denies every remote that requires a group\n- `droppedCapabilities` — the named capabilities never reach the bridge\n\n`host.remotes.setFault()` is gated on `decideDevtools`, the same gate the tools\nthemselves pass, so production cannot reach it even by calling it; setting a\nfault drops cached definitions so the next load takes the faulted path. The\nloader wrapper is always installed and always delegates, so with no faults set\nit is a pass-through, and `host.loader` still returns the loader the shell\npassed in, extra API and all.\n\nThe panel''s fifth fault, a 404ing manifest, needs no host support: it is\n`setLocalOverride` pointed at a URL that does not resolve.\n\n`DevtoolsFaults` on the `DevtoolsHost` port is structural like the rest of it,\nso a shell that cannot inject faults simply omits `setFault` and the panel says\nso instead of rendering dead switches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOtW0wns\n//76nIJO6Pu5jHzF2cud4OJsZkzeVPbTNqM999PVis+FQtm4XoNPbUhLIMKIWG5J6Sp8uOA314vn\nOAM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T08:32:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDE5Y2RiMzQ3OGM4ODFkODIxNTQ4YTMzNzYwOGI0YzkyMzQ2YmM2NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543","sha":"c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543"}],"sha":"19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/19cdb3478c881d821548a337608b4c92346bc65a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:25:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:25:24Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(cli): stop the scaffold teaching silent-wrong-data\n\n`templates/mfe/src/lib/api.ts` returned `SAMPLE_ASSETS` on every non-ok response\nand every non-abort error, so a 401 rendered three plausible-looking pumps\ninstead of failing. The official template was teaching a pattern that hides\noutages and authorization bugs behind data that looks real.\n\n`getJson` now checks `response.ok`, throws a `PlatformError`, and lets the\nroute''s `errorComponent` render it; the assets list gained the error and\npending components it was missing. The sample data existed to keep the harness\nworking without a backend and has no reason left to exist, so the widget takes\nits fields from props like every other widget rather than looking them up in a\nfixture.\n\nEvery call goes through the platform fetch, which needed a loader-side form:\n`context.platform.fetch` on the route context, built from the same\n`createPlatformFetch` that backs `usePlatformFetch()`. Loaders are not\ncomponents, and loading data from an authenticated backend is exactly what they\nare for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"3c166d5cfbe37535531bd26c5863e4bfa70aa523","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/3c166d5cfbe37535531bd26c5863e4bfa70aa523"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543","verification":{"payload":"tree 3c166d5cfbe37535531bd26c5863e4bfa70aa523\nparent e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789460724 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789460724 +0000\n\nfix(cli): stop the scaffold teaching silent-wrong-data\n\n`templates/mfe/src/lib/api.ts` returned `SAMPLE_ASSETS` on every non-ok response\nand every non-abort error, so a 401 rendered three plausible-looking pumps\ninstead of failing. The official template was teaching a pattern that hides\noutages and authorization bugs behind data that looks real.\n\n`getJson` now checks `response.ok`, throws a `PlatformError`, and lets the\nroute''s `errorComponent` render it; the assets list gained the error and\npending components it was missing. The sample data existed to keep the harness\nworking without a backend and has no reason left to exist, so the widget takes\nits fields from props like every other widget rather than looking them up in a\nfixture.\n\nEvery call goes through the platform fetch, which needed a loader-side form:\n`context.platform.fetch` on the route context, built from the same\n`createPlatformFetch` that backs `usePlatformFetch()`. Loaders are not\ncomponents, and loading data from an authenticated backend is exactly what they\nare for.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQBTVOWqh\nwLHXJs1kHQCH+DHcNnw+wNTQTU0WHeGKT4NaYFZ96mnTAfFbqnfvMyxv9jb3tIXNAfEm02WPn/m6\nLQ0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T08:32:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGM5YWY1YjMxNjVjNTdlYmI4M2Q2YmViNGU1NDAyYjllMDViMzY1NDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011","sha":"e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011"}],"sha":"c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/c9af5b3165c57ebb83d6beb4e5402b9e05b36543"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:17:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:17:10Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"feat(auth): add a credential port so an MFE can call an authenticated backend\n\nThe platform had no way for a remote to authenticate. There were fourteen\ncapabilities and none for auth, `HostBridge` carried no token, and the runtime\nconfiguration correctly refuses to carry one (`SENSITIVE_KEY_PATTERNS` rejects\n/TOKEN/i and /CREDENTIAL/i). The documentation says three times that permission\ngroups are UX-only and the backend is authoritative, but never said how the MFE\nreaches that backend. Teams were left to read cookies, reach into shell globals,\nbundle a second auth library — breaking the single session — or monkeypatch\n`fetch`, which rule 2 forbids.\n\nThe port is shaped like the ones that already work — `TelemetryAdapter`,\n`NotificationPort`, `StorageBackend`: the shell implements `CredentialAdapter`\nagainst its identity provider, and no SDK ever imports a vendor library.\n\n- `internal/core`: `CredentialAdapter`, `CredentialPort` and\n  `deniedCredentialPort`, `credentials` on `HostBridge`, the `auth` capability\n  (mapped from `useCredentials` / `usePlatformFetch`, so the Vite plugin infers\n  it with no extra work), and `AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` / `AUTH_FAILED`.\n- `@platform/host`: `credentials` on the host options and\n  `policy.credentialOrigins`. The bridge always carries a port, never\n  `undefined` — a remote without the capability, or a shell without an adapter,\n  gets one that rejects and names which of the two it is, so there is no silent\n  unauthenticated path to fall into.\n- `@platform/mfe-react`: `useCredentials()` and `usePlatformFetch()`, plus a\n  credential port in `createTestBridge`.\n\n`usePlatformFetch` attaches `Authorization: Bearer`, retries a 401 exactly once\nwith `forceRefresh`, and returns every other status to the caller untouched —\nit never decides what a 404 means. It also refuses to send a token to any origin\nbut the shell''s own and the ones the shell allow-listed: a token-attaching fetch\nwith no origin check is a credential-leak primitive. A refusal is recorded in\ndiagnostics and raised as `AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` before the request is made.\n\nCovered by unit tests on both sides of the bridge, a stub adapter and two\nbuttons in the conformance shell and asset tracker, and an E2E that asserts the\nheader is attached same-origin and that a cross-origin request is never sent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"5609eaf3606ac39e6135c71e3c27b3b463878c4d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/5609eaf3606ac39e6135c71e3c27b3b463878c4d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011","verification":{"payload":"tree 5609eaf3606ac39e6135c71e3c27b3b463878c4d\nparent 332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789460230 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789460230 +0000\n\nfeat(auth): add a credential port so an MFE can call an authenticated backend\n\nThe platform had no way for a remote to authenticate. There were fourteen\ncapabilities and none for auth, `HostBridge` carried no token, and the runtime\nconfiguration correctly refuses to carry one (`SENSITIVE_KEY_PATTERNS` rejects\n/TOKEN/i and /CREDENTIAL/i). The documentation says three times that permission\ngroups are UX-only and the backend is authoritative, but never said how the MFE\nreaches that backend. Teams were left to read cookies, reach into shell globals,\nbundle a second auth library — breaking the single session — or monkeypatch\n`fetch`, which rule 2 forbids.\n\nThe port is shaped like the ones that already work — `TelemetryAdapter`,\n`NotificationPort`, `StorageBackend`: the shell implements `CredentialAdapter`\nagainst its identity provider, and no SDK ever imports a vendor library.\n\n- `internal/core`: `CredentialAdapter`, `CredentialPort` and\n  `deniedCredentialPort`, `credentials` on `HostBridge`, the `auth` capability\n  (mapped from `useCredentials` / `usePlatformFetch`, so the Vite plugin infers\n  it with no extra work), and `AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` / `AUTH_FAILED`.\n- `@platform/host`: `credentials` on the host options and\n  `policy.credentialOrigins`. The bridge always carries a port, never\n  `undefined` — a remote without the capability, or a shell without an adapter,\n  gets one that rejects and names which of the two it is, so there is no silent\n  unauthenticated path to fall into.\n- `@platform/mfe-react`: `useCredentials()` and `usePlatformFetch()`, plus a\n  credential port in `createTestBridge`.\n\n`usePlatformFetch` attaches `Authorization: Bearer`, retries a 401 exactly once\nwith `forceRefresh`, and returns every other status to the caller untouched —\nit never decides what a 404 means. It also refuses to send a token to any origin\nbut the shell''s own and the ones the shell allow-listed: a token-attaching fetch\nwith no origin check is a credential-leak primitive. A refusal is recorded in\ndiagnostics and raised as `AUTH_UNAVAILABLE` before the request is made.\n\nCovered by unit tests on both sides of the bridge, a stub adapter and two\nbuttons in the conformance shell and asset tracker, and an E2E that asserts the\nheader is attached same-origin and that a cross-origin request is never sent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCj1kPyH\nwd5YA4HIdLUGOo67Dgx81sp2XBPtuychv2vMLz2QSg4rWE5djwZcnW4F/wgYoImofW/VigDlpHm+\nIQs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T08:17:13Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGU2ZmRlMWM2MDVhZGYzOTFmMjU3NzVjOGVhZWZmOTc2YjFmNWIwMTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb","sha":"332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb"}],"sha":"e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/e6fde1c605adf391f25775c8eaeff976b1f5b011"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:02:18Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T08:02:18Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(sdk): rename @platform/react to @platform/mfe-react\n\n`@platform/react` and `@platform/host-react` read as siblings when they sit on\nopposite sides of the boundary: one is what a remote imports, the other is what\na shell imports. The name now says which.\n\nThe code is unchanged. The sites that are not a plain find-and-replace:\n`REACT_BOUND_PACKAGES`, `PER_REMOTE_PACKAGES` and `SDK_SUBPATHS` in\n`internal/core/src/shared-deps.ts`, where a wrong entry would make remotes share\nan SDK copy they must not; `PLATFORM_PACKAGES` in the ESLint utilities; and the\n`withTecton` import written into the generated `.platform/entry.tsx`.\n\n`no-direct-mfe-import` flags `@scope/mfe-*` as another MFE''s source, which the\nSDK''s new name matches, so it now exempts platform sources first.\n\nTwo defects fixed along the way:\n\n- `platform validate` demanded `@tanstack/react-router` from every project,\n  including widget libraries that have no routes at all. It is required only\n  when `src/routes` exists; a widget-only fixture covers it.\n- `mount.completed` reported `routerVersion: \"@tanstack/react-router\"` — a\n  package name in a field typed as a version. A remote cannot read the router''s\n  version at runtime, so the SDK no longer claims to: the host resolves the real\n  one from the shared report and the manifest, which is what the developer tools\n  already displayed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"efa8ecadf6a08c23b8dce2404ba1ed14eb347de1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/efa8ecadf6a08c23b8dce2404ba1ed14eb347de1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb","verification":{"payload":"tree efa8ecadf6a08c23b8dce2404ba1ed14eb347de1\nparent adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789459338 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789459338 +0000\n\nrefactor(sdk): rename @platform/react to @platform/mfe-react\n\n`@platform/react` and `@platform/host-react` read as siblings when they sit on\nopposite sides of the boundary: one is what a remote imports, the other is what\na shell imports. The name now says which.\n\nThe code is unchanged. The sites that are not a plain find-and-replace:\n`REACT_BOUND_PACKAGES`, `PER_REMOTE_PACKAGES` and `SDK_SUBPATHS` in\n`internal/core/src/shared-deps.ts`, where a wrong entry would make remotes share\nan SDK copy they must not; `PLATFORM_PACKAGES` in the ESLint utilities; and the\n`withTecton` import written into the generated `.platform/entry.tsx`.\n\n`no-direct-mfe-import` flags `@scope/mfe-*` as another MFE''s source, which the\nSDK''s new name matches, so it now exempts platform sources first.\n\nTwo defects fixed along the way:\n\n- `platform validate` demanded `@tanstack/react-router` from every project,\n  including widget libraries that have no routes at all. It is required only\n  when `src/routes` exists; a widget-only fixture covers it.\n- `mount.completed` reported `routerVersion: \"@tanstack/react-router\"` — a\n  package name in a field typed as a version. A remote cannot read the router''s\n  version at runtime, so the SDK no longer claims to: the host resolves the real\n  one from the shared report and the manifest, which is what the developer tools\n  already displayed.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQOM5zhpn\nRx2uZh/IDCqZ5n8LJ98IIjxYVyqjvX0w6exe9oKUz/HNb7+yKaT9NEiFV9Ojt4ehiYrXGqbvdNW8\nrgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T08:02:21Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDMzMmYxNzgzODYxMWY2NzU4ZTAzODJmMzU0ZjJhYTU4NmZiN2JhZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8","sha":"adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8"}],"sha":"332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/332f17838611f6758e0382f354f2aa586fb7baeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:55:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:55:03Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(host): split the React bindings out and give the chrome to the shell\n\n`@platform/host` declared eight non-optional peer dependencies — react,\nreact-dom, @tanstack/react-router, @tecton/react, react-aria-components,\nlucide-react, cn and sonner — so a shell could not adopt the runtime without\nadopting the whole UI stack. Peer declarations are package-wide, so no\narrangement of subpath exports fixes that; the files had to leave.\n\nThree destinations:\n\n- `@platform/host-react` (new) gets `PlatformProvider` and the host hooks,\n  `MfeOutlet`, `WidgetSlot`, `SurfaceMount`, `outletStateFor` and the TanStack\n  bridge. This is platform API, not opinion: the mount lifecycle is ref timing,\n  dispose-on-unmount, StrictMode double-mounts and abort signals on in-flight\n  loads, and getting it subtly wrong looks like an MFE bug. It has no design\n  system, and it holds `@platform/host` as a peer rather than bundling it,\n  because a shell must have exactly one host runtime.\n- `apps/conformance-shell/src/components/` gets the command palette, the\n  settings host, breadcrumbs, the app finder, notifications, the overlay\n  provider, the help and release-note surfaces and the developer-tools toggle,\n  with their stylesheet. They were already built on the headless API the host\n  exports, so they moved unchanged: a real shell copies them and restyles them\n  rather than depending on them.\n- `@platform/host` keeps the runtime, and now declares no peer dependencies\n  at all.\n\nThe outlet needs to say something while it loads or fails even in a shell with\nno design system, so it renders a structural fallback built from the\n`platform-*` classes. A shell replaces it once for every outlet with\n`PlatformProvider`''s `renderLoading` / `renderError`, or per outlet with the\nexisting `fallback` / `errorFallback`; the conformance shell passes its Tecton\nversions, which is what the E2E suite exercises.\n\nThe fixtures behind the host''s own tests become `@platform/host/testing`, so a\nshell can unit-test its chrome against an in-memory host — which is how the\nchrome''s tests now run in `apps/conformance-shell`.\n\n`test/integration/package-boundaries.test.ts` enforces all of it: every rule is\non, none skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"de59b7f25669a77eb787c3551ec76461abd6e531","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/de59b7f25669a77eb787c3551ec76461abd6e531"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8","verification":{"payload":"tree de59b7f25669a77eb787c3551ec76461abd6e531\nparent 8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789458903 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789458903 +0000\n\nrefactor(host): split the React bindings out and give the chrome to the shell\n\n`@platform/host` declared eight non-optional peer dependencies — react,\nreact-dom, @tanstack/react-router, @tecton/react, react-aria-components,\nlucide-react, cn and sonner — so a shell could not adopt the runtime without\nadopting the whole UI stack. Peer declarations are package-wide, so no\narrangement of subpath exports fixes that; the files had to leave.\n\nThree destinations:\n\n- `@platform/host-react` (new) gets `PlatformProvider` and the host hooks,\n  `MfeOutlet`, `WidgetSlot`, `SurfaceMount`, `outletStateFor` and the TanStack\n  bridge. This is platform API, not opinion: the mount lifecycle is ref timing,\n  dispose-on-unmount, StrictMode double-mounts and abort signals on in-flight\n  loads, and getting it subtly wrong looks like an MFE bug. It has no design\n  system, and it holds `@platform/host` as a peer rather than bundling it,\n  because a shell must have exactly one host runtime.\n- `apps/conformance-shell/src/components/` gets the command palette, the\n  settings host, breadcrumbs, the app finder, notifications, the overlay\n  provider, the help and release-note surfaces and the developer-tools toggle,\n  with their stylesheet. They were already built on the headless API the host\n  exports, so they moved unchanged: a real shell copies them and restyles them\n  rather than depending on them.\n- `@platform/host` keeps the runtime, and now declares no peer dependencies\n  at all.\n\nThe outlet needs to say something while it loads or fails even in a shell with\nno design system, so it renders a structural fallback built from the\n`platform-*` classes. A shell replaces it once for every outlet with\n`PlatformProvider`''s `renderLoading` / `renderError`, or per outlet with the\nexisting `fallback` / `errorFallback`; the conformance shell passes its Tecton\nversions, which is what the E2E suite exercises.\n\nThe fixtures behind the host''s own tests become `@platform/host/testing`, so a\nshell can unit-test its chrome against an in-memory host — which is how the\nchrome''s tests now run in `apps/conformance-shell`.\n\n`test/integration/package-boundaries.test.ts` enforces all of it: every rule is\non, none skipped.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMO4i+8D\n3bOTnXz8rJZP75ohe/ft8J8e1BEhd7b4x6x7UnRORIo4iOxD6EJNiz88d6Y7k8ebxPNTYMkT0zZw\nIAs=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T07:55:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGFkZmQ4M2U4NWRkZDhkZGYxMGRjNDMxNGUyNzg4YmU5M2M5MzgwZTg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd","sha":"8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd"}],"sha":"adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/adfd83e85ddd8ddf10dc4314e2788be93c9380e8"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:38:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:38:41Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor(devtools): make the developer tools a package the shell loads\n\n`@platform-internal/devtools` was bundled into `@platform/host` behind a\nhardcoded `import(\"./devtools-entry\")`, so every shell carried React Flow, the\nwhole Tecton stack and the panel''s stylesheet in its dependency tree whether or\nnot it ever opened the tools.\n\nThe tools are now `@platform/devtools` (still private and workspace-resolved)\nand the shell decides whether and how to load them:\n\n    devtools: { ...runtimeConfig.devtools, load: () => import(\"@platform/devtools\") }\n\n`loadDevtools()` calls that loader, once per host, and says so plainly when a\nshell enables the tools without supplying one. `DevtoolsModule` is now a\nstructural interface described in the host''s own types, so `@platform/host`\nnames no UI package at all; the policy — `decideDevtools`, `shouldLoadDevtools`,\nthe flag helpers and the zod `devtools` schema — is unchanged, and `load` is a\nfunction, so it stays out of the serialisable runtime configuration.\n\nThe `.platform-devtools-*` rules move to `@platform/devtools/styles.css`, and\nthe internal packages move to devDependencies, since tsdown inlines them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"384ac43b225e849bffd488e7066fd864d2b5c0ed","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/384ac43b225e849bffd488e7066fd864d2b5c0ed"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd","verification":{"payload":"tree 384ac43b225e849bffd488e7066fd864d2b5c0ed\nparent 584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789457921 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789457921 +0000\n\nrefactor(devtools): make the developer tools a package the shell loads\n\n`@platform-internal/devtools` was bundled into `@platform/host` behind a\nhardcoded `import(\"./devtools-entry\")`, so every shell carried React Flow, the\nwhole Tecton stack and the panel''s stylesheet in its dependency tree whether or\nnot it ever opened the tools.\n\nThe tools are now `@platform/devtools` (still private and workspace-resolved)\nand the shell decides whether and how to load them:\n\n    devtools: { ...runtimeConfig.devtools, load: () => import(\"@platform/devtools\") }\n\n`loadDevtools()` calls that loader, once per host, and says so plainly when a\nshell enables the tools without supplying one. `DevtoolsModule` is now a\nstructural interface described in the host''s own types, so `@platform/host`\nnames no UI package at all; the policy — `decideDevtools`, `shouldLoadDevtools`,\nthe flag helpers and the zod `devtools` schema — is unchanged, and `load` is a\nfunction, so it stays out of the serialisable runtime configuration.\n\nThe `.platform-devtools-*` rules move to `@platform/devtools/styles.css`, and\nthe internal packages move to devDependencies, since tsdown inlines them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQP+zqnyg\nCh2PzVMYb/zCWcW0MIHuorT/J6GYS6Yz4RExqfvQo40dGVO3tZU2Cd6+9zB9Sv/syK7nU/HxpTA7\nhw0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T07:55:07Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDhkZjdlNzY4ZThiZDNlMjNiODg2Y2UxOGNlZWQzOThhMTdhNjVmZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89","sha":"584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89"}],"sha":"8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/8df7e768e8bd3e23b886ce18ceed398a17a65fdd"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:31:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:31:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"refactor: remove the local shell harness\n\nThe harness was a 1,250-line Tecton application inside `@platform/host`, and\nthe reason the host package carried React, TanStack Router, Tecton, react-aria,\nlucide, cn and sonner at all. Its four jobs are covered elsewhere:\n\n- Inner dev loop: point a shell at `http://localhost:<port>/platform-manifest.json`\n  with `?platform.override.<mfeId>=`, the manifest-override entry in local\n  storage, or the developer tools override control. The dev manifest already\n  carries `dev.hmr` and `dev.refreshPreamble`, so React Refresh is installed per\n  remote React instance — full HMR, and against a deployed development shell it\n  works with real authentication, which the harness never could.\n- Scaffold end-to-end tests: they belong with the apps and the shell, not in\n  every generated project.\n- Failure injection: moves to a developer-tools panel, where it works in any\n  shell rather than only in the harness.\n\nScaffolded MFEs no longer dev-depend on `@platform/host`, which is what forced\na React 19 peer onto React 18 projects.\n\n`platform dev` and the Vite plugin now serve the development manifest and the\nrefresh preamble only; `hostKind: \"harness\"` stays, because it is part of the\nbridge protocol rather than part of the harness.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"faa95d48d1a57e03fe5f8048597daa9049a607fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/faa95d48d1a57e03fe5f8048597daa9049a607fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89","verification":{"payload":"tree faa95d48d1a57e03fe5f8048597daa9049a607fd\nparent 43daa784a62bb5f1c7d8a81cf37cab7510a542d7\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789457473 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789457473 +0000\n\nrefactor: remove the local shell harness\n\nThe harness was a 1,250-line Tecton application inside `@platform/host`, and\nthe reason the host package carried React, TanStack Router, Tecton, react-aria,\nlucide, cn and sonner at all. Its four jobs are covered elsewhere:\n\n- Inner dev loop: point a shell at `http://localhost:<port>/platform-manifest.json`\n  with `?platform.override.<mfeId>=`, the manifest-override entry in local\n  storage, or the developer tools override control. The dev manifest already\n  carries `dev.hmr` and `dev.refreshPreamble`, so React Refresh is installed per\n  remote React instance — full HMR, and against a deployed development shell it\n  works with real authentication, which the harness never could.\n- Scaffold end-to-end tests: they belong with the apps and the shell, not in\n  every generated project.\n- Failure injection: moves to a developer-tools panel, where it works in any\n  shell rather than only in the harness.\n\nScaffolded MFEs no longer dev-depend on `@platform/host`, which is what forced\na React 19 peer onto React 18 projects.\n\n`platform dev` and the Vite plugin now serve the development manifest and the\nrefresh preamble only; `hostKind: \"harness\"` stays, because it is part of the\nbridge protocol rather than part of the harness.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQIG3TMiw\nKKfwnFNxisoJb18E/ESybj92FC6rqt9BhJfoUle54Mh6upHV9VUqND9DGIgLHQmkV5JAzy7DCmlE\nWAk=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T07:31:25Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDU4NGVhNDQ0ZTM5YjgyNDBhZmEzMTYwZDVlNWM0MDFmZjFiMDlkODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/43daa784a62bb5f1c7d8a81cf37cab7510a542d7","sha":"43daa784a62bb5f1c7d8a81cf37cab7510a542d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/43daa784a62bb5f1c7d8a81cf37cab7510a542d7"}],"sha":"584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/584ea444e39b8240afa3160d5e5c401ff1b09d89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/43daa784a62bb5f1c7d8a81cf37cab7510a542d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:20:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T07:20:15Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"test(integration): assert the packages that must stay framework-neutral\n\nThe platform ships adapters for React, TanStack Router and Tecton; it does\nnot depend on them. That only stays true if it is checked, because a single\nimport or a stray peer dependency quietly undoes it.\n\nTwo checks: an allow-list of each package''s dependencies and peer\ndependencies, so adding one is a deliberate edit to this file, and a source\nscan for framework imports in the packages that must not carry them.\n\n`@platform/host` and `@platform/host-react` are listed with their target\nshape but skipped behind a TODO naming the step that reaches them; the list\nis the definition of done for the decoupling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi","tree":{"sha":"0c387c4e11c23779ccfc450589e3816de54c6ad7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/0c387c4e11c23779ccfc450589e3816de54c6ad7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/43daa784a62bb5f1c7d8a81cf37cab7510a542d7","verification":{"payload":"tree 0c387c4e11c23779ccfc450589e3816de54c6ad7\nparent 7dd0d9ba4399eb9c1528cf4ea49acbb3b8d5fa1e\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789456815 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789456815 +0000\n\ntest(integration): assert the packages that must stay framework-neutral\n\nThe platform ships adapters for React, TanStack Router and Tecton; it does\nnot depend on them. That only stays true if it is checked, because a single\nimport or a stray peer dependency quietly undoes it.\n\nTwo checks: an allow-list of each package''s dependencies and peer\ndependencies, so adding one is a deliberate edit to this file, and a source\nscan for framework imports in the packages that must not carry them.\n\n`@platform/host` and `@platform/host-react` are listed with their target\nshape but skipped behind a TODO naming the step that reaches them; the list\nis the definition of done for the decoupling.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017DM6mHLcWaBpbFuUKdcsWi\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGwF8NCl\nniLxvr0IeMgSleTkYIza3Xewr89k60vWjvDbpbljBI+FKs8kzWmHCWMcTDlLuGFoTGACzM