d32101b7742"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c","sha":"f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c"}],"sha":"7dd0d9ba4399eb9c1528cf4ea49acbb3b8d5fa1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/7dd0d9ba4399eb9c1528cf4ea49acbb3b8d5fa1e"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T06:06:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T06:06:13Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(vite): stop warning about a widget command that labels itself at runtime\n\nEvery project made with `platform new` built with a warning it had nothing\nto fix:\n\n  [platform] src/widgets/asset-card.tsx: a command definition needs\n  literal `id` and `label` to be listed in the manifest.\n\nThe scaffold''s widget command is `id: \"open-asset\"` with\n``label: `Open ${title}` `` — the id is a literal, and the label reads\nfrom the widget''s props. That is the documented shape: the widget docs\nand the project-structure guide both teach it, and the conformance app\nuses it. So the platform was reporting its own happy path, and the\nmessage pointed at `id`, which was never the problem.\n\nA per-instance label cannot be known without running the code, but\nnothing is lost by leaving such a command out of the manifest: the\npalette only offers a manifest command that carries a `route`, because a\n`handler` cannot run before the remote loads (`search.ts` skips the\nrest), and a row has nothing to show without a label. The command\nregisters itself when the MFE mounts, which is when its label exists.\n\nSo a component-registered command whose label is not a literal is now\nordinary and silent. A static `createMfe({ registrations })` entry is\nmodule-scope data with no props in scope, so one that cannot state its\nlabel is still reported — and named: `the static command \"export-csv\"\nneeds a literal `label``. A non-literal `id` is still reported wherever\nit appears, since the command cannot be identified at all.\n\nThe help, release-note and settings-field warnings named every field\nthey checked too. They now name only the ones that were not literals,\nand the entry''s id when it has one, so a warning points at the line to\nchange rather than at the whole definition.\n\n`platform create` now has the test that would have caught this: a\nscaffolded project''s sources analyse with no warnings at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"0208a21265d270d81f37ec68e321f97d2930b267","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/0208a21265d270d81f37ec68e321f97d2930b267"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c","verification":{"payload":"tree 0208a21265d270d81f37ec68e321f97d2930b267\nparent 704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789452373 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789452373 +0000\n\nfix(vite): stop warning about a widget command that labels itself at runtime\n\nEvery project made with `platform new` built with a warning it had nothing\nto fix:\n\n  [platform] src/widgets/asset-card.tsx: a command definition needs\n  literal `id` and `label` to be listed in the manifest.\n\nThe scaffold''s widget command is `id: \"open-asset\"` with\n``label: `Open ${title}` `` — the id is a literal, and the label reads\nfrom the widget''s props. That is the documented shape: the widget docs\nand the project-structure guide both teach it, and the conformance app\nuses it. So the platform was reporting its own happy path, and the\nmessage pointed at `id`, which was never the problem.\n\nA per-instance label cannot be known without running the code, but\nnothing is lost by leaving such a command out of the manifest: the\npalette only offers a manifest command that carries a `route`, because a\n`handler` cannot run before the remote loads (`search.ts` skips the\nrest), and a row has nothing to show without a label. The command\nregisters itself when the MFE mounts, which is when its label exists.\n\nSo a component-registered command whose label is not a literal is now\nordinary and silent. A static `createMfe({ registrations })` entry is\nmodule-scope data with no props in scope, so one that cannot state its\nlabel is still reported — and named: `the static command \"export-csv\"\nneeds a literal `label``. A non-literal `id` is still reported wherever\nit appears, since the command cannot be identified at all.\n\nThe help, release-note and settings-field warnings named every field\nthey checked too. They now name only the ones that were not literals,\nand the entry''s id when it has one, so a warning points at the line to\nchange rather than at the whole definition.\n\n`platform create` now has the test that would have caught this: a\nscaffolded project''s sources analyse with no warnings at all.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQF1XnGfQ\n7mbGiuWc/xuOxtPqstAl4r2+cnAH0gS3g5Q7KH4cnattn0SdBewCF9ICsCTmPvGaNi2voOEUUuuo\njgg=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T06:06:16Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGYzNTg2MDQwZTliMjMzYmUyOWIzOGE2MmZlN2M1NzZmNWE0NzkzMGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a","sha":"704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a"}],"sha":"f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/f3586040e9b233be29b38a62fe7c576f5a47930c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T05:37:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T05:37:53Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(host): report a failure to telemetry once, with the error that was thrown\n\nThe conformance shell''s console shows one failure three times:\n\n  [error] Error: The development server of asset-tracker needs a restart…\n      at forward (…/internal/diagnostics/src/bus.ts)\n  [error] Error: The development server of asset-tracker needs a restart…\n      at forward (…/internal/diagnostics/src/bus.ts)\n  [error] PlatformError: The development server of asset-tracker needs a restart…\n      at assertLoadable (…/packages/host/src/host.ts)\n\nThe conditions are deliberate — a conformance slot mounts an unknown\nwidget, and an e2e test edits `mfe.config.ts` to force a restart — but\none failure is one failure, and a shell that ships a vendor adapter was\nbilling three events for it.\n\nA failure leaves through three channels: the call site that catches it\nreports it with its boundary, it is emitted as a diagnostic and the bus\nforwards that to telemetry, and the span it failed inside fails with it\n(which falls back to `adapter.error` when the adapter has no\n`spanStart`). Nothing reconciled them, and `toPlatformError` returns an\nexisting `PlatformError` unchanged, so all three carried one instance.\n\nThe copies were also the worse ones. `new Error(event.error.message)`\nkept only the message: no code, no hint, no docs link, no cause, and a\nstack pointing at the forwarding helper — so in a vendor tool every\nforwarded error in the platform groups under `forward`, whatever failed.\n\n`createTelemetry` now reports an error instance once, over the whole\ntree (a remote''s bridge telemetry is a child of the shell''s), and the\ndiagnostics bus forwards the live error instead of rebuilding one:\ndiagnostics that carry a failure pass it as `errorInstance`, which is\nused for the report and never recorded. Only an event that arrived\nalready serialised is reconstructed, and then as a `PlatformError`, so\nthe code, hint and docs link survive. De-duplication is by identity, so\ntwo attempts that each throw stay two events, and a span given to an\nadapter that implements `spanStart` still fails through `handle.fail` —\na span outcome is not an error report.\n\nThe owning call sites report before they emit, so the surviving event is\nthe one that knows the boundary, and the five sites that did both are in\nthat order now. The error boundary reports the platform error rather\nthan the raw one, so it is the same instance as its diagnostic.\n\nDiagnostics are untouched: every event is still recorded, so devtools\nand `host.diagnostics.list()` still show each step. Across the e2e run\nthe shell''s console goes from five error lines to two, one per\ndeliberate failure, each with the stack from its throw site.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"49466f134ab70d76fd37d52cbd8c0f113baf7949","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/49466f134ab70d76fd37d52cbd8c0f113baf7949"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a","verification":{"payload":"tree 49466f134ab70d76fd37d52cbd8c0f113baf7949\nparent 70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789450673 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789450673 +0000\n\nfix(host): report a failure to telemetry once, with the error that was thrown\n\nThe conformance shell''s console shows one failure three times:\n\n  [error] Error: The development server of asset-tracker needs a restart…\n      at forward (…/internal/diagnostics/src/bus.ts)\n  [error] Error: The development server of asset-tracker needs a restart…\n      at forward (…/internal/diagnostics/src/bus.ts)\n  [error] PlatformError: The development server of asset-tracker needs a restart…\n      at assertLoadable (…/packages/host/src/host.ts)\n\nThe conditions are deliberate — a conformance slot mounts an unknown\nwidget, and an e2e test edits `mfe.config.ts` to force a restart — but\none failure is one failure, and a shell that ships a vendor adapter was\nbilling three events for it.\n\nA failure leaves through three channels: the call site that catches it\nreports it with its boundary, it is emitted as a diagnostic and the bus\nforwards that to telemetry, and the span it failed inside fails with it\n(which falls back to `adapter.error` when the adapter has no\n`spanStart`). Nothing reconciled them, and `toPlatformError` returns an\nexisting `PlatformError` unchanged, so all three carried one instance.\n\nThe copies were also the worse ones. `new Error(event.error.message)`\nkept only the message: no code, no hint, no docs link, no cause, and a\nstack pointing at the forwarding helper — so in a vendor tool every\nforwarded error in the platform groups under `forward`, whatever failed.\n\n`createTelemetry` now reports an error instance once, over the whole\ntree (a remote''s bridge telemetry is a child of the shell''s), and the\ndiagnostics bus forwards the live error instead of rebuilding one:\ndiagnostics that carry a failure pass it as `errorInstance`, which is\nused for the report and never recorded. Only an event that arrived\nalready serialised is reconstructed, and then as a `PlatformError`, so\nthe code, hint and docs link survive. De-duplication is by identity, so\ntwo attempts that each throw stay two events, and a span given to an\nadapter that implements `spanStart` still fails through `handle.fail` —\na span outcome is not an error report.\n\nThe owning call sites report before they emit, so the surviving event is\nthe one that knows the boundary, and the five sites that did both are in\nthat order now. The error boundary reports the platform error rather\nthan the raw one, so it is the same instance as its diagnostic.\n\nDiagnostics are untouched: every event is still recorded, so devtools\nand `host.diagnostics.list()` still show each step. Across the e2e run\nthe shell''s console goes from five error lines to two, one per\ndeliberate failure, each with the stack from its throw site.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQGt/dTJs\n5ap/jsGacoRSpHSg/4tu8ifBVzGWPF/JIf8dIzGhHs/jzMphe0wnVB/FvFe7iGXl7DEXyp61P9ZY\nuQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T05:38:23Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDcwNGZiMjA0NDNlMWRiZTc5OWM3NjNiNThiM2QxYjBiNjFhZjcyN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016","sha":"70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016"}],"sha":"704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/704fb20443e1dbe799c763b58b3d1b0b61af727a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T05:04:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T05:04:28Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(vite): match route files by module id on Windows too\n\nThis is the Windows HMR failure, and the browser log names it:\n\n  TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading ''useContext'')\n    at useContext (127.0.0.1:4301/node_modules/.vite/deps/react.js)\n    at useMountScope (…/packages/react/dist/provider-…js)\n    at RootLayout (127.0.0.1:4301/src/routes/__root.tsx:38)\n    at renderWithHooks (127.0.0.1:4110/node_modules/.vite/deps/react-dom_client.js)\n\nThe remote''s `RootLayout` is rendered by the *shell''s* react-dom while\nits hooks call into the *remote''s* React: two copies, so the dispatcher\nis null. That happens when the remote''s root route replaces the shell''s,\nwhich is what the router plugin''s HMR glue does when it is left pointing\nat `window.__TSR_ROUTER__` — every remote''s root route is also called\n`__root__`. Rewriting that lookup to the platform''s per-remote registry\nis what keeps the shell''s router intact, and the rewrite is applied only\nto files under the routes directory.\n\nThat test compared a Vite module id, which always uses forward slashes,\nagainst a path from `resolve`, which follows the platform. On Windows the\ntwo never matched, so no route file was ever rewritten and every remote\nhijacked the shell''s root route. Linux was unaffected, which is why this\nonly ever failed there.\n\nThe comparison now converts separators, and also requires a path\nboundary, so a sibling such as `src/routes-legacy` no longer counts as\ninside `src/routes`. It lives in `isRouteFile`, separate from `resolve`,\nso the Windows case is a unit test rather than something only Windows CI\ncan reach — `normalizePath` would not do, since Vite''s own version\nrewrites separators only when it is running on Windows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"12c06d4351f392140613fd9079f0fd7224506ba6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/12c06d4351f392140613fd9079f0fd7224506ba6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016","verification":{"payload":"tree 12c06d4351f392140613fd9079f0fd7224506ba6\nparent 36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789448668 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789448668 +0000\n\nfix(vite): match route files by module id on Windows too\n\nThis is the Windows HMR failure, and the browser log names it:\n\n  TypeError: Cannot read properties of null (reading ''useContext'')\n    at useContext (127.0.0.1:4301/node_modules/.vite/deps/react.js)\n    at useMountScope (…/packages/react/dist/provider-…js)\n    at RootLayout (127.0.0.1:4301/src/routes/__root.tsx:38)\n    at renderWithHooks (127.0.0.1:4110/node_modules/.vite/deps/react-dom_client.js)\n\nThe remote''s `RootLayout` is rendered by the *shell''s* react-dom while\nits hooks call into the *remote''s* React: two copies, so the dispatcher\nis null. That happens when the remote''s root route replaces the shell''s,\nwhich is what the router plugin''s HMR glue does when it is left pointing\nat `window.__TSR_ROUTER__` — every remote''s root route is also called\n`__root__`. Rewriting that lookup to the platform''s per-remote registry\nis what keeps the shell''s router intact, and the rewrite is applied only\nto files under the routes directory.\n\nThat test compared a Vite module id, which always uses forward slashes,\nagainst a path from `resolve`, which follows the platform. On Windows the\ntwo never matched, so no route file was ever rewritten and every remote\nhijacked the shell''s root route. Linux was unaffected, which is why this\nonly ever failed there.\n\nThe comparison now converts separators, and also requires a path\nboundary, so a sibling such as `src/routes-legacy` no longer counts as\ninside `src/routes`. It lives in `isRouteFile`, separate from `resolve`,\nso the Windows case is a unit test rather than something only Windows CI\ncan reach — `normalizePath` would not do, since Vite''s own version\nrewrites separators only when it is running on Windows.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQL9sv+hm\n1nsaEIl+gaX/6H5rwGMy6H58cZPLf6YBppIngcNnb2UvSD0GyVJKcBR7BPSlonB49y+Ja2SJD20m\nkgA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T05:04:34Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDcwZGE2ZTE0NWJkNmE2NjBhMzY1Nzg4MjkxZmIzNzRhODZhNjQwMTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837","sha":"36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837"}],"sha":"70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/70da6e145bd6a660a365788291fb374a86a64016"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T04:46:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T04:46:26Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"test(e2e): report what the shell rendered when a remote never mounts\n\nLinux is green. The one failure left is the HMR suite on Windows, where\n`asset-tracker` never mounts in the development shell: 21 production\ntests pass on the same runner, so mounting itself works there and this is\nspecific to development mode.\n\nThe failure carries no evidence. The assertion says only that the root\nlocator never appeared, and the forwarding added in the previous commit\nwrites to the test''s stdout, which the reporters used on CI do not\nreliably echo — no `[browser:…]` line reached the last log even though\nthe same listeners produce them locally.\n\nSo the evidence now travels in the error itself, which is printed:\nwaiting for a remote''s root goes through a helper that, on timeout,\nfails with the page URL, the text the shell actually rendered, and the\ntail of the browser log. Every console level is recorded, not just\nerrors, because the shell writes its diagnostics stream through the\nconsole — whether `mfe.mounted` arrives, and what the host reported\nbefore it, is what distinguishes a remote that failed from one that was\nnever asked to mount.\n\nVerified by pointing the helper at a locator that cannot exist: the\nfailure prints the shell''s rendered text and the telemetry tail,\nincluding the manifest request outcomes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"bbedc49b2ddc36d8dd8ef2dbeb490c83697a8e05","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/bbedc49b2ddc36d8dd8ef2dbeb490c83697a8e05"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837","verification":{"payload":"tree bbedc49b2ddc36d8dd8ef2dbeb490c83697a8e05\nparent 759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789447586 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789447586 +0000\n\ntest(e2e): report what the shell rendered when a remote never mounts\n\nLinux is green. The one failure left is the HMR suite on Windows, where\n`asset-tracker` never mounts in the development shell: 21 production\ntests pass on the same runner, so mounting itself works there and this is\nspecific to development mode.\n\nThe failure carries no evidence. The assertion says only that the root\nlocator never appeared, and the forwarding added in the previous commit\nwrites to the test''s stdout, which the reporters used on CI do not\nreliably echo — no `[browser:…]` line reached the last log even though\nthe same listeners produce them locally.\n\nSo the evidence now travels in the error itself, which is printed:\nwaiting for a remote''s root goes through a helper that, on timeout,\nfails with the page URL, the text the shell actually rendered, and the\ntail of the browser log. Every console level is recorded, not just\nerrors, because the shell writes its diagnostics stream through the\nconsole — whether `mfe.mounted` arrives, and what the host reported\nbefore it, is what distinguishes a remote that failed from one that was\nnever asked to mount.\n\nVerified by pointing the helper at a locator that cannot exist: the\nfailure prints the shell''s rendered text and the telemetry tail,\nincluding the manifest request outcomes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQJpMmqMB\n1HcjyDRzC6al8XKQPtNaIwg4yIcmLnqKTZqwZGWWA8Y9dgm0fo7vxq5VXAesldZDl7YQFUJxJJYo\n7g0=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T04:46:33Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDM2YmE2Y2VkMmNjZTA0ZGExZWZiYjc3NDhiOTZmOTgxMzY3M2U4Mzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d","sha":"759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d"}],"sha":"36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/36ba6ced2cce04da1efbb7748b96f9813673e837"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T04:24:49Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T04:25:08Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(vite): stop reporting widgets declared by record key as unanalysable\n\nClears the avoidable warnings from `pnpm build:apps` and `pnpm test` on\nboth platforms, and finds one real analyser bug on the way.\n\nEvery `createWidget` call inside `createMfe({ widgets })` was analysed\ntwice: once through `createMfe`, which takes the id from the record key\nand lists the widget, and again on its own, where the call has no literal\n`id` and was reported as \"not listed in the manifest\". The manifest was\nalways right — the warning contradicted it on the documented API shape,\non every build. Calls claimed by a `createMfe` are now skipped, and a\ncall with no literal id defers its warning until the file has been\nwalked, because a widget can be declared above the `createMfe` that names\nit. `apps/conformance-react18`''s manifest is unchanged.\n\n`@tanstack/react-router` reads `React[\"use\"]` through a dynamic lookup\nprecisely so React 18 keeps working, and rolldown reports the miss\nagainst the federation shared-module shim as `IMPORT_IS_UNDEFINED`. The\nvalue is meant to be `undefined` there, so remote builds drop\n`IMPORT_IS_UNDEFINED` raised against a `virtual:mf:…__loadShare__`\nmodule and nothing else; a user-supplied `onwarn` still sees everything.\n\nThe docs route preloads MDX bodies on client-side navigation, so the\nasync collection''s runtime ships to the browser, and its server-only\n\"raw file\" branch reaches for `node:fs/promises` behind a dynamic import\nthe browser never evaluates.\n\nIn the tests, the widget-error case throws on purpose and React reports\nthe error it caught through `console.error`; that expected report is now\nasserted and suppressed. The devtools panel coalesces host and\ndiagnostics events into a timer, so a pending refresh could land after a\nsynchronous test body had finished and warn about an update outside\n`act`; both panel tests now unmount inside `act`.\n\nTwo warnings stay, because both are true: `@property` rules really are\ndocument-global and escape CSS scoping, and the conformance command\nreally does build its label from runtime data, so it cannot be listed\nstatically.\n\nAlso carries diagnostics for the one CI failure left, the HMR suite on\nWindows, where the remote never mounts and nothing is logged: the spec\nnow forwards browser console errors, page errors and failed requests to\nstdout, and the Tecton pre-bundling scan says so instead of returning an\nempty list, which would break the remote in the browser with nothing in\nthe server output. The first mount gets longer on CI, where Windows runs\nroughly an order of magnitude slower than a development machine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"c9dfcdcf7fa0ca22528b82f63b5c94d76b7356a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/c9dfcdcf7fa0ca22528b82f63b5c94d76b7356a1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d","verification":{"payload":"tree c9dfcdcf7fa0ca22528b82f63b5c94d76b7356a1\nparent d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789446289 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789446308 +0000\n\nfix(vite): stop reporting widgets declared by record key as unanalysable\n\nClears the avoidable warnings from `pnpm build:apps` and `pnpm test` on\nboth platforms, and finds one real analyser bug on the way.\n\nEvery `createWidget` call inside `createMfe({ widgets })` was analysed\ntwice: once through `createMfe`, which takes the id from the record key\nand lists the widget, and again on its own, where the call has no literal\n`id` and was reported as \"not listed in the manifest\". The manifest was\nalways right — the warning contradicted it on the documented API shape,\non every build. Calls claimed by a `createMfe` are now skipped, and a\ncall with no literal id defers its warning until the file has been\nwalked, because a widget can be declared above the `createMfe` that names\nit. `apps/conformance-react18`''s manifest is unchanged.\n\n`@tanstack/react-router` reads `React[\"use\"]` through a dynamic lookup\nprecisely so React 18 keeps working, and rolldown reports the miss\nagainst the federation shared-module shim as `IMPORT_IS_UNDEFINED`. The\nvalue is meant to be `undefined` there, so remote builds drop\n`IMPORT_IS_UNDEFINED` raised against a `virtual:mf:…__loadShare__`\nmodule and nothing else; a user-supplied `onwarn` still sees everything.\n\nThe docs route preloads MDX bodies on client-side navigation, so the\nasync collection''s runtime ships to the browser, and its server-only\n\"raw file\" branch reaches for `node:fs/promises` behind a dynamic import\nthe browser never evaluates.\n\nIn the tests, the widget-error case throws on purpose and React reports\nthe error it caught through `console.error`; that expected report is now\nasserted and suppressed. The devtools panel coalesces host and\ndiagnostics events into a timer, so a pending refresh could land after a\nsynchronous test body had finished and warn about an update outside\n`act`; both panel tests now unmount inside `act`.\n\nTwo warnings stay, because both are true: `@property` rules really are\ndocument-global and escape CSS scoping, and the conformance command\nreally does build its label from runtime data, so it cannot be listed\nstatically.\n\nAlso carries diagnostics for the one CI failure left, the HMR suite on\nWindows, where the remote never mounts and nothing is logged: the spec\nnow forwards browser console errors, page errors and failed requests to\nstdout, and the Tecton pre-bundling scan says so instead of returning an\nempty list, which would break the remote in the browser with nothing in\nthe server output. The first mount gets longer on CI, where Windows runs\nroughly an order of magnitude slower than a development machine.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHeqelXg\nhhevL3WR3G6wG+nHfrbxuJnSsVL+DqCkNV3EpGZoWCZGmY/cNvwNnTYrCVpLK6raYb4PkEIom/Fe\nhQo=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T04:25:14Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDc1OWY5NzA2NjkwYTRkNjQ0OGI2ZDY2NDE4ZTc1M2QzOTI2M2ViOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6","sha":"d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6"}],"sha":"759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/759f9706690a4d6448b6d66418e753d39263eb9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:58:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:58:19Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(conformance): bind the development servers to IPv4\n\nThe Linux leg reached `pnpm e2e` for the first time. All 21 production\ntests passed; the HMR project failed both attempts with a bare\n`\"beforeAll\" hook timeout of 120000ms exceeded`.\n\nThe remotes did start — their banners are in the log — but nothing ever\nanswered the hook''s health checks. The banners say what went wrong:\n`Local: http://localhost:4301/`, unresolved. `conformanceEnv` addresses\nevery remote as 127.0.0.1 and the suites wait on the same host, while\nVite defaults `server.host` to `localhost` and leaves DNS order verbatim,\nso on a dual-stack runner it can bind ::1 alone and refuse every\n127.0.0.1 request. Everything that passed on that runner binds IPv4\nexplicitly: the static servers in `serveStatic` and the shell''s `vite\npreview`. The conformance servers now say so too, which also keeps\n`pnpm dev:conformance` and a manual `pnpm dev` consistent with the\nmanifest URLs they are addressed by. Locally the banner changes from\n`http://localhost:4201/` to `http://127.0.0.1:4201/`.\n\nThe hook''s own timeout hid this. Each `waitFor` allows 120 s and names\nthe URL and last connection error when it gives up, but the project\ntimeout was also 120 s, so Playwright always killed the hook first and\nreported nothing useful. The HMR project now allows 180 s, leaving the\nwait to fail first and say which server never came up.\n\n`pnpm e2e` passes end to end: 24 tests across both projects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"75bdb57089aaea302347832c1a84e1414934f434","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/75bdb57089aaea302347832c1a84e1414934f434"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6","verification":{"payload":"tree 75bdb57089aaea302347832c1a84e1414934f434\nparent 67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789444699 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789444699 +0000\n\nfix(conformance): bind the development servers to IPv4\n\nThe Linux leg reached `pnpm e2e` for the first time. All 21 production\ntests passed; the HMR project failed both attempts with a bare\n`\"beforeAll\" hook timeout of 120000ms exceeded`.\n\nThe remotes did start — their banners are in the log — but nothing ever\nanswered the hook''s health checks. The banners say what went wrong:\n`Local: http://localhost:4301/`, unresolved. `conformanceEnv` addresses\nevery remote as 127.0.0.1 and the suites wait on the same host, while\nVite defaults `server.host` to `localhost` and leaves DNS order verbatim,\nso on a dual-stack runner it can bind ::1 alone and refuse every\n127.0.0.1 request. Everything that passed on that runner binds IPv4\nexplicitly: the static servers in `serveStatic` and the shell''s `vite\npreview`. The conformance servers now say so too, which also keeps\n`pnpm dev:conformance` and a manual `pnpm dev` consistent with the\nmanifest URLs they are addressed by. Locally the banner changes from\n`http://localhost:4201/` to `http://127.0.0.1:4201/`.\n\nThe hook''s own timeout hid this. Each `waitFor` allows 120 s and names\nthe URL and last connection error when it gives up, but the project\ntimeout was also 120 s, so Playwright always killed the hook first and\nreported nothing useful. The HMR project now allows 180 s, leaving the\nwait to fail first and say which server never came up.\n\n`pnpm e2e` passes end to end: 24 tests across both projects.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMVsae9b\n4UUnep6ShVELJJ1pJvVoU0vs4qdnpMpRZ3FzBRLKbGWxKba9Lbpt+vbTekuet3/gDC3kJm2UwRwh\nmQA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T03:58:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKGQ0ZWI1OTUxZDhiOTdjNzQ0ZmZiMTBlNjNlYTVhNDM5MmQ1NjQ3YTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193","sha":"67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193"}],"sha":"d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/d4eb5951d8b97c744ffb10e63ea5a4392d5647a6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:50:56Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:50:56Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(cli): keep the router generator''s temporary files on one volume\n\nThe Windows leg reached `pnpm test` for the first time and failed two of\n528 tests; both were Windows-specific.\n\n`platform validate` regenerates the route tree in a copy of `src/routes`\nto compare it against the committed `routeTree.gen.ts`. The generator\nwrites each file to a temporary path and renames it into place, and its\ntemporary directory defaults to `.tanstack/tmp` resolved against\n`process.cwd()` — the repository — while the copy lives in the system\ntemp directory. On the Windows runner those are different volumes (D:\nand C:) and the rename fails with EXDEV, so the check degraded to a\nwarning and the stale-tree test saw no finding. It takes an explicit\n`tmpDir`, which now points inside the copy. As a side effect the command\nno longer writes `.tanstack/tmp` into the project it is validating,\nwhich is how this is verified on Linux: the directory is not recreated\nat the repository root while the CLI suite runs.\n\nThe other failure was in the test rather than the code: `listSourceFiles`\nreturns filesystem paths, so the entries under `src/routes` came back\nwith backslashes and the assertion spelled them with forward slashes.\n`mergeAnalyses` already normalises separators before they reach a\nmanifest, so the production output was never affected; the test now\nnormalises the same way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"0991ed28bdf6a175b2a9fd76bedfe5bea910cf9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/0991ed28bdf6a175b2a9fd76bedfe5bea910cf9f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193","verification":{"payload":"tree 0991ed28bdf6a175b2a9fd76bedfe5bea910cf9f\nparent 7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789444256 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789444256 +0000\n\nfix(cli): keep the router generator''s temporary files on one volume\n\nThe Windows leg reached `pnpm test` for the first time and failed two of\n528 tests; both were Windows-specific.\n\n`platform validate` regenerates the route tree in a copy of `src/routes`\nto compare it against the committed `routeTree.gen.ts`. The generator\nwrites each file to a temporary path and renames it into place, and its\ntemporary directory defaults to `.tanstack/tmp` resolved against\n`process.cwd()` — the repository — while the copy lives in the system\ntemp directory. On the Windows runner those are different volumes (D:\nand C:) and the rename fails with EXDEV, so the check degraded to a\nwarning and the stale-tree test saw no finding. It takes an explicit\n`tmpDir`, which now points inside the copy. As a side effect the command\nno longer writes `.tanstack/tmp` into the project it is validating,\nwhich is how this is verified on Linux: the directory is not recreated\nat the repository root while the CLI suite runs.\n\nThe other failure was in the test rather than the code: `listSourceFiles`\nreturns filesystem paths, so the entries under `src/routes` came back\nwith backslashes and the assertion spelled them with forward slashes.\n`mergeAnalyses` already normalises separators before they reach a\nmanifest, so the production output was never affected; the test now\nnormalises the same way.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQCrUuPHN\nDO7rerlyhZPDDpIZ5Q/8Nm4Iud1gU8HXlCno/vAfExrs2fHBzmkmEOskdShx4nW5WeL74Z8629W2\nHAw=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T03:51:02Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDY3OTUwZTU0Nzc4YzY0ODM1OWE5OTAyOGZjMzU5MWUxMzQ0NjAxOTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7","sha":"7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7"}],"sha":"67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/67950e54778c648359a99028fc3591e134460193"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:42:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:42:42Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(deps): pin the React types at the workspace root\n\nWith the bin link fixed, the Linux leg reached `pnpm typecheck` for the\nfirst time and `apps/docs` failed with 27 errors — React 19 code checked\nagainst `@types/react@18.3.31`, including inside Tecton''s sources.\n\nThe repository installs both React majors, so both copies of the types\nare in the store. A package in the virtual store that does not resolve\n`@types/react` as a peer (`react-aria-components`, and through it\nTecton''s `.tsx` sources) walks up to `node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules`,\nand which major pnpm hoists there depends on install history rather than\nthe lockfile: an incrementally updated tree had React 19 there, while a\nclean install — what CI does — hoists React 18. That is why this passed\nlocally and failed in CI.\n\nDeclaring the types at the workspace root makes pnpm skip the hoisted\ncopy altogether (no `@types/react` alias in `hoistedDependencies`), so\nthe fallback for every package in the store is this one pinned version\ninstead of a coin flip. Applications are unaffected in their own files:\nthey resolve their own `node_modules/@types/react` first, and\n`apps/conformance-react18` still compiles against `@types/react@18`.\n\nReproduced by removing `node_modules` and reinstalling, which reproduces\nthe CI failure exactly; verified by two clean installs that produce no\nhoisted React types and a passing `pnpm typecheck`. Build, build:apps,\nformat:check, lint, typecheck, 528 unit tests, 21 production E2E and 3\nHMR E2E all pass on that clean tree, with no warnings in any build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"bd65703d6280452b7dc584154f732d830461d2fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/bd65703d6280452b7dc584154f732d830461d2fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7","verification":{"payload":"tree bd65703d6280452b7dc584154f732d830461d2fd\nparent 2ca2ab79eda88c47f688a229a00fc4799b57a0a0\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789443762 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789443762 +0000\n\nfix(deps): pin the React types at the workspace root\n\nWith the bin link fixed, the Linux leg reached `pnpm typecheck` for the\nfirst time and `apps/docs` failed with 27 errors — React 19 code checked\nagainst `@types/react@18.3.31`, including inside Tecton''s sources.\n\nThe repository installs both React majors, so both copies of the types\nare in the store. A package in the virtual store that does not resolve\n`@types/react` as a peer (`react-aria-components`, and through it\nTecton''s `.tsx` sources) walks up to `node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules`,\nand which major pnpm hoists there depends on install history rather than\nthe lockfile: an incrementally updated tree had React 19 there, while a\nclean install — what CI does — hoists React 18. That is why this passed\nlocally and failed in CI.\n\nDeclaring the types at the workspace root makes pnpm skip the hoisted\ncopy altogether (no `@types/react` alias in `hoistedDependencies`), so\nthe fallback for every package in the store is this one pinned version\ninstead of a coin flip. Applications are unaffected in their own files:\nthey resolve their own `node_modules/@types/react` first, and\n`apps/conformance-react18` still compiles against `@types/react@18`.\n\nReproduced by removing `node_modules` and reinstalling, which reproduces\nthe CI failure exactly; verified by two clean installs that produce no\nhoisted React types and a passing `pnpm typecheck`. Build, build:apps,\nformat:check, lint, typecheck, 528 unit tests, 21 production E2E and 3\nHMR E2E all pass on that clean tree, with no warnings in any build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQD+EJ5pZ\nMx49jkvvk5tI4ySnFthDSdKozSGoIzK7E7zvNgRYJa8/cxvGkvjyehKG+pnYN6HNnNFC2HR9B7JN\nDgE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T03:42:48Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDdmNGRhZDBmY2U1N2MxMWIxNzIzNmExZTlmNzNiNjQ3ZWQwMmQyZDc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/2ca2ab79eda88c47f688a229a00fc4799b57a0a0","sha":"2ca2ab79eda88c47f688a229a00fc4799b57a0a0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/2ca2ab79eda88c47f688a229a00fc4799b57a0a0"}],"sha":"7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/7f4dad0fce57c11b17236a1e9f73b647ed02d2d7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commits/2ca2ab79eda88c47f688a229a00fc4799b57a0a0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:29:20Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-15T03:29:20Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"fix(ci): link workspace bins on a fresh clone and check out with LF\n\nBoth CI legs failed on this branch for reasons unrelated to the platform\ncode, and every build printed avoidable warnings.\n\n`pnpm lint` failed on Linux with `platform: not found`. pnpm links bin\nentries during `pnpm install`, which in CI happens before anything is\nbuilt, so `\"platform\": \"./dist/bin.js\"` was skipped with a warning\n(\"Failed to create bin ... ENOENT\") and never linked afterwards. Both\npublished bins now point at a checked-in stub that imports the build\noutput, so the link is created at install time and resolves once the\npackage is built.\n\n`pnpm format:check` failed on Windows with 558 files reported. The\nWindows runner checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` while Prettier is\nconfigured with `endOfLine: \"lf\"`, so every text file mismatched. A\n`.gitattributes` with `* text=auto eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF.\n\nAlso quieted the build output, which is otherwise hard to read in CI:\n\n- tsdown''s `external`/`noExternal` are deprecated; every config now uses\n  `deps.neverBundle`/`deps.alwaysBundle` (the CLI already did).\n- Rolldown''s plugin-timing hint fires on almost every build and says\n  nothing actionable; it is off for the platform pipeline (overridable\n  via `build.rolldownOptions.checks.pluginTimings`), the shell and docs.\n- The harness and shell bundle React, Tecton and the host into one entry\n  deliberately, so the 500 kB chunk hint only ever fires on that entry;\n  both set an explicit `chunkSizeWarningLimit`.\n- The CI actions were pinned to versions targeting the deprecated Node\n  20 runner; bumped to checkout@v5, setup-node@v5, upload-artifact@v5\n  and pnpm/action-setup@v6.\n\nThe E2E harness spawned `process.execPath` with `shell: true` on\nWindows, which passes the command line through cmd.exe unquoted (any\nspace in the Node or repository path breaks it) and makes `child.kill()`\nkill the shell rather than the server. Spawning the executable directly\nneeds no shell.\n\nVerified on Linux: build, build:apps, format:check, lint, typecheck,\n528 unit tests, 21 production E2E and 3 HMR E2E all pass, with no\nwarnings in any build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz","tree":{"sha":"2a92f8dcb610dde75fc3507e9978fe9118426f3f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/trees/2a92f8dcb610dde75fc3507e9978fe9118426f3f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/git/commits/2ca2ab79eda88c47f688a229a00fc4799b57a0a0","verification":{"payload":"tree 2a92f8dcb610dde75fc3507e9978fe9118426f3f\nparent b1c30a53fdb4efc405f2f66e742d55f023a3b1bd\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789442960 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1789442960 +0000\n\nfix(ci): link workspace bins on a fresh clone and check out with LF\n\nBoth CI legs failed on this branch for reasons unrelated to the platform\ncode, and every build printed avoidable warnings.\n\n`pnpm lint` failed on Linux with `platform: not found`. pnpm links bin\nentries during `pnpm install`, which in CI happens before anything is\nbuilt, so `\"platform\": \"./dist/bin.js\"` was skipped with a warning\n(\"Failed to create bin ... ENOENT\") and never linked afterwards. Both\npublished bins now point at a checked-in stub that imports the build\noutput, so the link is created at install time and resolves once the\npackage is built.\n\n`pnpm format:check` failed on Windows with 558 files reported. The\nWindows runner checks out with `core.autocrlf=true` while Prettier is\nconfigured with `endOfLine: \"lf\"`, so every text file mismatched. A\n`.gitattributes` with `* text=auto eol=lf` pins the working tree to LF.\n\nAlso quieted the build output, which is otherwise hard to read in CI:\n\n- tsdown''s `external`/`noExternal` are deprecated; every config now uses\n  `deps.neverBundle`/`deps.alwaysBundle` (the CLI already did).\n- Rolldown''s plugin-timing hint fires on almost every build and says\n  nothing actionable; it is off for the platform pipeline (overridable\n  via `build.rolldownOptions.checks.pluginTimings`), the shell and docs.\n- The harness and shell bundle React, Tecton and the host into one entry\n  deliberately, so the 500 kB chunk hint only ever fires on that entry;\n  both set an explicit `chunkSizeWarningLimit`.\n- The CI actions were pinned to versions targeting the deprecated Node\n  20 runner; bumped to checkout@v5, setup-node@v5, upload-artifact@v5\n  and pnpm/action-setup@v6.\n\nThe E2E harness spawned `process.execPath` with `shell: true` on\nWindows, which passes the command line through cmd.exe unquoted (any\nspace in the Node or repository path breaks it) and makes `child.kill()`\nkill the shell rather than the server. Spawning the executable directly\nneeds no shell.\n\nVerified on Linux: build, build:apps, format:check, lint, typecheck,\n528 unit tests, 21 production E2E and 3 HMR E2E all pass, with no\nwarnings in any build.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012jL1JKH3T6fi4QUXK6NWqz\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQMFZFxsp\ndugmYLLY+TY9roaz2hyqRiNpDGm3OdjWme3gpg5xwoJO/eltCWW4suVA1/XsR2iR5cnMMtnNz9PX\n1wQ=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-15T03:29:26Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/2ca2ab79eda88c47f688a229a00fc4799b57a0a0","node_id":"C_kwDOUbKFU9oAKDJjYTJhYjc5ZWRhODhjNDdmNjg4YTIyOWEwMGZjNDc5OWI1N2EwYTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/rpkapps/mfe-platform-2/commit/b1c30a53fdb4efc405f2f66e742d55f023a3b1bd","sha":"b1c30a53fdb4efc405f2f6