de_id":"U_kgDODqvYTA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/08bd78555595140f55bbea3eb3133ddd8373f3d0","node_id":"C_kwDOUbLk3NoAKDA4YmQ3ODU1NTU5NTE0MGY1NWJiZWEzZWIzMTMzZGRkODM3M2YzZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91","sha":"e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b","sha":"33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b"}],"sha":"08bd78555595140f55bbea3eb3133ddd8373f3d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/08bd78555595140f55bbea3eb3133ddd8373f3d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246143052?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bif26","id":246143052,"login":"bif26","node_id":"U_kgDODqvYTA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:54:01Z","email":"bif26@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bif26"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T20:54:01Z","email":"bif26@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bif26"},"message":"feat(server-mode): expose controller on 0.0.0.0 so the app can be reached via the server''s domain (v0.10.0)\n\nWhat this enables\n- Run ./start.sh --server and open http://<server-ip-or-domain>:33111\n  from any browser on the network. The frontend, the controller API\n  (/api/controller/*), the WebSocket (/ws), and the proxied backend\n  (/api/*) are all reachable from the server''s public hostname.\n\nCode changes\n- backend/config.py:\n  * New settings: controller_host (DE_COACH_CONTROLLER_HOST, default\n    127.0.0.1), controller_port (DE_COACH_CONTROLLER_PORT, default 33111),\n    bind_host (DE_COACH_BIND_HOST, alias of DE_COACH_HOST for clarity).\n  * CORS origins are now env-overridable via DE_COACH_CORS_ORIGINS\n    (comma-separated) — set to your public https origin in production.\n  * New trust_proxy_headers flag (DE_COACH_TRUST_PROXY, default 1)\n    so the controller honors X-Forwarded-Proto/Host behind nginx.\n- backend/controller.py:\n  * BACKEND_PORT / CONTROLLER_PORT read from settings (env-overridable).\n  * CORS middleware uses settings.cors_origins instead of [\"*\"].\n  * uvicorn.run() passes proxy_headers=True + forwarded_allow_ips=''*''\n    so WebSocket upgrade and absolute redirects use the public\n    scheme/host when behind a reverse proxy.\n  * The spawned backend is still pinned to 127.0.0.1 — it is NEVER\n    exposed to the network; only the controller proxies it.\n- start.sh:\n  * New flags: --server (binds 0.0.0.0), --host <addr>, --port <n>.\n  * Exports DE_COACH_CONTROLLER_HOST / _PORT for the controller process.\n  * Prints the public URL hint in server mode; warns about plaintext\n    HTTP and points to the nginx recipe for HTTPS.\n- stop.sh:\n  * Accepts --host / --port flags and reads DE_COACH_CONTROLLER_HOST /\n    _PORT env vars; falls back to probing 127.0.0.1 (always reachable\n    from the host itself, even when the controller binds 0.0.0.0).\n- systemd/local-de-coach-controller.service:\n  * Ships commented env-var overrides for server mode\n    (DE_COACH_CONTROLLER_HOST=0.0.0.0, DE_COACH_CORS_ORIGINS, etc.).\n- docs/markdown/20-server-deployment.md (NEW):\n  * Architecture recap, three deployment shapes (direct / nginx /\n    tailnet), full env-var table, complete nginx + Let''s Encrypt\n    recipe with WebSocket upgrade pass-through, systemd server-mode\n    unit, smoke-test commands, security notes.\n\nTests\n- backend/tests/test_scorer.py: 8/8 passed\n- verify_imports.py: ALL CHECKS PASSED\n- scripts/test_server_mode.py (new): end-to-end smoke test that\n  starts the controller with DE_COACH_CONTROLLER_HOST=0.0.0.0 and\n  verifies: (1) config picks up env overrides, (2) the socket can\n  bind 0.0.0.0, (3) /api/controller/status responds 200, (4) the\n  frontend/stub is served at /, (5) CORS preflight returns the\n  configured Access-Control-Allow-Origin, (6) /ws WebSocket upgrade\n  succeeds and the server pushes a snapshot frame. ALL CHECKS PASSED.\n\nBackwards compatibility\n- Defaults are unchanged: localhost-only binding, original ports, the\n  old dev-origin CORS list. Existing ./start.sh / systemd users see\n  no behavior change unless they explicitly opt into --server or set\n  the new env vars.","tree":{"sha":"9db7f714e2e780a18c772c99b260a5720da20e7a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/trees/9db7f714e2e780a18c772c99b260a5720da20e7a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/commits/33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246143052?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bif26","id":246143052,"login":"bif26","node_id":"U_kgDODqvYTA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b","node_id":"C_kwDOUbLk3NoAKDMzNzM4MDAzNzEwMjYyZjE0MWIyYjE0NGFlNDI2NWNkMzAyOGI2OWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91","sha":"e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91"}],"sha":"33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/33738003710262f141b2b144ae4265cd3028b69b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246143052?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bif26","id":246143052,"login":"bif26","node_id":"U_kgDODqvYTA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T10:54:00Z","email":"bif26@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bif26"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T10:54:00Z","email":"bif26@users.noreply.github.com","name":"bif26"},"message":"fix(fetch): resume no longer freezes with a fake fast speed; diagnose dead networks (v0.9.6)\n\nUser-visible bug: after resuming a partial 1.3 GB download (IP had changed),\nthe bar sat frozen at 245.3 MB/19.4% showing a bogus \"244.85 MB/s ETA 00:04\"\nwhile zero bytes flowed. Root causes and fixes:\n\n1. Bogus speed/ETA on resume (scripts/fetch_models.py):\n   the first speed sample divided the RESUMED bytes (offset from 0) by ~1 s,\n   latching EMA at ~245 MB/s; with no growth no new samples ever replaced it.\n   Speed/ETA are now computed from the resume offset, and the speed decays to\n   nothing after 5 s without growth.\n\n2. No stall feedback: a stalled transfer now says\n   \"no data Ns → reconnect at 45s\" in the bar itself (human + machine mode).\n\n3. No network diagnosis: every stall now probes huggingface.co (5 s HEAD).\n   If the path is dead (IP/VPN/DNS/IPv6/captive portal) the script says so\n   and retries every 30 s instead of silently burning 40 attempts; a hint\n   with an actionable check (ping huggingface.co) appears after repeated\n   zero-gain reconnects.\n\n4. Orphan children: sweep_orphans() at startup SIGKILLs leftover fetcher\n   children of previous runs (they hold the HF per-file lock, which has NO\n   timeout, and would block every new attempt forever). Children are\n   identified by a unique marker in their cmdline — never unrelated procs.\n\n5. Offline leak guard: child env forces HF_HUB_OFFLINE=0 and\n   TRANSFORMERS_OFFLINE=0 — an offline-first app env could previously make\n   the downloader refuse to fetch (instant fail loop on resume).\n\nTests:\n- 22/22 stub unit tests (fake stalled child, 245.3 MB partial: watchdog\n  fires, bytes kept, retry resumes at >= partial, no speed >50 MB/s shown,\n  orphan sweep kills marked child only, offline guard, probe smoke).\n- 8/8 E2E on real network with huggingface_hub 0.34.4: whisper download\n  interrupted mid-transfer (exit 130) → 31.5 MB partial kept → re-run logs\n  \"RESUMING, nothing restarts from zero\" → completes in 8 s → --check\n  verdicts correct → --machine protocol unchanged for the backend worker.","tree":{"sha":"58f078c5c3c1be54ef243ae75755209bf362a43c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/trees/58f078c5c3c1be54ef243ae75755209bf362a43c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/commits/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246143052?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bif26","id":246143052,"login":"bif26","node_id":"U_kgDODqvYTA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91","node_id":"C_kwDOUbLk3NoAKGU5NDIwNmZjNGJkZThmOTE0OWUzMzJhMmFhNDU2N2YzZmE2MGFjOTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25","sha":"27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25"}],"sha":"e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/e94206fc4bde8f9149e332a2aa4567f3fa60ac91"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:27:04Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T00:27:04Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"message":"feat(download): live, stall-proof, resumable model downloads (v0.9.5)\n\nThe ''download stops / restarts from zero'' bug is fixed for good:\n\n* scripts/fetch_models.py — ONE download path for setup.sh AND warmup:\n  - LIVE byte-accurate progress (MB / % / speed / ETA from real disk\n    bytes, updated 2x per second) — never a frozen bar again\n  - stall watchdog: no byte growth for 45 s -> kill child process,\n    reconnect, resume at the exact same byte\n  - resume survives Ctrl+C, crashes and PC reboots: partial data stays\n    in $HF_HOME blobs/*.incomplete and the next run CONTINUES\n  - hf_transfer + xet disabled everywhere (they cannot resume — the\n    actual cause of frozen/restarting downloads on slow internet)\n  - --machine mode: @@PROG/@@DONE/@@FAIL JSON lines\n\n* backend/asr_worker.py: warmup-time downloads delegate to the same\n  script and mirror byte progress into /api/status (UI live progress);\n  whisper fetches through it too; hf_transfer disabled at worker start\n\n* setup.sh / start.sh / README: v0.9.5 banner + resume messaging\n\nTests: watchdog unit tests 4/4; real 1.26 GB download hard-killed twice\n(971 MB, 1.05 GB) and resumed from the same byte both times; offline\nE2E warmup ~5 s + score 200; pytest 13 passed; SvelteKit build OK","tree":{"sha":"fb6287952b4916ccbe529ec63ceb60f18d5c5fa9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/trees/fb6287952b4916ccbe529ec63ceb60f18d5c5fa9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/commits/27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25","node_id":"C_kwDOUbLk3NoAKDI3MjQwY2RlMGFiODhhOTI5ZTI3ZDM3YTMzYzY5MDQ1YmJkY2RmMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296","sha":"ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296"}],"sha":"27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/27240cde0ab88a929e27d37a33c69045bbdcdf25"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:53:33Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T23:53:33Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"message":"fix(warmup,setup): offline-first model loading — setup.sh pre-downloads + verifies ALL models (v0.9.4)\n\nRoot cause of ''load failed: Can''t load the model ... pytorch_model.bin'':\ninterrupted downloads left a partial HF cache that looked complete, and\nwarmup-time downloads had no retry/resume — on a slow/flaky connection the\nworker gave up after ~4 min with a cryptic OSError.\n\nsetup.sh / scripts/fetch_models.sh (offline-first):\n- download BOTH models (Whisper tiny + Wav2Vec2 large xlsr-53-german) once,\n  then the app runs 100% offline — no downloads at warmup, ever\n- a model counts as cached ONLY when its weights file is present + sane\n  size (>=1 GB w2v / >=70 MB whisper) — interrupted downloads never count\n- resumable + retried (3x, plain-downloader fallback after hf_transfer),\n  live HF progress bars, re-running skips complete models (idempotent)\n- setup.sh prints an OFFLINE-READY verdict at the end; stale v0.5.0\n  whisper-only texts removed; pre-flight shows both models\n\nasr_worker.py (defense in depth):\n- offline-first load: verified local snapshot -> from_pretrained(\n  local_files_only=True); zero network when cache is complete\n- incomplete cache -> resumable, retried download (4 attempts, never\n  touches the duplicate 1.26 GB flax file); corrupt cache -> auto-wipe +\n  re-download once (auto-repair)\n- friendly, actionable load errors surfaced to the UI\n\nengine/routes:\n- /api/score + /api/live wait max 180 s behind an in-flight warmup, then\n  503 ''still loading'' (was: hang up to 900 s then 500)\n- WorkerError maps to 503 + exact reason (service state, not a bug)\n\nE2E (real 1.26 GB model, CPU): offline warmup 3.95 s, score 200, unload\nfrees RAM, broken-model path -> clear error + fast 503, backend pytest\n13 passed, SvelteKit build OK","tree":{"sha":"15aeeb2b14c2cfc41713a3be3f04ee30f423b0bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/trees/15aeeb2b14c2cfc41713a3be3f04ee30f423b0bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/commits/ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296","node_id":"C_kwDOUbLk3NoAKGViZWVmMzZhNDE0NGVhYjVhOWRkOGUwNjMwZTkwYWFmNmYzNzUyOTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466","sha":"d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466"}],"sha":"ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/ebeef36a4144eab5a9dd8e0630e90aaf6f375296"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:49:52Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:49:52Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"message":"fix(warmup): move ASR model into a dedicated worker process (v0.9.3)\n\nField report on Python 3.14: ~17s into warmup the backend stopped answering\nand the controller watchdog SIGKILLed it (''Backend unresponsive for 30s'').\n\nTwo root causes:\n1. v0.9.1 loaded the model on a background THREAD — torch weight\n   deserialization holds the GIL, starving the asyncio event loop.\n2. The controller dropped its cached backend status on failed polls, so it\n   forgot a load was in flight and the unresponsive budget collapsed\n   from 120s back to 30s.\n\nFix — process isolation:\n- NEW backend/asr_worker.py: dedicated worker PROCESS owning torch /\n  transformers / faster-whisper and the hf_transfer download progress\n  patch. JSON-lines IPC over stdin/stdout (ping/load/score/live/unload).\n  Dies with the backend (PDEATHSIG + atexit); exits on unload so freed RAM\n  really returns to the OS. No orphaned ~1.5 GB processes.\n- core/engine.py is now a thin IPC client with the same load-state machine\n  and /api/status contract (live stage/bytes/speed/ETA preserved); worker\n  death mid-load surfaces as model_state=error.\n- /api/score and /api/live delegate decode + inference to the worker;\n  scoring math + DB stay in the API process.\n- /api/status RAM = API process + worker (RAM monitor stays truthful).\n- controller: keep last known backend status across failed polls (120s\n  load budget can''t collapse anymore), RAM breaker sums the whole process\n  tree, _stop_backend takes children down first.\n- NEW test_worker_integration.py: real-worker IPC roundtrip against the\n  tiny random Wav2Vec2 (would have caught the missing-command-id bug found\n  during testing). test_warmup_async.py ported to the fake worker.\n\nE2E with the real 1.26 GB model: warmup POST returns in 0.01s, health\nanswers in 7-21ms DURING the whole load, warm load 5.7s, 0 freeze kills,\nscore 200 (direct + proxied), unload 448→55MB with no orphan workers.","tree":{"sha":"a4f525a14f6e1ad26855e8bbe76a2a67066b848d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/trees/a4f525a14f6e1ad26855e8bbe76a2a67066b848d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/commits/d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466","node_id":"C_kwDOUbLk3NoAKGQxYzE4NmQ5YjdmN2E3Y2U0NzNiNDQ3MGY4YjFmOGE0Njc1ZDU0NjY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0","sha":"525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0"}],"sha":"d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/d1c186d9b7f7a7ce473b4470f8b1f8a4675d5466"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-13T20:59:47Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-13T21:01:11Z","email":"z@container","name":"Z User"},"message":"fix(score,warmup): UploadFile 422 regression, ffmpeg decode fallback, fast warmup with live progress (v0.9.2)\n\nPOST /api/score 422 (every real recording failed):\n- pydantic >= 2.12 (unpinned, pip-resolved) rejects ''bytes = File(...)'' with\n  ''Input should be a valid bytes'' on FastAPI 0.115 — switch to\n  UploadFile + await audio.read(), stable across all versions\n- libsndfile cannot decode browser WebM/Opus (or Safari MP4/AAC) containers,\n  so preprocessing 500''d with ''Format not recognised'' — new ffmpeg/pydub\n  fallback in preprocessor.decode_and_resample (16 kHz mono float32)\n\nWarmup speed + visibility:\n- enable hf_transfer parallel downloads (5-10x faster first warmup);\n  hub falls back to the resumable single-stream path on interruption\n- disable hf_xet: its deprecated download_files path fires the progress\n  callback only twice (0 -> final), leaving the UI at 0%\n- mirror huggingface_hub tqdm bars into the engine state machine and advance\n  ''n'' manually for disabled (headless) bars; /api/status now streams\n  stage/stage_detail/bytes_done/bytes_total/speed_bps/eta_s/progress_pct\n- Model card renders a determinate progress bar with stage label, MB done /\n  total, speed and ETA instead of an eternal indeterminate spinner\n- fetch_models.sh uses the same fast-downloader env for pre-downloads\n\nUI error handling:\n- format FastAPI 422 validation arrays into readable messages (was\n  ''[object Object]'' in the Practice error banner and toast)\n\nTests: backend pytest 12/12; E2E warmup (fresh 1.26 GB download with live\nprogress, cached reload 4.4 s) and score (HTTP 200) direct + proxied through\nthe controller; docs screenshots refreshed (live download progress + loaded\nstate); version 0.9.2 across backend, UI, docs and README release table.","tree":{"sha":"16e4a7600bfdade84c495a1e4bd45cb5b755efcc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/trees/16e4a7600bfdade84c495a1e4bd45cb5b755efcc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/git/commits/525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0","node_id":"C_kwDOUbLk3NoAKDUyNTA2OGQ3ZjdkZTQ3ZmM1Njg1MzJmNDY5MzdiYTQ0NTIwMTliZTA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commit/2a6a2ec9c38334db193698e586b7e030f3f20d96","sha":"2a6a2ec9c38334db193698e586b7e030f3f20d96","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/2a6a2ec9c38334db193698e586b7e030f3f20d96"}],"sha":"525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/HeaTTap/Local_DE_Coach/commits/525068d7f7de47fc568532f46937ba4452019be0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/246143052?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/bif26","id":246143052,"login":"bif26","node_id":"U_kgDODqvYTA","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bif26/repos","site_admin":