7:30Z","email":"changbae.bang@29cm.co.kr","name":"방창배(changbae bang)"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T05:17:30Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: compatibility matrix, preflight diagnostics and --env (#12)\n\nMake the support envelope explicit and make every wrong setup loud instead\nof a silent \"0 findings\" run.\n\nEntries\n- App Router loading/error/not-found/default.* are entries sharing the\n  page''s layout chain; global-error.* is an entry with an empty chain.\n  Parallel @slot and intercepting (.) segments stay plain directories\n  (fixture app-router-conventions).\n- Pages Router `Page.getLayout = …` assignments on the default export are\n  part of the page root, so Providers mounted there count.\n- Class components: `static contextType = C` / `Class.contextType = C`\n  are silent consumers.\n\nPreflight\n- No-entries error explains what was looked for, what exists instead,\n  nested Next.js apps under a monorepo root, and the --entry/--always\n  recipe.\n- tsconfig: unparseable file exits 2 with the TS message; unknown options,\n  invalid values and missing `extends` targets become `note tsconfig:`\n  diagnostics; references-only root configs get a pointer to --tsconfig.\n- Unresolved relative/alias imports are counted and reported.\n- jsconfig.json is used when no tsconfig.json exists.\n- `unprovided --env` (with --json) prints versions, root, boundary,\n  config, tsconfig, routers, entry counts and notes for bug reports.\n\nDocs\n- README / README.ko: \"Requirements & compatibility\" section with the\n  support matrix, \"What is detected / not detected\", \"How it fails\"\n  (every exit-2 message and note prefix) and the --env example; known\n  false negatives and roadmap updated. CHANGELOG Unreleased entry.\n- CI matrix adds Node 24.\n\nTests: 37 -> 53.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursor@cursor.com>","tree":{"sha":"007c264d4033d6049ba61175abffdeee6e1ebf78","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/changbaebang/unprovided/git/trees/007c264d4033d6049ba61175abffdeee6e1ebf78"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/changbaebang/unprovided/git/commits/77008be6a19c67f5246e8174c615b923dfdd0618","verification":{"payload":"tree 007c264d4033d6049ba61175abffdeee6e1ebf78\nparent 7d4109e4f30ccc15d25e405b7b81d1ad2b6b7ee5\nauthor 방창배(changbae bang) <changbae.bang@29cm.co.kr> 1789622250 +0900\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789622250 +0900\n\nfeat: compatibility matrix, preflight diagnostics and --env (#12)\n\nMake the support envelope explicit and make every wrong setup loud instead\nof a silent \"0 findings\" run.\n\nEntries\n- App Router loading/error/not-found/default.* are entries sharing the\n  page''s layout chain; global-error.* is an entry with an empty chain.\n  Parallel @slot and intercepting (.) segments stay plain directories\n  (fixture app-router-conventions).\n- Pages Router `Page.getLayout = …` assignments on the default export are\n  part of the page root, so Providers mounted there count.\n- Class components: `static contextType = C` / `Class.contextType = C`\n  are silent consumers.\n\nPreflight\n- No-entries error explains what was looked for, what exists instead,\n  nested Next.js apps under a monorepo root, and the --entry/--always\n  recipe.\n- tsconfig: unparseable file exits 2 with the TS message; unknown options,\n  invalid values and missing `extends` targets become `note tsconfig:`\n  diagnostics; references-only root configs get a pointer to --tsconfig.\n- Unresolved relative/alias imports are counted and reported.\n- jsconfig.json is used when no tsconfig.json exists.\n- `unprovided --env` (with --json) prints versions, root, boundary,\n  config, tsconfig, routers, entry counts and notes for bug reports.\n\nDocs\n- README / README.ko: \"Requirements & compatibility\" section with the\n  support matrix, \"What is detected / not detected\", \"How it fails\"\n  (every exit-2 message and note prefix) and the --env example; known\n  false negatives and roadmap updated. CHANGELOG Unreleased entry.\n- CI matrix adds Node 24.\n\nTests: 37 -> 53.\n\nCo-authored-by: Cursor <cursor@cursor.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqq3fqCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA+BAQAKZ7VkidxWW5GZU9FgTWEv+Z\nTn7ziG+OVx2UVNj/D57yCNM++5cG/ZuD83DYDwdbvpdI/c0i9LLiZ/wozVlkrydg\nULnLMEhwKgxTWSbGymU5hK/iZSbwzfE8mApMaQWnSZYrGQVNWhEEzqrSUrASN/TC\n6cHvWr7hRkQ2/T6IOSW3bysHX/6KVOW7Enk+huQZO2oCdfxeBy+9nttXEum0f0KS\nTNi4coQX23SLvM4uh160X8xPQb/P65l3LfzlHQcgchQFqBItpJBZaWX0QhjlNV70\ngW2QYJiBTh2jwZTyk5iNBQ+Sn/bpNWiFU5vYvGOkYYDYXSp9XoJf8DTkzbJ+hVk7\n5yu5ngruPPMGyp6lRQTBlTjP+5IEQXURQZ2t8XAwftpIbn+RPiQDpCicsRH5i69h\nGDf1ABErdN36QQfDlS7Lh/sz8p6doxWrVGojVM/M9nN/rVPuTgA9yOMJizWnQGj1\n7zZriey7AXqlMiur0H1Hw/rKcNQPS4Tyx7dnoO2E43HasdlR/S50idqR8kIUgfvE\nh2XGZduu5pbDsDb2OI+VsKPgGSianWi3ENGb7rIB2WD2AzZxNXXGquIkxkiRsp9y\nXAucv/j/lqDs2C/FBEDjIuZpFc0oFskGtksp137Xki6+mAqLyx6tZLSgI8K5tWqP\nkV9GoCBgAo9BHhXx8OKC\n=PMjq\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-17T05:17:30Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"htt