rkode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/commits/37b50d145e79955635cf4c1c2b54697aaccdb1a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-01T20:39:15Z","email":"103884938+animarkode@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Bell"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-01T20:39:15Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix(vault): renew API tokens before expiry (#33)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Renew the API''s Vault token before its TTL expires using a hosted\nservice that shares the existing singleton client. Retry transient\nfailures within the remaining lifetime and log terminal failures without\nexposing token material.\n- Add a least-privilege API policy and document provisioning an orphan\nperiodic token without an explicit maximum TTL, so production can\noperate beyond the ordinary token lifetime without a root token.\n\n## Linked issue\n\nCloses #31\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `dotnet build src/api/Faber.Api/Faber.Api.csproj` — zero warnings\nand errors.\n- [x] Vault integration suite — all 19 tests passed, including 12 new\ntests for repeated renewal beyond initial TTL and mount maximum TTL,\nrestricted permissions, transient recovery, terminal failures, expiry\nbounds, long TTLs, and cancellation.\n- [x] Branch diff reviewed; `git diff --check` passed. Policy\npermissions match the tested policy.\n- [ ] Production token provisioning and deployment validation.\n\n## Notes\n\nProduction requires a periodic token without an explicit maximum TTL;\nordinary renewable tokens retain Vault''s maximum lifetime. Expired or\nrevoked tokens require replacement and an API restart. Bootstrap\ncontinues to require a separate credential with write permissions.","tree":{"sha":"99d4ccf1947b04a69275182fac34406d94451f5d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/git/trees/99d4ccf1947b04a69275182fac34406d94451f5d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/git/commits/37b50d145e79955635cf4c1c2b54697aaccdb1a7","verification":{"payload":"tree 99d4ccf1947b04a69275182fac34406d94451f5d\nparent 393a032dcdfb5f50dc817a5359cfcc9a886529fb\nauthor Alex Bell <103884938+animarkode@users.noreply.github.com> 1790887155 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790887155 +0200\n\nfix(vault): renew API tokens before expiry (#33)\n\n## Summary\n\n- Renew the API''s Vault token before its TTL expires using a hosted\nservice that shares the existing singleton client. Retry transient\nfailures within the remaining lifetime and log terminal failures without\nexposing token material.\n- Add a least-privilege API policy and document provisioning an orphan\nperiodic token without an explicit maximum TTL, so production can\noperate beyond the ordinary token lifetime without a root token.\n\n## Linked issue\n\nCloses #31\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `dotnet build src/api/Faber.Api/Faber.Api.csproj` — zero warnings\nand errors.\n- [x] Vault integration suite — all 19 tests passed, including 12 new\ntests for repeated renewal beyond initial TTL and mount maximum TTL,\nrestricted permissions, transient recovery, terminal failures, expiry\nbounds, long TTLs, and cancellation.\n- [x] Branch diff reviewed; `git diff --check` passed. Policy\npermissions match the tested policy.\n- [ ] Production token provisioning and deployment validation.\n\n## Notes\n\nProduction requires a periodic token without an explicit maximum TTL;\nordinary renewable tokens retain Vault''s maximum lifetime. Expired or\nrevoked tokens require replacement and an API restart. Bootstrap\ncontinues to require a separate credential with write permissions.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvsTzCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAtkIQAFR09eITKSQb4ZIZS8kSNUIB\nm/zJ7BivMKJKzrTzsNQ/KAkAg5NidrihkrnrldBaOcNfnFadGouBPr/yvMzeJTwX\nzy6YeSzf/+sTwVt/81My5C9q9tW+HCnuxpoM9f2PYuw2B0azZNXOQDBtzYUBf3Vb\nkBwPWkfiNNOwr2njHOFkDIo0gq