t board, snapshot-preflight and deleted-solution\nreferences from `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\nand the `github-workflow` skill.\n\n## Linked issue\nCloses #28\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `bash scripts/verify-third-party-notices.sh` exits 0 locally\n- [x] `dotnet.yml` parses as valid YAML\n- [x] Repo-wide grep for the removed files/workflows/project board finds\nno stale references\n- [x] `.NET` workflow passes on this PR, including the new notices step\n\n## Notes\n- Secret scanning and push protection are already enabled on the repo\n(checked via `gh api`).\n- The `ADD_TO_PROJECT_PAT` secret still exists in repo settings and\nneeds deleting by hand; nothing references it any more.","tree":{"sha":"4dd57f72a9a0545e3bcc5e986cb36f0e058cebd6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/git/trees/4dd57f72a9a0545e3bcc5e986cb36f0e058cebd6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/git/commits/393a032dcdfb5f50dc817a5359cfcc9a886529fb","verification":{"payload":"tree 4dd57f72a9a0545e3bcc5e986cb36f0e058cebd6\nparent 3c44de0a5eb55cc15067049dc955ac8eb80afcf8\nauthor Alex Bell <103884938+VoxSollers@users.noreply.github.com> 1790708071 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790708071 +0200\n\nchore(infra): trim CI workflows and keep a single solution file (#29)\n\n## Summary\n- Keep `Faber.sln` and delete `Faber.slnx` (CI and local builds run on\nSDK 8, which cannot read `.slnx`); both files listed the same 36\nprojects.\n- Remove the migration-era `publication-readiness`, `add-to-project`,\n`move-linked-issue` and `remove-from-project` workflows, plus\n`verify-solution-projects.sh` and `verify-public-snapshot.sh`.\n- Run `verify-third-party-notices.sh` as a step in `dotnet.yml`.\n- Drop the project board, snapshot-preflight and deleted-solution\nreferences from `CONTRIBUTING.md`, `README.md`, `AGENTS.md`, `CLAUDE.md`\nand the `github-workflow` skill.\n\n## Linked issue\nCloses #28\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] `bash scripts/verify-third-party-notices.sh` exits 0 locally\n- [x] `dotnet.yml` parses as valid YAML\n- [x] Repo-wide grep for the removed files/workflows/project board finds\nno stale references\n- [x] `.NET` workflow passes on this PR, including the new notices step\n\n## Notes\n- Secret scanning and push protection are already enabled on the repo\n(checked via `gh api`).\n- The `ADD_TO_PROJECT_PAT` secret still exists in repo settings and\nneeds deleting by hand; nothing references it any more.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqvAlnCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMAcQAIPXypKwW1vA3enKyKR7is4s\nQJJLg/Jn/0gxf5+zYt6MlRWT6Bx6LSlPX2+R39I/tHVOIp5c5Wb/VZKSCNqx7hej\nULtVtS86hM4YoH+tEEEq+zT4Lclj2/I3fgW+oH9YCpWUfsutcAcGhyfl6cWU30Gg\nLK/NN7jRscyjV8P2h50tEfx5u4NZOxA75mSTlSQ4ABnMvvGibBhOD+dXQ1xs5t27\nb21WUreFuTkm+tAvXdfOvcWWm6R5En7ALfWKXafib5gmXmuReIY0bTYLWQS0NZve\n2h3+HGsFpDcK4qOokTtDqHlrwe71JRxAA0Trq9s8be9tTBnk1u738sKCmnm9GuNu\ntx8tvsbzut62IeqsXq1NYPxnTGo/QhQ+uglkq75xOIeqY9XUx9fkeKbzuaBMQLzd\nqRmVhp74v0ehd0lBB/gT37yhW5jipxpnHrGRyJve9+hM4047QhfuVJKeYorzaMoM\nlmGTyxh7VTRHngaovQKjkZ31TnnN9XS4gMbf2Wu3KUxQQBU8kpU3h9kKvUgH/D6w\n6Le0IKLvG8PpB4g1OH4AHYwVEFIkTHdcys/5bMDZu4aRjcGz2lQ/XVHTGDDKKI0b\nBMu1TgeyTlw8uM0OUq7hpaiBBhlLzJ4muhS/hziZZ5zgkpdg0fvH0eKplxWdmUZw\ny7ZJad6ebZMwvDYb4U0D\n=siFT\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-29T18:54:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/animarkode/faber/commit/393a032dcdfb5f50dc817a5359cfcc9a886529fb","node_id":"C_kwDOUclv5doAKDM5M2EwMzJkY2RmYjVmNTBkYzgxN2E1MzU5Y2ZjYzlhODg2NTI5ZmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/animarkode/faber/commit/3c44de0a5eb55cc15067049dc955ac8eb80afcf8","sha":"3c44de0a5eb55cc15067049dc955ac8eb80afcf8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/commits/3c44de0a5eb55cc15067049dc955ac8eb80afcf8"}],"sha":"393a032dcdfb5f50dc817a5359cfcc9a886529fb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/commits/393a032dcdfb5f50dc817a5359cfcc9a886529fb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/103884938?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/animarkode","id":103884938,"login":"animarkode","node_id":"U_kgDOBjEoig","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/animarkode","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/commits/3c44de0a5eb55cc15067049dc955ac8eb80afcf8/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:25:58Z","email":"103884938+VoxSollers@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Alex Bell"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:25:58Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat(resumes): cache resumes and generated PDFs in Redis (#22)\n\n## Summary\n- Wires a Redis-backed `HybridCache` from the Aspire `redis` connection\nstring and removes the `FaberRedis` config drift; the cache degrades to\nL1-only when no Redis is configured.\n- Caches the resume list, single resumes and rendered PDFs (shared by\n`download` and `generate`) under user-scoped keys, invalidated by one EF\nCore `SaveChangesInterceptor` so none of the ~40 write handlers has to\nremember to.\n- Keeps the API working uncached when Redis is unavailable, proven by a\ndedicated Redis-down fixture.\n\n## Linked issue\nCloses #15\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Resumes integration suite — 352 passing (cache hits, invalidation\nafter resume/nested-entity writes, PDF reuse and invalidation,\nRedis-down behaviour)\n- [x] Faber.Api integration suite — 57 passing, including the\n`expensive-resource` rate-limit tests that share the PDF path\n- [x] Resumes unit suite — 22 passing (cache-key shape)\n- [x] Manual: repeat PDF download is served from cache; an edit is\nreflected in the next download; stopping the `redis` resource does not\nbreak the app\n- [x] Auth integration suite (its fixture lost the fake Redis connection\nstring; not re-run locally)\n\n## Notes\n\n**Invalidation design.** Tags, not a version-stamp column: a stamp would\nhave meant an EF migration plus a bump in every nested write.\n`ResumesCacheInvalidationInterceptor` collects affected resumes/users\nfrom the change tracker before the save and removes the tags\n`resume:{id}` and `user:{id}:resumes` after it commits. Bulk\n`ExecuteUpdate`/`ExecuteDelete` bypass `SaveChanges` and would need\nexplicit invalidation; none exist in production code today, and\n`docs/decisions/caching.md` records that caveat.\n\n**Keys** are user-scoped and stamped with assembly MVIDs\n(`resumes:{build}:user:{u}:pdf:{r}:first-template:{templateBuild}`), so\na deploy that changes a cached DTO''s shape or a template''s markup gets\nfresh keys without anyone bumping a prefix.\n\n**Degradation.** The Redis client is forced to\n`AbortOnConnectFail=false`, `BacklogPolicy.FailFast` and 1 s timeouts,\nso an outage fails fast instead of queueing each request behind the 5 s\ndefault backlog. Invalidation failures after a committed write are\nlogged and swallowed — a committed write must never become a 500. No\nRedis health check, so an outage doesn''t mark the API unhealthy.\nStaleness is bounded by a 10 min expiration (1 min local).\n\n**Two bugs found by the branch review and fixed here:** cache factories\nnow own a service scope, because `HybridCache` runs one shared factory\nfor concurrent callers and the first caller''s scoped `DbContext` could\nbe disposed underneath the others; and post-commit invalidation uses\n`CancellationToken.None`, since an abort after the commit previously\nskipped invalidation silently.\n\n**Reviewer-visible extras.** The AppHost now starts RedisInsight\nalongside Redis for local inspection. The Resumes test assembly runs\nwithout parallelization: its fixture sets `VAULT_ADDR` process-wide, and\nthe new Redis-down fixture would otherwise race it.","tree":{"sha":"d1c79b6964d2d4511a61cdff19f80ec0b275395a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/git/trees/d1c79b6964d2d4511a61cdff19f80ec0b275395a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/animarkode/faber/git/commits/3c44de0a5eb55cc15067049dc955ac8eb80afcf8","verification":{"payload":"tree d1c79b6964d2d4511a61cdff19f80ec0b275395a\nparent ac33bd5a80c36474ca891b47328f668ffb9fd844\nauthor Alex Bell <103884938+VoxSollers@users.noreply.github.com> 1790101558 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790101558 +0200\n\nfeat(resumes): cache resumes and generated PDFs in Redis (#22)\n\n## Summary\n- Wires a Redis-backed `HybridCache` from the Aspire `redis` connection\nstring and removes the `FaberRedis` config drift; the cache degrades to\nL1-only when no Redis is configured.\n- Caches the resume list, single resumes and rendered PDFs (shared by\n`download` and `generate`) under user-scoped keys, invalidated by one EF\nCore `SaveChangesInterceptor` so none of the ~40 write handlers has to\nremember to.\n- Keeps the API working uncached when Redis is unavailable, proven by a\ndedicated Redis-down fixture.\n\n## Linked issue\nCloses #15\n\n## Test plan\n- [x] Resumes integration suite — 352 passing (cache hits, invalidation\nafter resume/nested-entity writes, PDF reuse and invalidation,\nRedis-down behaviour)\n- [x] Faber.Api integration suite — 57 passing, including the\n`expensive-resource` rate-limit tests that share the PDF path\n- [x] Resumes unit suite — 22 passing (cache-key shape)\n- [x] Manual: repeat PDF download is served from cache; an edit is\nreflected in the next download; stopping the `redis` resource does not\nbreak the app\n- [x] Auth integration suite (its fixture lost the fake Redis connection\nstring; not re-run locally)\n\n## Notes\n\n**Invalidation design.** Tags, not a version-stamp column: a stamp would\nhave meant an EF migration plus a bump in every nested write.\n`ResumesCacheInvalidationInterceptor` collects affected resumes/users\nfrom the change tracker before the save and removes the tags\n`resume:{id}` and `user:{id}:resumes` after it commits. Bulk\n`ExecuteUpdate`/`ExecuteDelete` bypass `SaveChanges` and would need\nexplicit invalidation; none exist in production code today, and\n`docs/decisions/caching.md` records that caveat.\n\n**Keys** are user-scoped and stamped with assembly MVIDs\n(`resumes:{build}:user:{u}:pdf:{r}:first-template:{templateBuild}`), so\na deploy that changes a cached DTO''s shape or a template''s markup gets\nfresh keys without anyone bumping a prefix.\n\n**Degradation.** The Redis client is forced to\n`AbortOnConnectFail=false`, `BacklogPolicy.FailFast` and 1 s timeouts,\nso an outage fails fast instead of queueing each request behind the 5 s\ndefault backlog. Invalidation failures after a committed write are\nlogged and swallowed — a committed write must never become a 500. No\nRedis health check, so an outage doesn''t mark the API unhealthy.\nStaleness is bounded by a 10 min expiration (1 min local).\n\n**Two bugs found by the branch review and fixed here:** cache factories\nnow own a service scope, because `HybridCache` runs one shared factory\nfor concurrent callers and the first caller''s scoped `DbContext` could\nbe disposed underneath the others; and post-commit invalidation uses\n`CancellationToken.None`, since an abort after the commit previously\nskipped invalidation silently.\n\n**Reviewer-visible extras.** The AppHost now starts RedisInsight\nalongside Redis for local inspection. The Resumes test assembly runs\nwithout parallelization: its fixture sets `VAULT_ADDR` process-wide, and\nthe new Redis-down fixture would otherwise race it.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqssg2CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAxtMQAIQo3WSU5NfXXWt2dVMRlDIV\nEdvDd4v5JFJtNYpR00je41el3Blg8TU3fdnM1ITfy4VZGI7GR7z0RVKvcw+FOHMd\ncGyIRQgNkfVb7ezH81cJvsvNNPCxemrDx+5ns14vscMPhnmRkUB74AfGLTmw/j1T\nJfXYyBUiS+6V7UKbcbhvBh9mCfYeyLbyXMicd2VNeHpWzDALeE6P1/2s/eaDT3vM\n8dujztJ24TW51EKeG1z4tPMZKagR9l8+oSGs0OO83rjnq1OMjXH+47TQ9VO5QGVR\nc3EUJf7SlNjMT0msupZmvB8rv1bUJHcm3BymfGiLhCMZf+y50cNeJ5WkwiLK/SDm\nVKLWohaGT229F6DlvR05SSIgVBcWJtdH0Iz/LoIQZROBZyL62/3syNg1Wfa9r8C9\n2ucx5Gxb3aA4JBe6fLtL4maes0+H2KFg9fUlBBCRr7HCgbLdcR9AUuOq8q3+LjNi\n1p8AlgpzP0EQCPoGCMhPKulb5tdLkt1Y17g3fufQ13qDc0xxBtdUgiP0kdo/hmqr\nE+Kdo5voqp2q94UlGp970cZDvsanKzVb/D9smgAp84AIp9Yt7LIaRmMLf3gtuoSx\nXCH8rxklIjFTnuYJDwxpkCnb3Z9Tmnrg1wrYev5kCSl4Sop3nPwLezI3NOagfzfX\n7V/XclVNlaZhZd4sXNg4\n=sp5A\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T18:25:59Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_