lguun Otgon"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-16T05:06:05Z","committedDate":"2026-09-16T05:06:05Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:41:36.544Z","repositoryId":1372537659,"sha":"1d46d0b52054043689d54d6bb4787dbf7609734d"},{"author":{"account":{"login":"dulguun0225","providerType":"User"},"email":"dulguun0225@gmail.com","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-16T05:03:17Z","committedDate":"2026-09-16T05:03:17Z","committer":{"account":{"login":"web-flow","providerType":"User"},"email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:41:36.544Z","repositoryId":1372537659,"sha":"a3601b91143f0578353a40442be0010fff8c6789"},{"author":{"account":null,"email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Hefesto Bot"},"authoredDate":"2026-09-16T04:58:17Z","committedDate":"2026-09-16T04:58:17Z","committer":{"account":null,"email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Hefesto Bot"},"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:41:36.544Z","repositoryId":1372537659,"sha":"829a895558cd418a895955de4c6b1ba9b61093c4"}],"observedAt":"2026-10-09T00:41:36.544Z","raw":[{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/86d9d9511385204533fd89b86ee02c0dd6d86dbf/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:40:58Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T03:40:58Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a refusal names its input and what is allowed; a request body has a size limit\n\njava-backend-api *A refusal names its input*, *A refused input gets one code wherever it travels*, *An\nundeclared member''s refusal lists the members allowed*, *A request body has a size limit, refused with its\nmaximum* (skills 54604d5).\n\n- FieldError names a body member by pointer or a path variable, query parameter or header by OpenAPI''s in and\n  name, never both; FieldError.ofParameter builds the second, and the ban covers every constructor.\n- ApiFieldCode: validation.unknown-field carries allowed (the declared members or query parameters, sorted);\n  new validation.invalid-value {expected}, validation.unknown-value {allowed}, validation.required.\n- DeclaredInputCheck, an interceptor, refuses before any argument is read: an undeclared query parameter (read\n  from getQueryString()), a repeated query parameter or single-valued header, and a UUID, int32, int64 or enum\n  text not in its exact form, untrimmed. Strict Converters were tried first and rejected by a run: Spring\n  retries a value the conversion service refused with its lenient property editors (0x10 bound as 16).\n- ApiExceptionHandler: MethodArgumentTypeMismatchException and isMissingAfterConversion() are\n  validation.invalid-value, an absent query parameter or header validation.required, at in and name;\n  validation.bad-request is left to a framework 400 no input code describes.\n- StrictJsonBodyConverter: allowed from the type; a malformed UUID (strict reader on the reader''s own mapper),\n  an integer past its range (was validation.malformed-body) and an enum value outside its set (was\n  wrong-type) are invalid-value and unknown-value; both passes record at most 100 entries and the rest leave as\n  errorsOmitted; wrong-type expected for a Number member is number, its schema type.\n- Body limit: api.request-body.max-size, DataSize, default 64KB (API_REQUEST_BODY_MAX_SIZE); a declared\n  Content-Length over it is refused unread, otherwise at most limit+1 bytes are read; 413 request.too-large\n  with params.max. Multipart is off (415), so that is the one 413; any other 413 is the catch-all 500.\n- WireError names a params record; request.too-large carries TooLarge(max); Rejected refuses a code with\n  params; the snapshot test checks response params and that each param name is one lower-case word.\n- OpenAPI: the error entry is one of {pointer} or {in, name}; the problem declares params and errorsOmitted;\n  every operation declares 400 and every body-taking one 413, written by a customizer and held by two new\n  vacuum rules.\n- Tests: RequestInputEndpointIT over a test-only probe (absent, blank, not parsing, outside the set,\n  repeated, undeclared, against the generated document''s parameters; a lenient route as negative control);\n  the body sweep asserts allowed and expected against the schema and 101 failures as 100 + errorsOmitted 1;\n  the limit at exactly and one over, with and without Content-Length; the default pinned. Each new mechanism\n  removed once, its tests seen failing, recorded as *(run)*.\n- GATES.md: the two caller-input named gaps leave; rows for non-body inputs and the body limit; the edge row\n  rewritten; named gaps 12 and 13 of the skill added; the limit and the 100-entry cap under Per-project\n  parameters.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a28b13bbbd8fd4cba055828800418efeefac5803","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/a28b13bbbd8fd4cba055828800418efeefac5803"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/86d9d9511385204533fd89b86ee02c0dd6d86dbf","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/86d9d9511385204533fd89b86ee02c0dd6d86dbf","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDg2ZDlkOTUxMTM4NTIwNDUzM2ZkODliODZlZTAyYzBkZDZkODZkYmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6","sha":"3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6"}],"sha":"86d9d9511385204533fd89b86ee02c0dd6d86dbf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/86d9d9511385204533fd89b86ee02c0dd6d86dbf"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:01:42Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-07T02:01:42Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a member given twice is refused; every field code carries typed params; no edge detail quotes the caller\n\n- StrictJsonBodyConverter: a first pass over the body''s tokens records validation.duplicate-member at the\n  pointer of every member repeated in one object, at any depth, declared or not, and returns the body unbound,\n  so neither value is bound (java-backend-api *A member given twice is refused*). STRICT_DUPLICATE_DETECTION\n  rejected: it fails the read as a malformed body at the first repeat.\n- A record''s unknown members are replayed by Jackson after its closing brace; their pointer now comes from the\n  object the source parser left, not the buffer''s context, which named {\"foo\":{\"z\":1}} as /foo/foo.\n- FieldCode names a FieldParams record per constant (max on validation.too-long, expected on\n  validation.wrong-type); FieldError.of takes the code from the record, the constructor refuses a mismatched\n  pair, BanListArchTest.fieldErrorsAreBuiltFromTheirParams keeps main code off it, and the catalog snapshot\n  records every (code, status, param names) triple with both directions of code <-> record reconciled.\n- Greeting length counted in code points, matching the char_length check.\n- Edge: a path variable of the wrong type names the variable and type without quoting the value; 405 and 415\n  name what is supported instead of quoting what was sent; 413 is request.too-large; a client-error status no\n  code carries is the catch-all 500, never validation.bad-request under another status.\n- GATES.md: rows updated; named gaps for naming a non-body input in a field entry, and for an allowed-members\n  param on validation.unknown-field.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1677a22c2525e75699636b6bc6e1b86d9245c86e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/1677a22c2525e75699636b6bc6e1b86d9245c86e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDM2ODljYTY5N2VhOWQ4ZjlmZWJkZjA0OGU1NWM0MDlmNTA0OTA3ZDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1","sha":"20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1"}],"sha":"3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/3689ca697ea9d8f9febdf048e55c409f504907d6"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:32:32Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:32:32Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: every allowed-map line is taken by code; an api subpackage is held internal by a fixture; each layering rule has a test of its own\n\nAdversarial review of a61aecd, 2026-10-06.\n\n- featureDependenciesAreInTheAllowedMap also reports a map line no dependency takes, a line naming a feature\n  that does not exist among them. Such a line passed, so a typo in the map, or a line left behind after the\n  last call went, stood as a permission no code had asked for. Now a line goes in with the code that takes it\n  and out with the last code that did, which is what holds the owner''s \"in the same commit as the code that\n  needs it\". A repeated line throws like the other malformed forms; a set had merged it silently.\n  theMapRefusesEveryLineThatIsNotOneEdgeBetweenTwoFeatures asserts each malformed form.\n- featuresReachAnotherFeatureOnlyThroughItsApi refused a subpackage of api, as docs/GATES.md said, but no\n  fixture held it: widening the comparison to a prefix passed every test.\n  PartnerPlatformCallsGreetingApiSubpackage, calling greeting.api.dto.GreetingView, now holds it.\n- everyLayeringRuleIsAFactoryWithATestOfItsOwn. The reflection tests take any violation in the fixture tree as\n  proof, so a new rule could pass on another rule''s fixture, the way the substring filter hid before e3db6bf,\n  and a rule built inside a test method escaped both. The test class''s own bytecode is now read: rules are\n  built only in factories, and each factory is called directly by a @Test of its own.\n- docs/GATES.md: \"the build failed and the implementing agent had to rewrite the boundary test\" is not in the\n  owner''s recorded words and no record of such a run was found; it now states the mechanism, that such a spec\n  could not pass without an edit to the test. The Money-converter sentence is marked as the template''s\n  reading of the owner''s generated-tree decision, and the two readings this commit adds are marked the same\n  way. \"names one feature twice\" now reads as a self-edge; the main code''s nothing-to-report claim is narrowed\n  to the api and map rules, since the cycle rule also covers the shared tier; why no cycle runs through the\n  base package is stated, and test sources are named as not imported.\n- README.md: the generated tree depends on nothing outside itself, not only on no feature. CLAUDE.md and the\n  test''s Javadoc: the api package itself, a line removed with the last call, a cycle of feature edges failing\n  whatever the map says.\n\nEach new assertion was seen to fail under a temporary break of its rule: finish() reporting no line; the api\ncomparison widened to a prefix; a repeated line accepted; a factory with no test of its own; a rule built in a\ntest method. node scripts/wall.mjs green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a15c34b677eedcc29761f81a6d1ac85b486fd836","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/a15c34b677eedcc29761f81a6d1ac85b486fd836"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDIwYmE1NWM3ZTRmYWNkMjI2ZDlhZWExNjBmNDA5NjUwNzEwNzQxZDE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a","sha":"a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a"}],"sha":"20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/20ba55c7e4facd226d9aea160f409650710741d1"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:14:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T07:14:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a feature reaches another through its api package over a mapped edge; the base package depends on no feature\n\nOwner''s decision, 2026-10-06: the ban on every feature-to-feature dependency is too strict as the\ntemplate''s permanent rule. Work is driven by spec-kit, and a spec can need one feature to call another,\nsuch as orders reserving stock from inventory; under the ban the build failed and the implementing agent\nhad to rewrite the boundary test to get through. featuresDoNotDependOnEachOther is replaced by the three\nrules java-backend-rules *The module boundary is enforced by ArchUnit, not by package naming* states:\nmodulesAreFreeOfCycles (every direct child of the base package, the shared tier included),\nfeaturesReachAnotherFeatureOnlyThroughItsApi (the callee''s api package itself), and\nfeatureDependenciesAreInTheAllowedMap over ALLOWED_FEATURE_DEPENDENCIES, one `caller -> callee` line per\nedge, empty. Adding an edge is one line there in the commit that needs it; a line that does not parse,\nnames platform or db, or names one feature twice fails the build. Module names compare whole.\n\nCorrection: e3db6bf and docs/GATES.md recorded \"the no-feature-edge map stays\" as the owner''s decision.\nIt was not; the strict map was chosen in an assistant''s task brief and recorded as the owner''s in error.\ngeneratedTreeDependsOnNothingOutsideIt is the owner''s explicit decision and stays, as do\nplatformDependsOnNoFeature and controllersLiveInFeaturePackages.\n\nNew rule, owner-approved: basePackageDependsOnNoFeature, so a class directly in the base package\n(Application, ApiExceptionHandler) depends on no feature. Main code passes it.\n\nEvery factory now takes a Layout, the base package and its allowed map; reflection requires that\nsignature and runs each factory over main with ALLOWED_FEATURE_DEPENDENCIES and over\nstarterfixtures.layering with FIXTURE_ALLOWED_FEATURE_DEPENDENCIES. New fixtures, each asserted exactly:\norders and inventory call each other through api, allowed both ways, and the cycle rule still reports\nthem (with the shared-tier cycles the other fixtures close); partnerplatform calls greeting''s internal\nGreetingService over an allowed edge; feedback calls greeting.api with no map line; RootCallsFeature, in\nthe base package, calls greeting; billing calls greeting.api over an allowed edge and nothing reports it.\nEach assertion was seen to fail under a temporary break of its rule.\n\ndocs/GATES.md: the layering row states the seven rules, how to add an edge, both owner decisions and the\ncorrection, and what the rules do not reach, now without the base-package-to-feature hole; the fixture\nrow names the seven exact assertions. README.md, CLAUDE.md, the base package-info and TableOwnershipTest''s\ncomment describe the new rule.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"33216c81da28eb23b4d44f22d719c38b0f14aac2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/33216c81da28eb23b4d44f22d719c38b0f14aac2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGE2MWFlY2QyODk4ZGU2NmFjZDlhMjdhNzI2OWJlZGI0MGMwOTY5NWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15","sha":"f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15"}],"sha":"a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/a61aecd2898de66acd9a27a7269bedb40c09695a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:33:34Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:37:31Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: the generated tree names nothing outside itself; every layering factory runs over main and fixtures\n\nReview of the layering negative controls. The no-feature-edge map was said to meet java-backend-rules'' three\nmodule-boundary rules by consequence, but nothing constrained the generated jOOQ tree''s own references: a\ngenerated class naming a feature or a platform class, as a forced type''s converter does, closed a cycle\nthrough the tree (feature <-> db, or platform <-> db with the platform''s allowed read) and passed every rule.\ngeneratedTreeDependsOnNothingOutsideIt refuses it; fixtures GeneratedTableNamesAFeature and\nGeneratedTableNamesThePlatform must be reported, GeneratedTable''s in-tree reference must not. The first\nforced type naming a class outside the tree is a committed map change, like the first feature edge.\n\nThe factory reflection matched the declared return type ArchRule exactly, so a factory declared as the\nSliceRule a slices rule builds was skipped and the coverage test stayed green over a silent rule (run at\ne3db6bf). It now takes any ArchRule subtype and fails on a factory that is not static or does not take the\nbase package. The main-code checks were hand-written @Test methods, so a factory with a fixture and no\n@Test passed both tests and never ran over main; everyLayeringRuleHoldsOverTheMainCode now checks every\nfactory reflection finds, after asserting the import holds platform.Tx and Application.\n\ncontrollersLiveInFeaturePackages exempted a controller directly in the base package and matched only a\ndirect @RestController; it now requires a feature package for any class meta-annotated with @Controller.\nFixture RootController (@Controller, base package) must be reported. The platform rule also refuses a\ndependency on a class directly in the base package; fixture PlatformCallsTheBasePackage pins it and the\nrule''s reason and docs/GATES.md now say so.\n\ndocs/GATES.md: the layering row states all four rules, the generated tree''s edge in the by-consequence\nargument, and two more references the rules do not see (a feature''s into the base package, an inlined\ncompile-time constant); the fixture row names the four exact assertions.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"15d1d95c5a14617f3671a35caabc0fad8f4ae16e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/15d1d95c5a14617f3671a35caabc0fad8f4ae16e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGYxNjFiNDNjZTQ5ZTY0Y2JmZjk4OTg1N2YxMDk1Yzg1YmU2NjliMTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea","sha":"e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea"}],"sha":"f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/f161b43ce49e64cbff989857f1095c85be669b15"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:18:43Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-10-06T06:18:43Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a violating fixture per layering rule; feature slices matched by exact name\n\nLayeringArchTest''s three rules are now static factories over a base package, checked over the main code\nand over starterfixtures.layering, a fixture tree with the platform tier, a generated-tree stand-in and\nfour features. everyLayeringRuleReportsTheFixtureTree evaluates every factory over it and fails on one that\nreports nothing; three tests pin each rule to exactly the fixture classes written to break it. The main\ncode holds one feature, so the feature rule could report nothing there.\n\nThe feature filter compared slice descriptions by substring, so a feature `feedback` (it contains `db`)\ndepending on `greeting` passed while `billing` doing the same was reported. It now compares the slice\nname whole against platform and db; fixtures `feedback` and `partnerplatform` prove both halves.\n\nThe no-feature-edge map stays (owner, 2026-10-06): it is the strictest map java-backend-rules *The\nmodule boundary is enforced by ArchUnit, not by package naming* admits and meets its three rules by\nconsequence; the first feature-to-feature edge is a committed map change. docs/GATES.md re-points the\nlayering row at that directive, records the decision and what the rules do not reach, and names every\nnegative control in the fixture row.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"031750f38bb304a385887d70d8ee632af59c106c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/031750f38bb304a385887d70d8ee632af59c106c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGUzZGI2YmZmYTFkMjJlZTA3ZTVmZDZjYWM0NGEyYzliYmFiMDZjZWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20","sha":"20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20"}],"sha":"e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/e3db6bffa1d22ee07e5fd6cac44a2c9bbab06cea"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:18:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:18:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: every mise tool pinned by checksum in mise.lock; the wall refuses a stale lock or a missing checksum\n\nmise.lock beside mise.toml and project-root/mise.toml, written with mise 2026.9.7 (lock format 2, which the\nCI''s 2026.9.7 reads) for linux-x64, linux-arm64, macos-x64, macos-arm64 and windows-x64: sha256 for Node,\nosv-scanner and vacuum, sha512 for Maven, SHA-1 for the Liberica JDK, the only digest BellSoft publishes.\nmise.toml sets [tool_config] locked = true, so mise install refuses a tool the lock lacks instead of\nrewriting the lock, and lockfile_platforms, so mise lock refreshes all five.\n\nscripts/check-mise-lock.mjs runs first in the wall: a tool at a version or options the lock lacks, a lock\nentry mise.toml does not list, a platform without a url or accepted checksum, a missing lock, locked or\nlockfile_platforms unset, and a declared exemption that no longer applies each fail; fixtures under\nscripts/fixtures/mise-lock show each refused by its rule alone. The JDK''s SHA-1 is the one declared\nexemption and a named gap. By hand with mise 2026.9.7: a changed digit in the osv-scanner, Maven and JDK\nlinux-x64 checksums each failed mise install, and a vacuum pin moved without mise lock was refused.\n\nRenovate''s mise manager runs `mise lock <tool>` after it moves a pin (read from its source); its\nignorePaths now skips the fixtures. GitLab''s mise cache keys on mise.lock.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"78d3ff47a15221cf1435bb3598e4f96241341daf","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/78d3ff47a15221cf1435bb3598e4f96241341daf"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDIwZDkxM2E1MjZhZGFhYjY4ZjdiOTEzMjBjMjMxMTFkNDYyYThhMjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9","sha":"5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9"}],"sha":"20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/20d913a526adaab68f7b91320c23111d462a8a20"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:18:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-29T04:18:36Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"deps: Jackson 3.1.7 and 2.21.7 over Boot''s 3.1.5 and 2.21.5\n\nThree jackson-databind advisories published 2026-09-28 (GHSA-gx83-3vf8-gh7j, GHSA-q4xh-88c3-wmh7,\nGHSA-wjgm-6hv5-3cvf) cover both lines Boot 4.1.1 manages; osv-scanner failed the wall on them. Fixed in\n3.1.6 and 2.21.6; the override takes the newest patch on each line, as the Tomcat one does.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"83f908e422cb0cd2c31596bcfae005d5f15607dc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/83f908e422cb0cd2c31596bcfae005d5f15607dc"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDUwMDlmYjhkMDQzMzBmYWYwNzJjNTBhYmM2NmUwNTk3Yjk3NjA5YTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257","sha":"52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257"}],"sha":"5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5009fb8d04330faf072c50abc66e0597b97609a9"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T02:07:48Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T02:58:20Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"template: method-neutral; spec-kit, the constitution and traceability move out, the wall runs listed project checks\n\nThe feature pipeline and its gate belong to dulguun0225/scalith. Removed: the constitution, the worktree\nsetting, check-traceability.mjs with its canary and fixtures, and every mention of them. The wall''s\ntraceability steps become one hook: the Node scripts listed in <project root>/scripts/wall-checks.txt,\nrun in order from the project root; the template lists none.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3cbb0796d2ae5ed81010ebd8f8a7a84bf7b0dbab","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/3cbb0796d2ae5ed81010ebd8f8a7a84bf7b0dbab"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDUyZWU0ZDdlZjJiNjUzM2Q5NTUzOWRjZTI1ZGRiZTJkMWU1Y2YyNTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197","sha":"1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197"}],"sha":"52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/52ee4d7ef2b6533d95539dce25ddbe2d1e5cf257"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:45:38Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:45:38Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"project: the unattended build''s branch is build/<NNN>-<name>\n\nscalith''s build-feature names its short-lived branch build/<NNN>-<name>;\nthe spec-freeze rule and the worktree note named feature/<NNN>-<name>.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"198b4588c35300d8a88dbfe2a4e216ebea770a65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/198b4588c35300d8a88dbfe2a4e216ebea770a65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDFkZGY2ZWVkZDgzYTJlMTM4MDk5YWQ2Y2EyNDU2NzFjY2NjYmYxOTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77","sha":"31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77"}],"sha":"1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/1ddf6eedd83a2e138099ad6ca245671ccccbf197"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:42:42Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-28T00:42:42Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"project: trunk-based development on dev\n\nEveryone commits to dev directly; when dev is stable, main takes a pull\nrequest from dev and a release is made from main.\n\n- dev.json: refuses deletion and force-push only. The pull-request,\n  required-checks and linear-history rules are gone: they refused a direct\n  push, and the unattended build''s short-lived branch lands merge commits.\n- main.json: required checks not strict. main only receives dev, so the\n  merged tree is dev''s, and strict would force main back into dev before\n  every release.\n- check-required-checks.mjs checks only branches whose ruleset requires\n  checks, now main alone, and fails when none does.\n- CI no longer cancels a run on a push to dev or main; only superseded\n  pull-request runs (GitHub) and other branches'' pipelines (GitLab) are\n  cancelled.\n- Project CLAUDE.md: a session a person runs pulls dev before changing a\n  file, writes specs on dev and never branches for one, and commits and\n  pushes the spec at the end of every specify or clarify session, saying\n  nothing about git to the person. Workflow agents run only their prompt''s\n  git steps. A feature''s spec is fixed once its build has started; a later\n  change is a new feature.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9ef05554903cc641947dd3432df7e966b1d00845","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/9ef05554903cc641947dd3432df7e966b1d00845"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDMxMDA5ZmRlZWExY2IyNTllNDAyNjdkMmMzMDY5NmQ1M2Q2MzNhNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68","sha":"0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68"}],"sha":"31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/31009fdeea1cb259e40267d2c30696d53d633a77"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4142584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225","id":4142584,"login":"dulguun0225","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNDI1ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-27T18:34:03Z","email":"dulguun0225@gmail.com","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-27T18:34:03Z","email":"dulguun0225@gmail.com","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"project: services work on dev; main takes pull requests from dev only\n\nThe project CLAUDE.md names `dev` as the base branch. CI runs on pushes to\ndev and main. Two rulesets: dev.json (the former main.json, now naming\nrefs/heads/dev) and main.json (no push, no deletion, pull requests merged\nby merge commit, backend and frontend required). The backend job fails a\npull request into main from any branch but dev, on GitHub and GitLab.\napply-ruleset.mjs applies every ruleset; check-required-checks.mjs checks\nevery branch they name. A standalone init moves the template''s own\nCLAUDE.md line and CI trigger to dev. This template itself stays on main.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"097af0347b7d84e80e760a0d8b6e72e5c42ad6fd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/097af0347b7d84e80e760a0d8b6e72e5c42ad6fd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4142584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225","id":4142584,"login":"dulguun0225","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNDI1ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDBjMDk2MGM5MDRlYTA1YTM0NjU5Njg0NDI3NTI0MjNlY2NkMmFlNjg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2","sha":"9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2"}],"sha":"0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/0c0960c904ea05a3465968442752423eccd2ae68"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:00:13Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T14:00:13Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: any feature reads any table; only the owner writes it\n\nTableOwnershipTest failed any feature that named another feature''s table, reads included,\nunless it sat on LICENSED_READERS, which shipped empty; LayeringArchTest also forbids calling\nanother feature''s classes, so a feature that needed another feature''s rows had no path inside\nthe build. The owner''s instruction was to stop forbidding that read.\n\n- TableOwnershipTest: reads are unrestricted; onlyTheOwnerWritesATable fails a method that\n  starts a write (a DSLContext or DSL insert, update, delete, merge, truncate, batch or load,\n  or a VersionedUpdate call) and names a table its feature does not own. Method-scoped, like\n  the versioned-update and id-ordering bans; a lambda counts toward the method declaring it,\n  so a method that reads a foreign table and writes its own is reported too, and the read\n  moves to its own method. LICENSED_READERS is gone.\n- Negative control theRuleReportsAForeignWriteAndNothingElse over starterfixtures.ownership:\n  feature reader reads GREETING (not reported) and writes it inside tx.write (reported);\n  feature greeting writes it (not reported). OffsetPaginationFixture no longer serves it.\n- Constitution Article VI (amendment, reason above): a feature owns its tables; only it writes\n  them, and any feature may read them through the generated jOOQ tables, never through the\n  owner''s classes. CLAUDE.md, README and docs/GATES.md say the same; the GATES row names what\n  the check does not reach and cites ai-maintainer-principles *each table written only by the\n  module that owns it*, the narrowed directive.\n\nnode scripts/wall.mjs green.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"35ab741d1492f26363d4219b337adccd62a735ba","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/35ab741d1492f26363d4219b337adccd62a735ba"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDlmZmYwNTRiMDdmMTAwMDcyNWY5OWI0ODUyMzNiMGExZTAzNDY2ZjI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53","sha":"d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53"}],"sha":"9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/9fff054b07f1000725f99b485233b0a1e03466f2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T23:41:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T23:41:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: strict request bodies — identifiers in the path only, one request type per operation\n\nPorted from netcore-platform/reference-data 1b74507, adapted to the template. Spring Boot turns\nJackson FAIL_ON_UNKNOWN_PROPERTIES off, so an update type that omits the path identifier silently\naccepts a sent one and answers 200. That pushed plan agents to declare the identifier in the body,\ncompare it and refuse a mismatch with a *-immutable code.\n\nEvery @RequestBody now binds as platform.error.BoundBody<T>, read only by StrictJsonBodyConverter.\nA per-read DeserializationProblemHandler collects, in one pass, every undeclared member\n(validation.unknown-field), every top-level member named after a route template variable\n(validation.identifier-in-path) and every wrong JSON type (validation.wrong-type, detail\n\"expected <type>\"). BoundBody.validate merges these with the feature''s field rules into one\nvalidation.failed, and the service calls it before any transaction. validation.malformed-body\nremains for non-object input and a missing body, and now carries a detail with the line and column.\nStrictness lives in the reader only. The global spring.jackson flag is unchanged, because broker\nmessages must tolerate unknown members. greeting binds through it.\n\nGates: BanListArchTest.requestBodiesBindThroughBoundBody (fixture RawRequestBodyFixture,\nnegative control, meta row REQUEST_BODY_OUTSIDE_BOUND_BODY); RequestBodyContractTest (record with\nno path-variable member, nothing widening, String/Boolean/Number or own deserializer, no record\nshared by two handlers; negative control over RequestBodyContractFixture); StrictBodyEndpointIT\n(sweep over handler-mapping operations, held equal to openapi/v1.json; a probe controller keeps the\npath-identifier case non-vacuous, and a raw-bound handler is its negative control);\nStrictJsonBodyConverterTest; BoundBodyTest. Request-body schemas carry additionalProperties: false\nthrough an OpenApiCustomizer, and the vacuum rule request-body-schemas-are-closed fails on absent\nand on true.\n\nConstitution Article IV, CLAUDE.md and docs/GATES.md state the rule and name what the gates miss:\npath-variable matching by name only, and no static check that an update type declares only what\nit writes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"63d54e7cf2bc25a2bdc0c99824f8fe1c94b39b2d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/63d54e7cf2bc25a2bdc0c99824f8fe1c94b39b2d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGQ2YzU5OGU5YjdlNmY2ZGE1ZTdjNjQzNGFkMThhM2FmM2E1YWNhNTM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce","sha":"00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce"}],"sha":"d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/d6c598e9b7e6f6da5e7c6434ad18a3af3a5aca53"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:40:55Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T22:41:02Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"docs: the project CLAUDE.md states the base branch in one line\n\nThe line \"Base branch: `main`\" goes beside the definition-of-done command in both\nCLAUDE.md files: project-root/CLAUDE.md, which init.mjs lifts to a project''s\nroot, and the service''s own, which is the root file of a standalone repo.\nbuild-feature reads that one line, in that exact form, from the repository\nroot''s CLAUDE.md as committed on the branch a run starts on, after\nargs.baseBranch and before origin/HEAD. main is this template''s trunk: the\nscaffold runs `git init -b main`, CI triggers on push to main, and the\nruleset protects main. The service''s copy says it is not read when the\ndirectory is backend/ inside a project. No build input changed.\n\nChecked: check-traceability.mjs and check-forbidden-flags.mjs green; the wall\nwas not run.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018TLSeNHAGLyHKsykjsMfGx","tree":{"sha":"1b61a4340ffe192e1d817f6119df85cbef9f7fd5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/1b61a4340ffe192e1d817f6119df85cbef9f7fd5"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDAwNjM5YTkxODcxMmY2ZDgxNWFlNmFkNDA3ZWI0NWJkMjM0MGIwY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4","sha":"a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4"}],"sha":"00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/00639a918712f6d815ae6ad407eb45bd2340b0ce"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:09:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:09:50Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"init: the printed procedure formats after the rename, before the wall\n\nThe rename changes where the project''s own imports sort and how long lines wrap:\na package that sorts after `java.` (mn.*, org.*) left the tree unformatted, and\nspotless:check inside `mvn verify` refused the scaffold. Seen 2026-09-21 on\nmn.netgroup.netcore.pricingfeeparameter. init.mjs stays pure Node and does not\nrun Maven; its \"next:\" line and the README procedure now say\n`mvn spotless:apply` between codegen and verify. The scaffold script in the\nskills repo runs the same step.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ecfc736fa419921c958d51e14cd3e892f79bd70c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/ecfc736fa419921c958d51e14cd3e892f79bd70c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGE4OWJkMjgxOTUzYzIwNzYxOTRiOTFkNzE0N2NjYWRlMTQxNjdlYzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b","sha":"5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b"}],"sha":"a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/a89bd281953c2076194b91d7147ccade14167ec4"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:53:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:53:37Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"constitution: Article VII reads \"None\", not \"Add what this product decides\"\n\nAn empty heading over a comment that opened with \"Add\" and listed six topics was\nread as a to-do, by agents and by the plans that grew it to fourteen\nsub-articles. The section now states that empty is complete and that an article\narrives only by amendment.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3157b473b493b48c5af7b4f477c3c4db08c8bb77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/3157b473b493b48c5af7b4f477c3c4db08c8bb77"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDVlNzVjZjczZWY2ZDFhYzBmMDU3NTU1NGE0NGIyNmZhNzMwNmI0M2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77","sha":"32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77"}],"sha":"5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5e75cf73ef6d1ac0f0575554a44b26fa7306b43b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:45:46Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:45:46Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"docs: /speckit.constitution is not a step; Article VII is an optional slot\n\nREADME, the project CLAUDE.md and the constitution''s header comment each listed\n/speckit.constitution as what follows `specify init --here`. Agents read that as\na step owed and handed it to the owner, twice by 2026-09-21. Nothing reads\nwhether Article VII is filled; it is amended later from a feature''s plan. The\nscaffold-before-spec-kit ordering is unchanged.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"de0da80f64fb0f38aaf69c838c92b2d94ae008af","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/de0da80f64fb0f38aaf69c838c92b2d94ae008af"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDMyZmQ0ZDg2YWFkZGJjOTUwODNiNWIxMjc5YjAwZmFkNDUyMmNmNzc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38","sha":"4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38"}],"sha":"32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/32fd4d86aaddbc95083b5b1279b00fad4522cf77"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:26:53Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T03:26:53Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gate: specs are written here, so provenance is not a layer the gate holds\n\nRe-vendors backend/scripts/check-traceability.mjs, its selftest and the whole\nscripts/fixtures/traceability/ tree from product-catalog@520c00f, which dropped\nthe upstream-provenance layer: no more trace-upstreams.tsv, trace-upstream-dropped.tsv,\npinned specs/upstream/ snapshots or refresh-upstream-snapshot.mjs. The gate keeps only\na shape recogniser: a <QUALIFIER>/FR-nnn token whose qualifier is not a three-digit\nfeature number is prose, not a citation, never coverage -- so it is dropped rather than\nmisread as the bare id it wraps.\n\nCLAUDE.md, README.md, project-root/CLAUDE.md and docs/GATES.md reworded the same way,\nadapted from backend/scripts/ to scripts/. The 20 upstream-*/dropped-* fixture trees are\ngone; foreign-accepted, foreign-not-coverage and foreign-not-tasks replace them, holding\nthe fixture count at 31 trees / 34 cases.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"9085dd6d13031cc0ffa2399ab5e59ebb0479992e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/9085dd6d13031cc0ffa2399ab5e59ebb0479992e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDRhMWM2ZmQwYjZhYzFmMWIxYjA4NjFmMzFiNzk1NDk3MDg5MTRjMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f","sha":"f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f"}],"sha":"4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/4a1c6fd0b6ac1f1b1b0861f31b79549708914c38"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:47:29Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:47:29Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a listed-but-absent build file carries no flags to find\n\ncheck-forbidden-flags.mjs read every git-listed build/deploy file unguarded, the same\nhole 8334581 fixed in check-traceability.mjs: a tracked file deleted from the working\ntree is still listed by `git ls-files`, and the unguarded readFileSync died with an\nuncaught ENOENT stack trace instead of a verdict. Fixed the same way -- absence on a\nlisted path is skipped, any other read error fails the gate naming the file.\n\nsquawk-changed-migrations.mjs has the same shape of read but does not crash: squawk-cli\nitself reads the files it is handed, and a missing one surfaces as its own\n\"Configuration error\" exit, not an uncaught exception. Left as is here -- unlike\nproduct-catalog, this repo has no gate that owns refusing a deleted shipped migration,\nso skipping the absent path in squawk would make it silently pass over a deletion\nnothing else here catches.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"befcf24d6335996688fadcc88a28070f4838b8d9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/befcf24d6335996688fadcc88a28070f4838b8d9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGYyODlhNTI1M2QzZjZjZjI0MzU5ZDFiMmIxMGUyYjI0YjY5MGRjNmY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b","sha":"8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b"}],"sha":"f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/f289a5253d3f6cf24359d1b2b10e2b24b690dc6f"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:38:35Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:38:35Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: a tracked file deleted from the working tree carries no citations\n\nRe-vendored from product-catalog, byte-identical: `git ls-files` lists the index,\nso a file deleted from the working tree and not yet staged is listed and is not on\ndisk. The traceability gate opened every listed path unguarded and died with an\nuncaught ENOENT stack trace instead of a verdict -- hit in a fresh scaffold, where\n`init.mjs` removes this directory''s `.github/` before the first commit.\n\nSuch a path is skipped: a file that is not there carries no citations. Only\nabsence, and only on a listed path -- every other read error is a gate error\nnaming the file, not a stack trace. The canary proves it on a throwaway git\nrepository it builds in a temp directory, since no committed fixture can hold a\nfile that is at once tracked and absent.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"5514352fddfd28aa8b7ca24382e980df46145d8f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/5514352fddfd28aa8b7ca24382e980df46145d8f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDgzMzQ1ODFlMGE5NzQ1NzAxZjE0MmM4NDRkMzIxNzNhM2YwYmQ2N2I","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a","sha":"b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a"}],"sha":"8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/8334581e0a9745701f142c844d32173a3f0bd67b"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:23:31Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T02:23:31Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: an upstream citation resolves against a pinned copy of its document\n\nVendored from product-catalog, where the extension was built and proven: the\ntraceability gate, its canary and the fixture trees arrive byte-identical, and\n`refresh-upstream-snapshot.mjs` comes with them.\n\nA `<QUALIFIER>/FR-nnn` citation used to be accepted on its qualifier alone -- the\nrepository the qualifier names is not checked out in CI, so nothing could tell that the\ndocument still defined that id, and a requirement of it could vanish out of a project''s\nreading with nothing noticing. Each declared qualifier now carries a committed copy of\nits document at `specs/upstream/<QUALIFIER>.md`, and its row in `specs/trace-upstreams.tsv`\ngrows to five columns: the feature that reads it, the location, the source commit the copy\nwas taken at, and the copy''s git blob sha, recomputed from the bytes on disk. A snapshot\nedited by hand fails; `scripts/refresh-upstream-snapshot.mjs` re-takes one from a local\ncheckout at a named revision and rewrites the row, so a moved pin is a reviewable diff of\nthe document and CI still reads only committed files.\n\nThat buys both directions: a citation has to name an id the snapshot defines, and every FR\nand SC the snapshot defines is cited under the feature that reads that document or carries\na row in `specs/trace-upstream-dropped.tsv`, `dropped` or `deferred`, with the committed\ndecision named. Beside it, spec -> tasks: every requirement of every feature that has a\n`tasks.md` is named by some task there, or waived.\n\nThe template ships none of the four lists, no `specs/upstream/` and no `specs/` tree: each\nis optional, and the first feature that needs a row creates it. The gate still runs here\nwith zero defined ids, and the canary is 53 cases over 48 fixtures. `wall.mjs` needed no\nchange -- the canary already runs before the gate it proves.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e855b4f88729bd8fcf9961ef4bbafcb9c566e216","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/e855b4f88729bd8fcf9961ef4bbafcb9c566e216"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGIyMWRiZjlmY2MxMjE4MjQ2MTg1ZmM0NDNiOWQ0NWU5ZjRhMzg2M2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd","sha":"e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd"}],"sha":"b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/b21dbf9fcc1218246185fc443b9d45e9f4a3863a"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T01:16:06Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T01:16:06Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"gates: spec<->code traceability, with the canary that proves it\n\nPorted from product-catalog, where the gate was built and is green. The three\nfiles -- scripts/check-traceability.mjs, scripts/check-traceability.selftest.mjs\nand scripts/fixtures/traceability/ -- are byte-identical between the two repos,\nso the next port in either direction is a copy.\n\nThe script discovers its layout rather than assuming one: the backend root is its\nparent directory, the project root is the git toplevel, and the specs tree is\n<project root>/specs. Here the backend *is* the repository and there is no specs\ntree at all, so zero requirement ids are defined -- every citation dangles, every\nbare id still fails, and the gate says on every run that it found no specs\ndirectory. It ran unchanged.\n\n- scripts/wall.mjs: the canary first, then the gate it proves. A gate that cannot\n  fail proves nothing, so that order is the argument for believing the verdict.\n- docs/GATES.md: the citation-form paragraph in the header (every new row in that\n  file is itself a citation), and the two Wired rows with the caveats the gate\n  prints on every run -- a citation is a claim and not a coverage, ids carry no\n  user stories, an en-dash range is not parsed, an upstream id is accepted on its\n  qualifier alone, an upstream id written bare is invisible, a legacy-listed file\n  is exempt at file level.\n- CLAUDE.md, project-root/CLAUDE.md, README.md: the citation rule and the wall''s\n  step list, naming the gate rather than counting the steps.\n\nNone of the three lists under specs/ -- trace-waivers.tsv, trace-legacy-files.tsv,\ntrace-upstreams.tsv -- ships here. Each is optional to the gate and the first\nfeature that needs a row is what creates it; the text says so where the rule is\nstated.\n\nOne change was needed in the gate itself and was made in product-catalog first,\nso the two stay byte-identical: the header''s example citation was spelled with\nreal digits (004/FR-047). That file sits inside the gate''s own scan root, so the\nexample was a live citation -- resolving in product-catalog, dangling in a repo\nwith no specs tree. It is now a placeholder, like every other id in that file.\n\nnode scripts/wall.mjs green at the template root.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cee2a208b708a3ce7ddad4b350ccf3607cba3e67","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/cee2a208b708a3ce7ddad4b350ccf3607cba3e67"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKGU2Y2JhMDU5YmI5Yjk3NDE3MDg4MzMwNzMxMDZhOTJkOWNlOThiZGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb","sha":"5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb"}],"sha":"e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/e6cba059bb9b9741708833073106a92d9ce98bdd"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-17T02:59:12Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-17T02:59:12Z","email":"dulguun.o@netgroup.mn","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"message":"scaffold: project-level .claude/settings.json pins worktree.baseRef=head\n\nAn agent launched with worktree isolation branches from origin/main by default,\nwhich predates any feature branch and leaves the agent working on a tree without\nthe files earlier tasks created. The lifted project settings make every scaffold\nstart such worktrees from the session''s HEAD; .claude/worktrees/ is ignored.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6e5e0e0117c0c47e57d9ce90ba1795e30eb2c611","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/6e5e0e0117c0c47e57d9ce90ba1795e30eb2c611"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDVhM2FmM2U5Y2Q1NDcxNmRjOWEzMmM4NjBlNzAzYzEyYjI0M2VjYmI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/b1a356644115c0d2335bd579ae2aedc73723be21","sha":"b1a356644115c0d2335bd579ae2aedc73723be21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/b1a356644115c0d2335bd579ae2aedc73723be21"}],"sha":"5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/5a3af3e9cd54716dc9a32c860e703c12b243ecbb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4142584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225","id":4142584,"login":"dulguun0225","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNDI1ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/b1a356644115c0d2335bd579ae2aedc73723be21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:12:34Z","email":"dulguun0225@gmail.com","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T15:12:34Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"gates: guarded version update, ORDER BY id ban, table ownership, vacuum ruleset, migration lint additions (#9)\n\nPorted from the first project built on this template, generic parts only.\n\n- platform/VersionedUpdate + VersionedUpdateTest: the one construct that renders UPDATE on a\n  version-columned table; the worked-example table gains `version integer not null` (and\n  char_length in place of length), jOOQ regenerated.\n- BanListArchTest: VERSIONED_TABLE_UPDATES_GO_THROUGH_HELPER and NO_ORDER_BY_ID_OUTSIDE_PAGER,\n  with HandWrittenVersionedUpdateFixture and OrderByIdFixture; ORDER_BY_ID_COLUMN leaves DEFERRED\n  and HAND_WRITTEN_VERSIONED_UPDATE joins the ban enum in BanCoverageMetaTest.\n- TableOwnershipTest: one feature package owns each table, a new table with no owner row fails.\n- platform/error/Rejected and the handler for it; the worked example throws it and ProblemBody,\n  which then had no user, is gone.\n- OpenApiConfiguration registers the Problem schema and the ETag header; the greeting operations\n  declare operationIds and problem responses; openapi/v1.json regenerated.\n- MigrationConventionsTest bans create trigger, create function and octet_length, each on a fixture.\n- vacuum: rulesets/openapi.yaml, scripts/vacuum-openapi.mjs, a wall step, and the 0.30.5 pin in\n  both mise.toml files.\n- project-root/.gitlab-ci.yml as the GitLab variant of the two required jobs; the forbidden-flag\n  scan covers it.\n- .squawk.toml says how an opt-out is actually spelled: squawk 2.65 honours only the file-level\n  `-- squawk-ignore-file`, which is why the migration carries one for prefer-bigint-over-int.\n- docs/GATES.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md follow.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ednGGn1FkeasWdu8vhXwf\n\nCo-authored-by: Dulguun Otgon <dulguun.o@netgroup.mn>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fb2019a272147c5a773e86ef1c3ab84039d5e296","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/fb2019a272147c5a773e86ef1c3ab84039d5e296"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/b1a356644115c0d2335bd579ae2aedc73723be21","verification":{"payload":"tree fb2019a272147c5a773e86ef1c3ab84039d5e296\nparent 2ee1d16052f6f94f150a3ab5ec67a8c545d1b546\nauthor Dulguun Otgon <dulguun0225@gmail.com> 1789571554 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789571554 +0800\n\ngates: guarded version update, ORDER BY id ban, table ownership, vacuum ruleset, migration lint additions (#9)\n\nPorted from the first project built on this template, generic parts only.\n\n- platform/VersionedUpdate + VersionedUpdateTest: the one construct that renders UPDATE on a\n  version-columned table; the worked-example table gains `version integer not null` (and\n  char_length in place of length), jOOQ regenerated.\n- BanListArchTest: VERSIONED_TABLE_UPDATES_GO_THROUGH_HELPER and NO_ORDER_BY_ID_OUTSIDE_PAGER,\n  with HandWrittenVersionedUpdateFixture and OrderByIdFixture; ORDER_BY_ID_COLUMN leaves DEFERRED\n  and HAND_WRITTEN_VERSIONED_UPDATE joins the ban enum in BanCoverageMetaTest.\n- TableOwnershipTest: one feature package owns each table, a new table with no owner row fails.\n- platform/error/Rejected and the handler for it; the worked example throws it and ProblemBody,\n  which then had no user, is gone.\n- OpenApiConfiguration registers the Problem schema and the ETag header; the greeting operations\n  declare operationIds and problem responses; openapi/v1.json regenerated.\n- MigrationConventionsTest bans create trigger, create function and octet_length, each on a fixture.\n- vacuum: rulesets/openapi.yaml, scripts/vacuum-openapi.mjs, a wall step, and the 0.30.5 pin in\n  both mise.toml files.\n- project-root/.gitlab-ci.yml as the GitLab variant of the two required jobs; the forbidden-flag\n  scan covers it.\n- .squawk.toml says how an opt-out is actually spelled: squawk 2.65 honours only the file-level\n  `-- squawk-ignore-file`, which is why the migration carries one for prefer-bigint-over-int.\n- docs/GATES.md, CLAUDE.md, README.md follow.\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ednGGn1FkeasWdu8vhXwf\n\nCo-authored-by: Dulguun Otgon <dulguun.o@netgroup.mn>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqrHiCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAj6QQAEmZ644WsagaiBdFKlL/POVt\nFEfhVIMdvejMD/8VQLpMloUIh5We/3gbhC8+nNaEeyeH5lILzXAQlDq9MOYubVAm\ncVgHL6rImKTWQP2mox3HrMvD+UgVV+iq2L1rtqHZHUq/o1jcZhzqKXnxa+d9wD5t\njSePd1N2vh/rB4Vb+Dq0Jo9P1vfeTzCdBxBE8TZx