e1d16052f6f94f150a3ab5ec67a8c545d1b546"}],"sha":"b1a356644115c0d2335bd579ae2aedc73723be21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/b1a356644115c0d2335bd579ae2aedc73723be21"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4142584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225","id":4142584,"login":"dulguun0225","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNDI1ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/2ee1d16052f6f94f150a3ab5ec67a8c545d1b546/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:13:43Z","email":"dulguun0225@gmail.com","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T12:13:43Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"constitution: Article VI names no package; CLAUDE.md holds the pointer (#8)\n\nReason: Article VI ended with \"The greeting package is the worked shape; copy\nit, then delete it.\" The first real feature in a project deletes greeting as\ninstructed, and the sentence then points at a package that no longer exists.\nA constitution that names the current example goes stale every time the\nexample changes, and fixing it inside a feature task hides a constitution\namendment in a code change.\n\nThe principle (one worked shape, copy it) stays in Article VI. The mutable\npointer moves to the backend CLAUDE.md bullet that already names the example,\nand that bullet now says it is the pointer. Found in product-catalog, whose\nconstitution received the same amendment on its own (b5f0870 there).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ednGGn1FkeasWdu8vhXwf\n\nCo-authored-by: Dulguun Otgon <dulguun.o@netgroup.mn>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f878221db7f6f0609ab6f12358ec66e7e1e46888","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/f878221db7f6f0609ab6f12358ec66e7e1e46888"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/2ee1d16052f6f94f150a3ab5ec67a8c545d1b546","verification":{"payload":"tree f878221db7f6f0609ab6f12358ec66e7e1e46888\nparent 4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7\nauthor Dulguun Otgon <dulguun0225@gmail.com> 1789560823 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789560823 +0800\n\nconstitution: Article VI names no package; CLAUDE.md holds the pointer (#8)\n\nReason: Article VI ended with \"The greeting package is the worked shape; copy\nit, then delete it.\" The first real feature in a project deletes greeting as\ninstructed, and the sentence then points at a package that no longer exists.\nA constitution that names the current example goes stale every time the\nexample changes, and fixing it inside a feature task hides a constitution\namendment in a code change.\n\nThe principle (one worked shape, copy it) stays in Article VI. The mutable\npointer moves to the backend CLAUDE.md bullet that already names the example,\nand that bullet now says it is the pointer. Found in product-catalog, whose\nconstitution received the same amendment on its own (b5f0870 there).\n\n\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_012ednGGn1FkeasWdu8vhXwf\n\nCo-authored-by: Dulguun Otgon <dulguun.o@netgroup.mn>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqof3CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhRIQACisqqZq/1UOvRu00xV7DOen\nYcM2EUTm2qvOxXLwOKv/9EcrAYj5/+0+E3VB60hoUBvpo089tVK14kWHzslrgOEN\nLizlJ7UnEip5uHdcYfCwMy6Zr0cqB+X1OmCg9CodolO90OuZCF+INHwhXoUoElSZ\n4gm9Lyga49igIAZ58PrrXWbL1iRcMducKvfJVfw5dMFkmnCWDcKvhituGL8ZFEN1\nwUNdnl9O3UuYHxkR1DDGrpH4VU3xrMDBlMu5WNXp/KrjRNPrGDn81IpIqwvCZRGp\nXNzX7IKd7cD9eymKRhto2ISgDSKxP9oxczgGpXBxqRQv3YaCKTjnrMET16B58ftS\nPsygyvPe6UwGHlOdTCSNcsudxvNb9b53UrLS5jtekSKmuqf6DdtDgWhF8Kb80AKs\nWpBqus/ZOhIITAZ1ED0mErbYTkB31ZsZf4iYHddmrlbqTHb1pl0EVyLlv/uHPccH\n96Db0COoxy7BqSe328D6glBbJKCIzTMr3FyXk5IHodtUH4bQnynAK2D7BiySgrP5\npnbpi1MmjlvJQ9UFH4DUsSBCAQS0zw/dbn2iEWkSPhUQrDhHHL2EZ//VstGKGZRh\n4kWN/o5GxHZRMmi3KFhtg0BvS/rb90bvpSnZq8JJuzPcWa10kVQOx4AP9IoR3r+j\ngssW6I+5jPR9kJqM6SOd\n=yHr4\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T12:13:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/2ee1d16052f6f94f150a3ab5ec67a8c545d1b546","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDJlZTFkMTYwNTJmNmY5NGYxNTBhM2FiNWVjNjdhOGM1NDVkMWI1NDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7","sha":"4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7"}],"sha":"2ee1d16052f6f94f150a3ab5ec67a8c545d1b546","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/2ee1d16052f6f94f150a3ab5ec67a8c545d1b546"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4142584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225","id":4142584,"login":"dulguun0225","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNDI1ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T07:07:56Z","email":"dulguun0225@gmail.com","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T07:07:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"build: scripts are Node, not bash; toolchain is what mise.toml pins (#7)\n\n* build: JDK is BellSoft Liberica in the image too, same vendor as mise.toml and ci.yml\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: scripts are Node, not bash; toolchain is what mise.toml pins\n\nThe ten shell scripts under scripts/ and project-root/scripts/ become .mjs\nfiles on Node''s standard library, no package.json, so the wall, the rename\nand the project-root checks run the same on Linux, macOS and Windows. Node\nis the runtime the skills install already needs (npx) and the frontend gate\nalready called; it is pinned in mise.toml beside Java and Maven.\n\nosv-scanner is no longer downloaded per OS by the script (the old script\nfetched linux_amd64 only, with one checksum); mise.toml pins it and the aqua\nbackend verifies the release checksum. CI installs the toolchain with\nmise-action from the same file, replacing setup-java, with ~/.m2 cached.\napply-ruleset no longer needs python3.\n\nAlso carries the pending Liberica pins for mise.toml and both workflows, and\nthe README''s empty-commit fix for `git subtree add`.\n\nVerified: node scripts/wall.mjs green locally (Java 25, Maven 3.9.16, Node\n24.21.0, osv-scanner 2.6.0, Docker); init.mjs output diffed byte-identical\nto init.sh on the same input; forbidden-flag, action-pin and frontend gates\nfail on a planted violation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: scaffold before spec-kit; /speckit.constitution amends Article VII only\n\ninit.mjs warns when the kept file is the constitution, since that is the one\nfile where ''kept existing'' means the platform articles did not land.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Hefesto Bot <dulguun.o@netgroup.mn>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"07ca75352b8c73540478123ab30def74b7bfd68e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/07ca75352b8c73540478123ab30def74b7bfd68e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7","verification":{"payload":"tree 07ca75352b8c73540478123ab30def74b7bfd68e\nparent 7ea886bc94bf12416a4bc9a379947f2b74fe9e59\nauthor Dulguun Otgon <dulguun0225@gmail.com> 1789542476 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789542476 +0800\n\nbuild: scripts are Node, not bash; toolchain is what mise.toml pins (#7)\n\n* build: JDK is BellSoft Liberica in the image too, same vendor as mise.toml and ci.yml\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* build: scripts are Node, not bash; toolchain is what mise.toml pins\n\nThe ten shell scripts under scripts/ and project-root/scripts/ become .mjs\nfiles on Node''s standard library, no package.json, so the wall, the rename\nand the project-root checks run the same on Linux, macOS and Windows. Node\nis the runtime the skills install already needs (npx) and the frontend gate\nalready called; it is pinned in mise.toml beside Java and Maven.\n\nosv-scanner is no longer downloaded per OS by the script (the old script\nfetched linux_amd64 only, with one checksum); mise.toml pins it and the aqua\nbackend verifies the release checksum. CI installs the toolchain with\nmise-action from the same file, replacing setup-java, with ~/.m2 cached.\napply-ruleset no longer needs python3.\n\nAlso carries the pending Liberica pins for mise.toml and both workflows, and\nthe README''s empty-commit fix for `git subtree add`.\n\nVerified: node scripts/wall.mjs green locally (Java 25, Maven 3.9.16, Node\n24.21.0, osv-scanner 2.6.0, Docker); init.mjs output diffed byte-identical\nto init.sh on the same input; forbidden-flag, action-pin and frontend gates\nfail on a planted violation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: scaffold before spec-kit; /speckit.constitution amends Article VII only\n\ninit.mjs warns when the kept file is the constitution, since that is the one\nfile where ''kept existing'' means the platform articles did not land.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Hefesto Bot <dulguun.o@netgroup.mn>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqkBMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAR80QAJreQp2Ehm8VCtp3lOYEiWhf\nu2OeV95BLA+Ih6H48vwwLhkBIm2lblghymi43v1fnd4Tr2q+6IXCMc6Fs9I32wLc\nO1ym2ca+CUeLG1FRtmTOMrZQ45Bp95c6ftUz9eY4EFFltQPQO1r84qmpIMQJAKNq\nFlKQZwUzB3sYVFPueL1LvKAErwbWDBqZYqhgtsYGfshOq5uSa/pH5aP5SbDy/g0n\nBm7ASGEbkyvtNkCTu5H+ntjvEoHkGnPQbse92rBX6hChLgM4MvGBGUg6sv3Tl/PY\n5xVJHWpOraggI4v1860xVQ9Ntv7/BpF6kXxoSTxQ9i+LJ4MMGoR/BDOP1MB9sGZN\n9dQA3Ie6R7EF/MSi6tEb0er94Toag29QYPor2e86u9gixThokCSrljSaIrdHFX1o\n0Nq2owiZRT/OoTP03+M50pE2VF08uJO3oIg2sSezXcrW6P519eVrydaaP4lJW1C5\nNnzHEPyj1/g8kKK6Jf2Dxc53vNNSNUuNPQrzvEbTnccwZS036aZygVcWDva5bw9R\nNZA6tget4df3NR9Km2BngGJ4nsd0aMlrS+tsCsoqmHMyhvzCyP5Ax80LsSJZ8gh8\nz1AM83iKKF3lqnDEjCrMHMOrWQ4hiqcHQWjd1ilyltFNBItqQby6+1Is1NrW8UYw\nE5tek5z0vHvytnrwMhA3\n=fRFb\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-16T07:07:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7","node_id":"C_kwDOUc9DO9oAKDRjMDI4MTIxZTU3ZDc0YTNjYWNkNjFkZTJiMWY5MjI2NjljMDRlYTc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commit/7ea886bc94bf12416a4bc9a379947f2b74fe9e59","sha":"7ea886bc94bf12416a4bc9a379947f2b74fe9e59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/7ea886bc94bf12416a4bc9a379947f2b74fe9e59"}],"sha":"4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/4c028121e57d74a3cacd61de2b1f922669c04ea7"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4142584?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/dulguun0225","id":4142584,"login":"dulguun0225","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxNDI1ODQ=","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dulguun0225","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/commits/7ea886bc94bf12416a4bc9a379947f2b74fe9e59/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-16T06:14:22Z","email":"dulguun0225@gmail.com","name":"Dulguun Otgon"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-16T06:14:22Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"refactor: the template is the backend, vendored into a project''s backend/ (#6)\n\nThe template root is now the service module. project-root/ carries what a\nproject needs at its root (CI with backend+frontend jobs, ruleset, compose,\nfrontend stub, spec-kit constitution, project CLAUDE.md, root scripts);\nscripts/init.sh lifts it one level up when it detects it is vendored, and\nonly renames when the repo is the service itself. scripts/wall.sh is the\none backend wall both workflows run. Proven: wall at root, simulated\nvendoring plus init.sh, and mvn verify inside the vendored renamed copy.\n\nCo-authored-by: Hefesto Bot <dulguun.o@netgroup.mn>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"1a529d3824d5911bcd893ac0c82f10a9226bd9ac","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/trees/1a529d3824d5911bcd893ac0c82f10a9226bd9ac"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dulguun0225/java-backend-template/git/commits/7ea886bc94bf12416a4bc9a379947f2b74fe9e59","verification":{"payload":"tree 1a529d3824d5911bcd893ac0c82f10a9226bd9ac\nparent e36d4625f4ee49f5f8bbf86d4dfb96b835c6adae\nauthor Dulguun Otgon <dulguun0225@gmail.com> 1789539262 +0800\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789539262 +0000\n\nrefactor: the template is the backend, vendored into a project''s backend/ (#6)\n\nThe template root is now the service module. project-root/ carries what a\nproject needs at its root (CI with backend+frontend jobs, ruleset, compose,\nfrontend stub, spec-kit constitution, project CLAUDE.md, root scripts);\nscripts/init.sh lifts it one level up when it detects it is vendored, and\nonly renames when the repo is the service itself. scripts/wall.sh is the\none backend wall both workflows run. Proven: wall at root, simulated\nvendoring plus init.sh, and mvn verify inside the vendored renamed copy.\n\nCo-authored-by: Hefesto Bot